PlaySound hit_heavy","One salvor is overly hasty and skips a step in the measured protocols that made the reputation of your ops chief.

This earns the consequences of a custom-rigged defensive measure hidden in the access panel for the cargo bay override.",GS_ADVENTURERS_contBoom:Continue,
GS_ADVENTURERS_contBoomSel,DialogOptionSelected,$option == GS_ADVENTURERS_contBoom,,"Your ops chief growls, bullying the remaining salvors into paranoid compliance. Several more explosives and panel overloads are disarmed before hull access is cleared.",GS_ADVENTURERS_cont2:Continue,
GS_ADVENTURERS_cont2Sel,DialogOptionSelected,$option == GS_ADVENTURERS_cont2,$salvageLeaveText = Leave 0,"This is a ship of mercenary-adventurers crewed by a colorful mix of distinct personalities from worlds representative of a broad swath of the Persean Sector.

The captain was a former officer who found himself on the losing side of minor rebellion out of the Persean League. The pilot, a racer-turned-smuggler recovered from stim addiction. Former Diktat gone renegade, present at the massacre of... scion of an Eventide officer family, overbearing mother, disowned after... the engineer, the armorer, the navigator... all irrelevant details. You skim the report faster.

You can't imagine how they managed to work together. It doesn't matter; they're all dead now.","salExplore:Assess the ship's salvage value
defaultLeave:Leave",
,,,,,,
"Abyssal ghost ships, ""Chartery of Opis"" variation",,,,,,
GS_OPIS_open,OpenInteractionDialog,"$tag:salvageable
$gsType == GS_OPIS score:1000
!$explored","ShowDefaultVisual
PrintWreckDescription",Your $shipOrFleet approaches $aOrAn $nameInText.,"GS_OPIS_cont1:Explore
defaultLeave:Leave",
GS_OPIS_cont1Sel,DialogOptionSelected,$option == GS_OPIS_cont1,"$explored = true
UniqueEncounter setInteractedWith $gsType","You watch the salvage teams via vid-feed as their rig and attendant drone swarm approach the derelict.

Details from long-range optical scans are confirmed: beneath a patina of space-weathering, the hull still bears a corporate registration and the crest of the Chartery of Opis, a polity annihilated during the Askonia Crisis of cycle 181.",GS_OPIS_cont2:Continue,
GS_OPIS_cont2Sel,DialogOptionSelected,$option == GS_OPIS_cont2,,"The only body found aboard is the former captain, sitting at his command console, desiccated eyes fixed ahead at the suffocating nothingness of deep space.

Behind the CIC, in the armored computer center, there is a Tri-Tachyon manufactured AI core interface. Just sitting there unassuming out in the open, a perfectly casual commercial hardware installation. This dates the ship back further, to before the AI Wars.

No core lies in the cradle, however. Perhaps it was taken when the ship was abandoned.",GS_OPIS_cont3:Continue,
GS_OPIS_cont3Sel,DialogOptionSelected,$option == GS_OPIS_cont3,$salvageLeaveText = Leave 0,"Your tech officer oversees an attempt to read the logs, to find some hint of what happened and why - but the memory banks have all been cleared by a repeating wipe program that continued until backup power faded.

A full forensic-archeological investigation might reveal answers, but you have neither the time nor equipment for such indulgence.","salExplore:Assess the ship's salvage value
defaultLeave:Leave",
,,,,,,
"Abyssal ghost ships, ""Pirates"" variation",,,,,,
GS_PIRATES_open,OpenInteractionDialog,"$tag:salvageable
$gsType == GS_PIRATES score:1000
!$explored","ShowDefaultVisual
PrintWreckDescription",Your $shipOrFleet approaches $aOrAn $nameInText.,"GS_PIRATES_cont1:Explore
defaultLeave:Leave",
GS_PIRATES_cont1Sel,DialogOptionSelected,$option == GS_PIRATES_cont1,"$explored = true
UniqueEncounter setInteractedWith $gsType","As your salvor teams breach the hull, they discover tell-tale signs of a pirate crew: prominently-displayed hand weapons, decor as bold and brutal as it is unsophisticated - skulls and blood-red predominate, and signs of lackadaisical maintenance performed on the less interesting ship systems.

It is not a tomb-ship, however. 

By numbers, most of the crew appears to have escaped before leaving the hull derelict. A few unfortunate victims of personal violence - or parts of them - appear to have been left behind from some kind of internal conflict. The cycles since were not kind to what remained as the life support systems slowly failed.",GS_PIRATES_cont2:Continue,
GS_PIRATES_cont2Sel,DialogOptionSelected,$option == GS_PIRATES_cont2,$salvageLeaveText = Leave 0,"A cursory trawl of what logs the senior officers bothered to keep suggests that this ship was part of a small pirate flotilla tracking a well-supplied independent expedition working its way through the outer fringe. That expedition spotted the pirates, then burned rapidly toward the Abyss. The pirates followed and soon lost their prey in the stultifying darkness.

With supplies and fuel dwindling and no certainty of a 'hostile resupply', the pirate leadership began to argue, and then to scrap hulls while consolidating crew onto the remaining ships - at the barrel of a gun, as necessary.

There wasn't quite enough room for everyone, it appears.","salExplore:Assess the ship's salvage value
defaultLeave:Leave",
,,,,,,
"# Abyssal ghost ships, ""ZGR Merc"" variation",,,,,,
GS_ZGR_MERC_open,OpenInteractionDialog,"$tag:salvageable
$gsType == GS_ZGR_MERC score:1000
!$explored","ShowDefaultVisual
PrintWreckDescription",Your $shipOrFleet approaches $aOrAn $nameInText.,"GS_ZGR_MERC_cont1:Explore
defaultLeave:Leave",
GS_ZGR_MERC_cont1Sel,DialogOptionSelected,$option == GS_ZGR_MERC_cont1,"$explored = true
UniqueEncounter setInteractedWith $gsType
$global.foundZGRabyssMercs = true","As your salvors approach, some kind of proximity sensor is triggered - a faint comms transmission begins. The power system is clearly degraded and running down, causing the transmission to sputter and warble.

It's a repeating recording, not an active feed. Your comms officer does their best to clean it up, and forwards it to your command console.

A face appears, presumably the unfortunate ship's captain, his expression twisted by an appalling mixture of privation and hatred.",GS_ZGR_MERC_cont2:Continue,
GS_ZGR_MERC_cont2Sel,DialogOptionSelected,$option == GS_ZGR_MERC_cont2,"$option = GS_ZGR_MERC_cont3 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","""...Zunya, if you ever see this, know that my last wish and curse is that you burn, and burn slowly in the radiation of a leaking reactor. I hope your eyes boil, and your blood sublimes into the vacuum as your dying body is thrown into space by the others you've betrayed. You're as heartless as-""",GS_ZGR_MERC_cont3:Continue,
GS_ZGR_MERC_cont3SelA,DialogOptionSelected,$option == GS_ZGR_MERC_cont3,,He goes on to describe various torments deserved due to the poor character of someone called Zunya Glamor-Rotanev. By context clues you presume her to be some kind of high ranking Tri-Tachyon executive who commissioned him to carry out a failed expedition.,GS_ZGR_MERC_cont4:Try to find out what Tri-Tachyon was looking for out here,
GS_ZGR_MERC_cont3SelB,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == GS_ZGR_MERC_cont3
$player.metZGR",,He goes on to describe various torments deserved due to the poor character of Director of Special Acquisitions Zunya Glamor-Rotanev. It seems unlikely that she would be interested in a recording of the transmission.,GS_ZGR_MERC_cont4:Try to find records of what the mercenaries may have found,
GS_ZGR_MERC_cont4Sel,DialogOptionSelected,$option == GS_ZGR_MERC_cont4,ShowImageVisual salvor_explore_hull,"Your ops chief gives the order, and salvage teams move to prioritize the recovery of datacores and sensor buffers.

They are efficient in their work, and soon their relays hum with recovered data. Tiny packet drones shuttle recovered hardware between the wreck and your $shipOrFleet.",GS_ZGR_MERC_cont5:Investigate the results,
GS_ZGR_MERC_cont5Sel,DialogOptionSelected,$option == GS_ZGR_MERC_cont5,$salvageLeaveText = Leave 0,"Your tech officer is only frustrated by the results, however. The datacores have been wiped, memory overwritten thousands of times with hateful messages directed at Glamor-Rotanev. If these mercs found anything, if their logs had any clues, it's all been erased. If there was anything esoteric in their cargo holds, it's been dumped.

""It's all just scrap, $playerSirOrMadam,"" your tech officer reports, disappointed. Your ops chief grunts neutral acknowledgement; it's always scrap to them.","salExplore:Assess the ship's salvage value
defaultLeave:Leave",
,,,,,,
"# Abyssal ghost ships, ""Academy"" variation",,,,,,
GS_ACADEMY_open,OpenInteractionDialog,"$tag:salvageable
$gsType == GS_ACADEMY score:1000
!$explored","ShowDefaultVisual
PrintWreckDescription",Your $shipOrFleet approaches $aOrAn $nameInText.,"GS_ACADEMY_cont1:Explore
defaultLeave:Leave",
GS_ACADEMY_cont1Sel,DialogOptionSelected,$option == GS_ACADEMY_cont1,"$explored = true
UniqueEncounter setInteractedWith $gsType
$global.foundGAabyssExpedition = true","This hull is damaged, but through the scars of impacts and stripped armor your sensors officer recognizes the crest of the Galatia Academy. This expedition was lightly and inconspicuously armed, enough to discourage casual piracy while not offending the official neutrality of the Academy.

Perhaps this was not enough.

Salvage repeaters - a common feature of high-risk Academy probes and expeditions which promise a reward for return of data - are all dead. Manually disabled, overloaded and fused or even smashed with hand-tools, from the looks of it. Clearly someone did not want them transmitting their message, or any message, in this place.",GS_ACADEMY_cont2:Continue,
GS_ACADEMY_cont2Sel,DialogOptionSelected,$option == GS_ACADEMY_cont2,,"The expedition's equipment is not the best money can buy, but the sensor suites and detector arrays were obviously lovingly modified and maintained - what's left of them, anyway. They're torn apart, twisted and burnt into jagged black filaments.

Shielded datacores are recovered by salvor teams and returned for analysis in a signal-quarantined vault kept for this purpose. It does not take long for your tech officer to report results.","GS_ACADEMY_cont2b:""Report.""",
GS_ACADEMY_cont2Selb,DialogOptionSelected,$option == GS_ACADEMY_cont2b,,"""Judging from logs and fabrication tags, the expedition dates to circa cycle 176,"" your tech officer says. ""This was the flagship of a small flotilla. The rest were... lost.""

""Someone... tried to erase all records. Forge-reset.""","GS_ACADEMY_cont3:""So there's nothing?""",
GS_ACADEMY_cont3Sel,DialogOptionSelected,$option == GS_ACADEMY_cont3,,"""Not quite,"" your tech officer suppresses a sly grin.

There's simple deletion and there's systemic erasure done to ensure that data recovery is effectively impossible. Whoever did this was not proficient enough to do the latter.",GS_ACADEMY_cont4:Find out what happened to the expedition,
GS_ACADEMY_cont4Sel,DialogOptionSelected,$option == GS_ACADEMY_cont4,,"Datastreams are painstakingly recovered, the high-interest combat logs prioritized by your techs. The data is lossy, and the gaps must be filled by algorithms which, used improperly, have a reputation for confidently asserting false results.

Nonetheless.

You see the black of the abyss, and the cluster of lights and icons signifying the Galatia Expedition's flotilla. The view is highly abstract, a reconstruction of a visualization necessary in not only hyperspace but the uncertain depths of the Abyss.

You speed the stream forward to the point where everything goes wrong.",GS_ACADEMY_cont4B:Continue,
GS_ACADEMY_cont4SelB,DialogOptionSelected,$option == GS_ACADEMY_cont4B,,"The fleet approaches an Abyssal Light. A glow in the simulated display, a foggy illumination which somehow captures the cold and solipsistic loneliness of the veil beyond deep space.

The flagship comms hum with excited academicians eager to finally perform their experiments after long weeks of boredom.",GS_ACADEMY_cont5:Continue,
GS_ACADEMY_cont5Sel,DialogOptionSelected,$option == GS_ACADEMY_cont5,,"The flotilla's hyperspace bubble ripples, then strains under an impossible force. Anomalous sensor readings are tagged, then...

An error pops up from your own software. 
EXTREME UNRELIABILITY. Output may not reflect accurate reconstruction of data. Continue?",GS_ACADEMY_cont6:Hit 'continue',
GS_ACADEMY_cont6Sel,DialogOptionSelected,$option == GS_ACADEMY_cont6,,"The display is full of red icons, jagged warnings vectoring toward elements of the flotilla.

The chief Academician orders a full sensor burst, max power, using the integrated suite of the entire flotilla. There is a flash as EM surges; and gravimetrics pulse, hyperwave doppler, Atherton resonators...

Another error.
INTERRUPT: INSUFFICIENT DATA. Continue to next viable reconstruction?",GS_ACADEMY_cont7:Hit 'continue',
GS_ACADEMY_cont7Sel,DialogOptionSelected,$option == GS_ACADEMY_cont7,$salvageLeaveText = Leave 0,"The feed is degraded, patchy. The flotilla is gone; only the flagship remains, panicked voices on ship comms, in retreat from its previous course. The timeline show a halting record of desperate damage repairs and the crews' slow realization that they cannot make it back to civilized space.

It is a death-spiral known and feared by all spacer crews.

Systems break down, fuel and supplies dwindle. Morale breaks down. Then discipline. It unravels faster than usual with so many civilians.

You shut it off.","salExplore:Assess the ship's salvage value
defaultLeave:Leave",
,,,,,,
# Derelict Vambrace 1,,,,,,
GS_VAMBRACE_open,OpenInteractionDialog,"$id == derelict_vambrace score:1000
!$explored
#$gsType == GS_VAMBRACE score:1000","ShowDefaultVisual
FireAll gsVambraceHubOpts",Your $shipOrFleet approaches $aOrAn $nameInText.,,
gsVambOptHubDescriptionA,gsVambraceHubOpts,"!$didDescription
!$player.hasThreatDetectionSensorMods",$didDescription = true 0,"A starship-sized metal structure spins slowly before your $shipOrFleet. It is no ship, but a regular form of asymmetric proportions with a trough-like interior. It appears to have sustained tremendous battle-damage on its convex face, which is riven with gaping holes.

A cloud of debris, presumably from the structure, hangs in the blackness like flies around a corpse.",,
gsVambOptHubDescriptionB,gsVambraceHubOpts,"!$didDescription
$player.hasThreatDetectionSensorMods
!PlayerFleetHasShipWithBaseHull onslaught_mk1",$didDescription = true 0,"A starship-sized metal structure spins slowly before your $shipOrFleet. It is no ship, but a modular armor section from the Onslaught Mk.I which your sensors officer readily matches to your records despite the tremendous battle-damage.

Smaller pieces of debris, presumably from the structure, hang in the blackness like flies around a corpse.",,
gsVambOptHubDescriptionC,gsVambraceHubOpts,"!$didDescription
$player.hasThreatDetectionSensorMods
PlayerFleetHasShipWithBaseHull onslaught_mk1","$didDescription = true 0
$playerHasOneslaught = true","A starship-sized metal structure spins slowly before your $shipOrFleet. It is no ship, but a modular armor section which, despite tremendous battle-damage, matches the armored vambrace of the Onslaught Mk.I.

Your sensors officer builds a scan of the structure from your $shipOrFleet's sensor suite then overlays it onto the 'arm' of your own Onslaught Mk.I. The visual match is obvious despite the violence which has torn and warped the structure.

Smaller pieces of debris, presumably from the vambrace, hang in the blackness like flies around a corpse.",,
gsVambOptHubA,gsVambraceHubOpts,!$scanned,,,gsVambrace_explore1:Run a detailed scan,
gsVambOptHubB,gsVambraceHubOpts,"$scanned
!$investigated",,,gsVambrace_salvors1:Send salvors in for a closer look,
gsVambOptHubC,gsVambraceHubOpts,"$investigated
!$player.tookVambraceSamples
$player.metTanaica",,,"gsVambrace_sample:Take samples for Oya Tanaica, the nanoforge engineer on Asher",
gsVambOptHubLeave,gsVambraceHubOpts,,,,defaultLeave:Leave,
gsVambraceSample,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gsVambrace_sample,"AddTextSmall ""Acquired derelict structure samples"" highlight
$player.tookVambraceSamples = true
SetPersonHidden nanoforge_engineer false
FireAll gsVambraceHubOpts",You order material samples taken from representative sections of the structure. It is possible that something more might be learned about its provenance.,,
gsVambraceExplore1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gsVambrace_explore1,"$scanned = true
FireAll gsVambraceHubOpts","""Spectra and mass returns are consistent, mostly, with ship armor,"" your sensors officer reports. ""No active power systems, no atmo, no habitable volumes. Temperature approaching background.""

They look over their shoulder at you. ""It's dead. And it's been dead for a very long time.""

Sensors gives you an apologetic look. ""Conditions are strange out here, $playerSirOrMadam. We'll need a closer look to find out more.""",,
gsVambraceExplore1b,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == gsVambrace_explore1
$playerHasOneslaught","$scanned = true
FireAll gsVambraceHubOpts","""Spectra and mass returns are consistent with original armor composition from our, ah, matching specimen,"" your sensors officer reports. ""No active power systems, no atmo, no habitable volumes. Temperature approaching background.""

They look over their shoulder at you. ""It's dead, and it's been dead for a very long time.""

Sensors gives you an apologetic look. ""Conditions are strange out here, $playerSirOrMadam. We'll need a closer look to find out more.""",,
gsVambraceSalvors1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gsVambrace_salvors1,ShowImageVisual cache_large,"You give the word.

Your operations chief nods, then barks out deployment orders to the waiting salvor teams.

The investigation proceeds smoothly. The derelict structure and its attendant debris are truly cold and dead. Such battle-damage is familiar to your salvors, and this survey even easier due to the apparent lack of live munitions and none of the usual frozen or fried vacuum-desiccated remains.

Sensing a laxity in the crews, your ops chief growls admonitions over the general comms then orders a more detailed adherence to procedure.",gsVambrace_salvors2:Continue,
gsVambraceSalvors2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gsVambrace_salvors2,,"As reports and scans come in, a picture emerges - both a detailed holographic mapping and an understanding of what this structure is.

It is a piece of modular armor with structural attachment points, flux vent ports, and even an auxiliary sensor network, though no internal power sources.

The engineering is all recognizable as related to Domain standards, but as if from a crude half-foreign culture. Power connectors, for instance, are robustly built but oddly shaped and accompanied by an odd drift in signage iconography. It's nothing your salvors can't understand or adapt, but it is technology unlike even the oldest nanofabricated hulls and hardware designs used in the Persean Sector.","gsVambrace_salvors3:""Tech, what are we looking at here?""",
gsVambraceSalvors3,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gsVambrace_salvors3,,"Your technology officer jumps at your words; they were apparently quite lost in thought.

""Um, $playerSirOrMadam. If I had to... in short, it's..."" 

Your ops chief maintains an even expression, pointedly unreactive to this stuttering.

""It's ancient,"" Tech finally settles on a word. ""It can only be a product of the Early Domain.""","gsVambrace_salvors4:""Why is it here?""",
gsVambraceSalvors4,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gsVambrace_salvors4,"$investigated = true
FireAll gsVambraceHubOpts","""Judging by the battle damage..."" Your technology officer looks back at the specs, struggling. ""There was a battle.""

A look of concern grows. ""It has been here for a long time, but from the debris cloud... the conditions are strange enough, but I would speculate that this is not an untouched site. It's nothing like salvagers or scrappers, they've got distinctive patterns. I couldn't say who, or what, but I suspect the site has been disturbed, or moved.""

""If only it had datacores, buffers, something to analyze!"" Tech looks at your ops chief, who gives a single shake of their head.",,
gsVambraceSalvors1b,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == gsVambrace_salvors1
$playerHasOneslaught",ShowImageVisual cache_large,"You give the word.

Your operations chief nods, then barks out deployment orders to the waiting salvor teams.

The investigation proceeds smoothly. The structure and its attendant debris are truly cold and dead. Such battle-damage is familiar to your salvors, and this survey even easier due to the apparent lack of live munitions and none of the usual frozen or fried vacuum-desiccated remains.

Sensing a laxity in the crews, your ops chief growls admonitions over the general comms then orders a more detailed adherence to procedure.",gsVambrace_salvors2b:Continue,
gsVambraceSalvors2b,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gsVambrace_salvors2b,,"Reports and scans come in, a detailed holographic mapping forms in your primary display, and all data confirms with certainty that this is an Onslaught Mk.I vambrace.

The modular armor features structural attachment points, flux vent ports, and even an auxiliary sensor network, though no internal power sources.

The engineering is all recognizable as related to Domain standards, but as if from a crude half-foreign culture. Power connectors, for instance, are robustly built but oddly shaped and accompanied by an odd drift in signage iconography. Your salvors have understood and adapted to these oddities before. Nonetheless, it is technology unlike even the oldest nanofabricated hulls and hardware designs used in the Persean Sector.","gsVambrace_salvors3b:""Tech, what are we looking at here?""",
gsVambraceSalvors3b,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gsVambrace_salvors3b,"$investigated = true
FireAll gsVambraceHubOpts","""Judging by the battle damage..."" Your technology officer looks back at the specs, struggling. ""There was a battle.""

A look of concern grows. ""It has been here for a long time, but from the debris cloud... and just one vambrace, abandoned here? The conditions are strange enough, but I would speculate that this is not an untouched site. It doesn't look like salvagers or scrappers, they've got distinctive patterns. I couldn't say who, or what, but I suspect the site has been disturbed. Or moved.""

""If only it had datacores, buffers, something to analyze!"" Tech looks at your ops chief, who gives a single shake of their head.",,
,,,,,,
"# take Vambrace sample to Tanaika 
# and/or give her a Oneslaught sample?",,,,,,
DEVnanoforgeEngineerOption,PopulateOptions,"$global.isDevMode
$hasMarket
$market.id == asher
$menuState == main","SetOptionColor DEVoyaTanaica_askSample gray
SetOptionColor bffi_talkToEngineer0 gray",,"50:DEVoyaTanaica_askSample:DEV talk to nanoforge engineer about samples
50:bffi_talkToEngineer0:DEV do BFFI_TALK_TO_ENGINEER convo (janky)",
DEVnanoforgeEngineerOption2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == DEVoyaTanaica_askSample,"BeginConversation nanoforge_engineer
ShowPersonVisual
FireAll PopulateOptions",,,
oyaTanaicaAskSampleOption,PopulateOptions,"$id == nanoforge_engineer
$player.tookVambraceSamples
!$player.didVambraceSampleInvestigation",,,"oyaTanaica_askSample:""I'd like you to look at a material sample. I'll pay.""",
oyaTanaicaAskSampleResp,DialogOptionSelected,$option == oyaTanaica_askSample,FireAll oyaTanaicaSampleOpts,"""Hmm,"" she gives you a renewed look of interest. ""You're the one who had the glove. Right."" 

""Well you had me at 'pay', captain. Come on down and we'll have a look at... what did you say you had?""",,
oyaTanaicaAskSampleVambraceOpt,oyaTanaicaSampleOpts,"$player.tookVambraceSamples
!$player.didVambraceSampleInvestigation",,,"oyaTanaica_sampleVambrace:""A piece of modular armor found in the Abyss.""",
#,,,,,oyaTanaica_sampleOmega:,# Maybe later.
#,,,,,oyaTanaica_sampleThreat:,
#,,,,,oyaTanaica_sampleDweller:,
oyaTanaicaAskSampleBack,oyaTanaicaSampleOpts,,,,"oyaTanaica_sampleBack:""Never mind.""",
oyaTanaicaAskSampleBack2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == oyaTanaica_askSampleBack,,"She shrugs. ""It's your credits.""",,
oyaTanaicaAskSampleVambrace,DialogOptionSelected,$option == oyaTanaica_sampleVambrace,$sample_vambrace = true 0,"""The Abyss?"" Her eyes widen. ""You're braver than you look. Or stupider.""

""Anyway, come on down. I'll feed some excuse to traffic control.""","oyaTanaica_sampleShuttle:Shuttle down with the armor sample
oyaTanaica_sampleBack:""Never mind.""",
oyaTanaicaAskNeverMind,DialogOptionSelected,$option == oyaTanaica_sampleBack,FireAll PopulateOptions,"""Alright.""

She glances aside, not bothering to hide that she's checking the time.",,
oyaTanaicaAskSampleShuttle,DialogOptionSelected,$option == oyaTanaica_sampleShuttle,"EndConversation DO_NOT_FIRE
ShowLargePlanet","Descending to Asher, you glance out the viewport of your shuttle.

Stars disappear from the black tapestry of space as it begins to glow with a deep violet-blue before sinking into dim, ruddy brown.

The thick clouds of suspended fines are whipped away by the shuttle's flight through cold winds, and the shadow is replaced by the generalized sandy murk of Asher.",oyaTanaica_vambrace0:Continue,
oyaTanaicaVambrace0,DialogOptionSelected,$option == oyaTanaica_vambrace0,"BeginConversation nanoforge_engineer
ShowPersonVisual","* * *

""Doesn't look like much, does it,"" says Senior Engineer Tanaica as she takes the sample from you - a block of armor composite, edges rough from the salvors' plasma cutters.

She places the sample onto a shelf which retracts into the towering white casing of the analysis suite. Transparent panes reveal the machine's arcane inner workings.

""You found it in the Abyss, you said?""

A containment shield drops over the sample port with a satisfying clunk.","oyaTanaica_vambrace1:""A planetoid in the Abyss. Some nameless rock.""",
oyaTanaicaVambrace1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == oyaTanaica_vambrace1,"SetTextHighlights ""10,000""
DoCanAffordCheck 10000 oyaTanaica_vambrace2 false","""Most of 'em are, aren't they.""

She manipulates the controls, evacuating the atmo from the sample container. Then she stops to look at you.

""If this is just a chunk of starship armor, I can tell you that for free. Saves you 10,000 credits.""

""But if you want me to look real close and do some professional speculation,"" she holds out her datapad, ready to receive payment.","oyaTanaica_vambrace2:Pay 10,000 credits
oyaTanaica_vambraceEarlyOut:""It's a piece of armor. I'll take it and go.""",
oyaTanaicaVambraceEarlyOut,DialogOptionSelected,$option == oyaTanaica_vambraceEarlyOut,"EndConversation
ShowDefaultVisual","She shrugs, and reverses the sample insertion procedure. 

Senior Engineer Tanaica sends you on your way back to orbit with no more farewell than a succinct ""Right then.""",,
oyaTanaicaVambrace2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == oyaTanaica_vambrace2,AddCredits -10000,"Your TriPad pings confirmation, and hers responds cheerfully.

""Right then,"" she says, equally cheerful.

Tanaica's datapad disappears as she turns back to the controls. A loud humming grows - it feels almost ticklish in your teeth for a moment as she adjusts power levels.

Displays bloom with readouts, cheerful greens abounding. A holo of the sample flickers into being.",oyaTanaica_vambrace3:Continue,
oyaTanaicaVambrace3,DialogOptionSelected,$option == oyaTanaica_vambrace3,,"The machine's hum drops an octave, and loses some of its urgency.

""Huh,"" she says. She wears a look of blank unease.

""Weird.""","oyaTanaica_vambrace4:""What's weird?""",
oyaTanaicaVambrace4,DialogOptionSelected,$option == oyaTanaica_vambrace4,,"Tanaica manipulates her controls and a small cutaway pulls out of the rough block of armor. It scales to fill the volume of the holo.

Another segmentation of scale iterates, then another as Tanaica brings the resolution to the nearly-atomic. Patterns of false colour flash highlighting pseudo-crystals, various regular - and irregular - structures, as well as flaws.

""It's the damnedest thing, isn't it,"" she says, attention focused on the display.","oyaTanaica_vambrace5:""Is it?""
oyaTanaica_vambrace5a:""Definitely. Wow. Look at that. The... ah...""",
oyaTanaicaVambrace5a,DialogOptionSelected,$option == oyaTanaica_vambrace5a,"$player.ethosSarcastic++
$option = oyaTanaica_vambrace5 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","She turns to look at you, raising an eyebrow.",,
oyaTanaicaVambrace5-1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == oyaTanaica_vambrace5,,"""Sorry, cap,"" she says. ""I should be thinking out loud, you paid good credits for this after all.""

She licks her lips, then releases a breath.",oyaTanaica_vambrace5-2:Continue,
oyaTanaicaVambrace5-2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == oyaTanaica_vambrace5-2,,"""It's nanoforged. Obvious stuff, look at that drift,"" she taps something and a distortion in the material structure becomes exaggerated.

""Crude, relatively speaking. Modern forges won't do it like this. Hm. 'Modern' meaning anything from the last thousand cycles. Seems like you found a genuine museum piece. Not unheard of 'course. Scavengers pull in bits of old sporeships and Explorarium junk often enough. Saw a bit of cryosleeper scanned when I was in training. Fascinating stuff.""

She taps not the controls, but the casing of the analysis suite. ""So it's old, but that's not what's strange.""","oyaTanaica_vambrace6a:""You like drawing this out for maximum drama, don't you.""
oyaTanaica_vambrace6b:""So what makes it strange?""",
oyaTanaicaVambrace6a,DialogOptionSelected,$option == oyaTanaica_vambrace6a,,"""Ha!"" She smiles, if uneasily. ""Got me. It's boring as dirt here in Luddie-land, gotta make my own fun.""

""Still, this really is interesting... There's no embedded fabrication-rights!""

She looks at you significantly, as if this means something important.","oyaTanaica_vambrace7:""So? A hacked pirate forge will strip out the FRM.""",
oyaTanaicaVambrace6b,DialogOptionSelected,$option == oyaTanaica_vambrace6b,,"""There are no embedded fabrication-rights!""

She looks at you as if this means something important, and you're supposed to respond.","oyaTanaica_vambrace7:""So? A hacked pirate forge will strip out the FRM.""",
oyaTanaicaVambrace7,DialogOptionSelected,$option == oyaTanaica_vambrace7,,"""Sure. And they've been churning out garbage for 200 cycles. But what we see here is that this was made by a very old, very large forge. Probably top of the line for the time. And your sample has been exposed to space for a long, long time. And no FRM.""

""Haven't seen this before."" She rubs her fingers together, thinking. ""Either someone was running a starsystem polity-level illicit forge a couple thousand cycles ago and you found the results, or... hm, you found something really weird.""

She turns to you. ""Where'd you find this? Some rock in the Abyss?""","oyaTanaica_vambrace8:""Some rock. Why can't it have been legally forged with no FRM?""",
oyaTanaicaVambrace8,DialogOptionSelected,$option == oyaTanaica_vambrace8,,"""That's... that'd be insane. The whole point of the Domain was to control this stuff! Well,"" she concedes to herself, ""Maybe the Gate Network was point number one.""

""But regulating the nanoforges would have been two. Maybe three. Definitely important. Everything is stamped and tracked, that way you know who made what, where it ends up, when to collect forge-taxes, and who to blame when things go wrong.""

""It was..."" She shakes her hands at the analysis suite in an odd gesture, emphasizing the size of the concept. ""It was the basis for interstellar civilization itself!""",oyaTanaica_vambrace9:Continue,
oyaTanaicaVambrace9,DialogOptionSelected,$option == oyaTanaica_vambrace9,"$option = oyaTanaica_vambrace10 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","She takes a deep breath, looking self-conscious at her own outburst, then busies herself with flicking at some controls; the machine slows its hum to a dull whine and then a sudden unsettling absence of a background noise you weren't even conscious of hearing.

""Some rebel polity in the Domain-era I guess? Maybe they had some frontier-freedom notions before the Domain Armada re-stomped them into compliance. I'd pay good credits myself to learn how in Ludd's seven hells it ended up on some rock in the Abyss!""

She catches herself, then grins. ""Uh, not that I wouldn't appreciate that answer for free if you happen to solve it.""",,
oyaTanaicaVambrace10optsA,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == oyaTanaica_vambrace10
!$global.foundOneslaught",,,"oyaTanaica_vambrace11:""I'll consider it. If I find out more""",
oyaTanaicaVambrace10optsB,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == oyaTanaica_vambrace10
$global.foundOneslaught",,,"oyaTanaica_vambrace11:""I'll consider your request.""
oyaTanaica_vambraceOneslaught1:""Have you heard of the Onslaught mk.I?""",
oyaTanaicaVambrace11,DialogOptionSelected,$option == oyaTanaica_vambrace11,AdjustRepActivePerson FRIENDLY 1,"The sample emerges, and - more gingerly, now - Senior Engineer Tanaica pulls on some gloves and places it back in your sample container.

""You find some interesting stuff out there if you don't mind me saying so, captain.""

She nods approvingly. ""Thank you for the subsidy. I'll be sure to enjoy myself once I wrap up this miserable Asher contract.""",oyaTanaica_vambraceOut1:Continue,
oyaTanaicaVambraceOneslaught1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == oyaTanaica_vambraceOneslaught1,"$option = oyaTanaica_vambraceOneslaught2 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","""Oh sure,"" she says.

The sample emerges, and - more gingerly, now - Senior Engineer Tanaica pulls on some gloves and places it back in your sample container.

""Wait."" She looks at the sample container. ""Really?""",,
oyaTanaicaVambraceOneslaught2a,DialogOptionSelected,$option == oyaTanaica_vambraceOneslaught2,,,"oyaTanaica_vambraceOneslaught3a:""Really.""",
oyaTanaicaVambraceOneslaught2b,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == oyaTanaica_vambraceOneslaught2
