FireAll BFINconvOpts","Bornanew looks almost surprised at your words. He does not pray, or thank Providence. He simply looks directly at you through the waver of the comm-link.

""Thank you, captain. Against all odds, you've cast a light upon my path toward redemption.""

Perhaps apologetic for the moment of earnestness, he quickly adds, ""I am prepared to leave when you are ready for me. I shall await word of your shuttle.""",,
BFFIshuttleBornanew,DialogOptionSelected,$option == BFFI_shuttleBornanew,"HideFirstPerson
ShowLargePlanet
SetPersonHidden bornanew true",Traffic control is mercifully efficient when arranging transport for a Knight of Ludd.,BFFI_shuttleBornanew2:Continue,
"# BFFI - Bornanew Files, case of the False Idols",,,,,,
BFFIshuttleBornanew2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == BFFI_shuttleBornanew2,"ShowPersonVisual
unset $global.bffi_bornanewLocation
$global.bornanewBadBoy = 0
AddCredits 50000","Before long, Novice Bornanew steps aboard your flagship carrying only a small satchel of his possessions.

Your TriPad pings acknowledgement of a funds transfer from the Church of Galactic Redemption.","BFFI_onBoardingStateroom:""I've ordered an officer's stateroom cleared for you.""
BFFI_onBoardingBerth:""You'll be given a berth, like any member of the crew.""
BFFI_onBoardingBerthPenance:""You'll be given a berth, like any member of the crew. Penance is penance.""",
BFFIonBoardingBerth,DialogOptionSelected,$option == BFFI_onBoardingBerth,"$option = BFFI_onBoarding2 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","""You have my thanks, captain,"" he says. ""That will serve my needs most adequately.""",,
BFFIonBoardingBerthPenance,DialogOptionSelected,$option == BFFI_onBoardingBerthPenance,"$option = BFFI_onBoarding2 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","""Of course, captain,"" he says. ""That will serve my needs most adequately.""",,
BFFIonBoardingStateroom,DialogOptionSelected,$option == BFFI_onBoardingStateroom,,"""Such extravagance is not necessary for a mere novice, captain,"" he says uncomfortably.","BFFI_onBoardingStateroomWork:""A private workspace will allow you to best perform your duties.""
BFFI_onBoardingStateroomHosp:""Nonsense. You're my guest and I'll treat you as such.""
BFFI_onBoardingStateroomDowngrade:""If you wish, you will be given a crew-berth.""",
BFFIonBoardingRespWork,DialogOptionSelected,$option == BFFI_onBoardingStateroomWork,"$player.BFFIgaveBornanewStateroom = true
$option = BFFI_onBoarding2 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","Bornanew nods, not quite a bow. ""You are right, of course.""",,
BFFIonBoardingRespHosp,DialogOptionSelected,$option == BFFI_onBoardingStateroomHosp,"$player.BFFIgaveBornanewStateroom = true
$option = BFFI_onBoarding2 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","Bornanew nods, not quite a bow. ""My apologies, I did not intend to spurn your hospitality. It is a virtue.""",,
BFFIonBoardingRespDowngrade,DialogOptionSelected,$option == BFFI_onBoardingStateroomDowngrade,"$option = BFFI_onBoarding2 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","""If you would, please,"" Bornanew says with a nod that isn't quite a bow. ""It would be most appropriate for my service of penance.""",,
BFFIonBoard2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == BFFI_onBoarding2,"HideFirstPerson
ShowLargePlanet","You have Bornanew's luggage taken to his quarters by a couple crew who clearly expected heavier lifting, then have him meet you in a debriefing room to plan your next move.",BFFI_onBoardingYarbStart:Continue,
BFFIonBoardYarbStart,DialogOptionSelected,$option == BFFI_onBoardingYarbStart,"ShowPersonVisual
Highlight ""Menes Yaribay""
$option = BFFI_onBoardingYarbResp 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","Novice Bornanew speaks from the head of the table on which he has placed a paper notebook. He seems disinclined to use the shared workspace of the holo visualization suite; you're not even sure he brought a datapad.

""...collector who now possesses this duplicate relic is a man by the name Menes Yaribay, a minor member of Gens Yaribay of Kazeron,"" he looks to you for a sign of recognition.",,
BFFIonBoardYarbRespA,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == BFFI_onBoardingYarbResp
$player.metHorusYaribay",,"Of course you know the Yaribays. You were given Horus Yaribay's diplomatic credentials to arrange a meeting with High Hegemon Daud.

Horus Yaribay might owe you a favor, depending on how he views the situation.",BFFI_onBoardingYarb2know:Explain this to $global.jethroName,
BFFIonBoardYarbRespB,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == BFFI_onBoardingYarbResp
$player.abusedYaribayCred score:10",,"Of course you know the Yaribays. You were given Horus Yaribay's diplomatic credentials to arrange a meeting with High Hegemon Daud and have, on at least one occasion, used those credentials to call a favor on account of Gens Yaribay's prestige.

Hopefully he didn't find out.","BFFI_onBoardingYarb2confess:Explain everything to $global.jethroName
BFFI_onBoardingYarb2noConfess:Explain, but leave out the abuse of credentials part",
BFFIonBoardYarbRespC,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == BFFI_onBoardingYarbResp
$player.gaveDaudYaribayContact score:5",,"Of course you know the Yaribays. You were given Horus Yaribay's diplomatic credentials to arrange a meeting with High Hegemon Daud. During that meeting, you handed over the key required for an encrypted channel between Horus Yaribay and Baikal Daud.

Horus Yaribay might owe you a favor, depending on how he views the situation.",BFFI_onBoardingYarb2know:Explain this to $global.jethroName,
BFFIonBoardYarbRespD,DialogOptionSelected,$option == BFFI_onBoardingYarbResp,,"You know of Gens Yaribay of Kazeron, one of the three dominant ruling family-corporations. Theirs is most inclined toward rapprochement with the Hegemony, focusing less on heavy military industry and more on interfactional ventures.","BFFI_onBoardingYarb2:""Yes, I've heard of the Yaribays.""",
BFFIonBoardYarbRespBconfess,DialogOptionSelected,$option == BFFI_onBoardingYarb2confess,$player.BFFIconfessedYaribayCredAbuse = true,"Bornanew looks concerned as you describe your dealings. ""Your conscience, your soul, is between you and- well, I am not your judge or confessor.""

""From a practical standpoint, I would advise caution in asking too much of Horus of Gens Yaribay, to his face or behind it. He may know but choose not to act on your transgression.""",BFFI_onBoardingYarb3:Continue,
BFFIonBoardYarbRespBnoConfess,DialogOptionSelected,$option == BFFI_onBoardingYarb2noConfess,$player.BFFIdidntConfessYaribayCredAbuse = true,"A brief look of concern crosses Bornanew's face, and he pauses as if composing an awkward question. He puts his hand back down on the table, seeming to dismiss the notion, and responds in a different tone.",BFFI_onBoardingYarb3:Continue,# 'course he knows.
BFFIonBoardYarb2knowEm,DialogOptionSelected,$option == BFFI_onBoardingYarb2know,,"""This is providential,"" he says, nodding. ""Your previous dealings with Horus Yaribay could open an easier path to resolving the Church's problem.""","BFFI_onBoardingYarb3:""My, uh, thoughts exactly.""",
BFFIonBoardYarb2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == BFFI_onBoardingYarb2,"$option = BFFI_onBoardingYarb3 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected",He nods and proceeds.,,
BFFIonBoardYarb3,DialogOptionSelected,$option == BFFI_onBoardingYarb3,"Highlight ""Olinadu""
FireAll BFFIonBoardMenesOpts","""The question, then, is how Horus Yaribay, the nominal gens leader, views Menes Yaribay's recent interest in religious artifacts.""

Bornanew flips through his paper book, not really taking the time to read the dense notes therein. He runs a finger across lists of names.

""Not long ago Menes Yaribay was assigned the office of demarch, in essence the executive administrator, of Olinadu in the Kumari Kandam system. It is not a prestigious post. Olinadu is a small mining colony and the system is rife with Luddic Path activity. It is a dangerous, corrupt place.""

Bornanew eye's return to you. ""This is why I need your help.""",,
BFFIonBoardMenesOpt1,BFFIonBoardMenesOpts,!$askedMenes ,,,"BFFI_onBoardAskMenes:""You've done your research. Tell me about Menes Yaribay himself.""",
BFFIonBoardMenesOpt2,BFFIonBoardMenesOpts,!$askedOlinadu,,,"BFFI_onBoardAskInCharge:""How did a Kazeron aristocrat get put in charge of Olinadu?""",
BFFIonBoardMenesOpt3,BFFIonBoardMenesOpts,!$askedRelic,,,"BFFI_onBoardAskRelic:""Tell me more about the relic at the center of this. What is it?""",
BFFIonBoardMenesOpt4,BFFIonBoardMenesOpts,"$askedRelic
!$saidTartessus",,,"BFFI_onBoardAskTart4:""Wait, why's the real glove on Tartessus if Ludd removed it on Gilead?""",
BFFIonBoardMenesOpt5,BFFIonBoardMenesOpts,$askedRelic,,,"BFFI_onBoardAskPlan:""What's the plan? Ask Menes nicely for the glove?""",
#BFFIonBoardMenesOptWar,,,,,,
BFFIonBoardMenesOptYou,BFFIonBoardMenesOpts,!$askedChalcedon,,,"BFFI_onBoardAskChalcedon:""Kumari Kandam? You were on Chalcedon. With the Path.""",
BFFIonBoardAskChalcedon,DialogOptionSelected,$option == BFFI_onBoardAskChalcedon,"$askedChalcedon = true 0
FireAll BFFIonBoardMenesOpts","""Indeed I was."" He's steady. ""You know of this. There I met Wrestling Sedge of the Luddic Path, and there I left my vows. For a time.""

A pause. ""You followed my path, and spoke with the man Sedge. He told you where I went from there, Mazalot, where you found me.""",,
BFFIonBoardAskChalcedonShot,DialogOptionSelected,"$player.shotSedge
$option == BFFI_onBoardAskChalcedon","$askedChalcedon = true 0
FireAll BFFIonBoardMenesOpts","""Indeed I was."" He's steady as he speaks. ""You know of this. There I met Wrestling Sedge of the Luddic Path, and there I left my vows. For a time.""

A pause. ""And you killed the man Sedge,"" he says. ""The Path will have no love for you there, but I trust that you will be prepared for... that.""",,
BFFIonBoardAskMenes,DialogOptionSelected,$option == BFFI_onBoardAskMenes,$askedMenes = true 0,"""Certain tawdry media outlets in the outer League worlds and beyond report rumor and gossip about affairs, social vendettas, and... how shall I put this... decadent festivities undertaken by Menes. More so in his younger years, at least."" Bornanew turns pages in his notebook, not reading, but recalling as he goes through the motions with his hands.

""His enthusiasm for such pursuits has waned from the cycles of his youth, and his interests have shifted. At heart, I suspect Menes is still a man who wishes for all to hear his name, and for all who hear it to be very impressed.""",BFFI_onBoardAskMenes2:Continue,
BFFIonBoardAskMenes2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == BFFI_onBoardAskMenes2,FireAll BFFIonBoardMenesOpts,"""Unfortunately for his ambition, he is a natural dilettante in all pursuits. He avoids challenge, seeking instead flattery and the appearance of success which may be purchased with credits."" Bornanew reports this without obvious outward judgment, as if discussing the results of a gravimetric survey.

""To his gens, Menes has given only scandal and debt. I suspect he was placed in the Olinadu administration to limit his ability to further damage their reputation.""

Bornanew smiles grimly now. ""It is some irony that he has potentially stumbled into more trouble than ever.""",,
BFFIonBoardAskInCharge,DialogOptionSelected,$option == BFFI_onBoardAskInCharge,"$askedOlinadu = true 0
FireAll BFFIonBoardMenesOpts","""Gens Yaribay has a controlling interest in the military corporation which exercises the monopoly of violence for the polity of Olinadu. The Pathers are an ever-present threat, so those who don't cooperate... well, that is the stick which compels. The carrot, on the other hand, is a stream of investment credits facilitated by Gens Yaribay brokers.""

""The locals cooperate with this arrangement, and agreed to vote Menes Yaribay to an executive position, perhaps understanding that he'd play the role as a figurehead rather than a serious administrator. Olinadu receives investment and safety while, from all accounts, Menes Yaribay simply wants to be liked.""

""Compared to the alternatives,"" says Bornanew, ""he is an ideal overlord.""",,
BFFIonBoardAskRelic,DialogOptionSelected,$option == BFFI_onBoardAskRelic,$askedRelic = true 0,"""Yes, the... artifact."" Bornanew looks down, clasping his hands together, then taking them apart and setting them deliberately on the table.

""Ludd's right-hand glove,"" an abashed smile appears.

""A standard work-glove of Domain manufacture. Light vac-suit compatible. The story is that Ludd removed it to touch the ground of Gilead.""","BFFI_onBoardAskRelic1a:""And you don't think it's real? The original, I mean.""
BFFI_onBoardAskRelic1b:""Seems like a lot to get worked up about.""
BFFI_onBoardAskRelic1c:""What's Ludd going to do with two right-hand gloves?""",
BFFIonBoardAskRelic1a,DialogOptionSelected,$option == BFFI_onBoardAskRelic1a,"$option = BFFI_onBoardAskRelic2 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","""It's a real glove,"" he says, ""That much is true.""

""It's just a work glove, one of many designs prevalent through the immediate pre- and post-Collapse Persean Sector.""",,
BFFIonBoardAskRelic1b,DialogOptionSelected,$option == BFFI_onBoardAskRelic1b,"$option = BFFI_onBoardAskRelic2 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","""I think,"" he begins, ""it is a matter of seeking a physical connection with the sacred.""",,
BFFIonBoardAskRelic1c,DialogOptionSelected,$option == BFFI_onBoardAskRelic1c,"$option = BFFI_onBoardAskRelic2 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","Bornanew laughs. ""Yes, exactly.""",,
BFFIonBoardAskRelic2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == BFFI_onBoardAskRelic2,,"""My objection is that the glove, even if it is the glove, is not important. What is important is Ludd's message, Ludd's sacrifice; it is the act of a divine moral force touching the soul of humanity with supreme grace.""",BFFI_onBoardAskRelic3:Continue,
BFFIonBoardAskRelic3,DialogOptionSelected,$option == BFFI_onBoardAskRelic3,,"""What is a glove to the light of Revelation?"" The words come out forcefully.

""Even if it were Ludd's glove - and that we can't, and should not, be sure of - would God love you more for possessing it? Touching, looking upon, and worshipping it?""

His brow furrows. ""Then some would try to extract DNA from the glove. Clone Ludd, they say, to re-open a connection to God."" He shakes his head furiously, ""As if you could fool God with the twin of the prophet's body!""

""Or the glove that body might have worn.""",BFFI_onBoardAskRelic4:Continue,
BFFIonBoardAskRelic4,DialogOptionSelected,$option == BFFI_onBoardAskRelic4,$player.sawBornanewGoBeastMode = true,"""It's the fool's logic of 'magic' of the lowest kind, the heretical notion that humanity might manipulate the Divine to our own ends. Creation turned on its head!""

You've never seen Bornanew like this, his voice like a river; his physical size giving power to his words. Seeing you see this, he realizes it himself.

""I apologize for my outburst, captain,"" he says, looking down.","BFFI_onBoardAskRelic5a:""Let's try to focus on the matter, ah, at hand.""
BFFI_onBoardAskRelic5b:""No need to apologize. I can't help but agree.""
bffi_onBoardAskRelic5d:""But magic isn't real. So what harm is focusing on a glove, fake relic or not?""",
BFFIonBoardAskRelic5a,DialogOptionSelected,$option == BFFI_onBoardAskRelic5a,FireAll BFFIonBoardMenesOpts,"He nods, suppressing a smile, looking down at his notebook. He puts his hands together again.",,
BFFIonBoardAskRelic5b,DialogOptionSelected,$option == BFFI_onBoardAskRelic5b,FireAll BFFIonBoardMenesOpts,"He meets your gaze. ""I shall interpret your words as forgiveness. It is nonetheless unseemly for a Knight to let uncontrolled passion rule their actions.""",,
BFFIonBoardAskRelic5c,DialogOptionSelected,$option == BFFI_onBoardAskRelic5c,,,,
BFFIonBoardAskRelic5d,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_onBoardAskRelic5d,#FireBest BFFIonBoardAskRelic5dCheck,"""Of course, of course."" He rubs his chin, calmer now.

""The problem is not that it might work, but that such self-trickery will lead the Faithful astray from the Word. And if we don't follow the Word, then what use have we for revelation? Are we to simply discard God's gifts?""

He sits, looking into the distance somewhere. ""Ludd chose the revealed path not because it was easy, and not because it was without suffering. Ludd chose because it was Good.""",bffi_onBoardAskRelic5e:Continue,"# bffi_onBoardAskRelic5dCotton:""I've heard those words before. From Brother Cotton."""
#BFFIonBoardAskRelic5dCheck,BFFIonBoardAskRelic5dCheck,!$player.luddChoseBecauseItWasGood,RemoveOption bffi_onBoardAskRelic5dCotton,,,
BFFIonBoardAskRelic5e,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_onBoardAskRelic5e,FireAll BFFIonBoardMenesOpts,"He glances at you with a fleeting grimace of self-reflection.

""With further apology for the ramble through theology, captain; the matter of the false relic should be our focus.""",,
BFFIonBoardAskRelic5f,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_onBoardAskRelic5f,FireAll BFFIonBoardMenesOpts,"Mention of Cotton dims Bornanew's expression. ""He's read the Word, too, of course. In his way.""

He sighs, deeply. ""Let his crimes, worldly and spiritual, serve as bloody warning of the path those... that those uncertain of their faith might be compelled to follow. I pray it weren't so.""

""Which, with apologies for the ramble through theology, brings us back to the false relic.""",,
BFFIonBoardAskTart4,DialogOptionSelected,$option == BFFI_onBoardAskTart4,"$saidTartessus = true 0
FireAll BFFIonBoardMenesOpts","Bornanew gives you a look.

""It's a tedious story. And unimportant.""",,
BFFIonBoardAskPlan1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == BFFI_onBoardAskPlan,FireAll BFFIonBoardHorusCheck,"Bornanew closes his book of notes.

""It has been made clear to me that the Church would like this problem, this false idol, to quietly disappear,"" he says. ""It can only tear open old rifts within the Church which would weaken the resolve of the Faithful. It would turn walker against walker in troubling times which promise naught but more trouble.""

""I am prepared to ask nicely, but I do not believe Menes will agree to give someone like myself his glove.""","bffi_onBoardPlanToMe:""But you think he might listen to someone like me.""
bffi_onBoardPlanBuy:""We could offer to buy it.""
bffi_onBoardPlanSteal:""We could steal it.""
bffi_onBoardPlanHorus:""I could talk to Horus Yaribay. He leads his gens, presumably.""",
BFFIonBoardHorusCheck,BFFIonBoardHorusCheck,!$player.gaveDaudYaribayContact ,RemoveOption bffi_onBoardPlanHorus,,,
BFFIonBoardPlanOptsToMe,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_onBoardPlanToMe,"$option = BFFI_onBoardEnd 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","""Yes,"" he says with the hint of a smile.",,
BFFIonBoardPlanOptsHorus,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_onBoardPlanHorus,"$option = BFFI_onBoardEnd 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","""Interesting."" Bornanew rubs his chin. ""If you believe Horus will be receptive to you bearing this... news. I wonder if it may be as simple as that.""",,
BFFIonBoardPlanOptsSteal,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_onBoardPlanSteal,"$option = BFFI_onBoardEnd 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","""It is... yes, that is possible,"" he says begrudgingly. ""I would like to know more before we act, however. I pray this may prove simpler than could be hoped.""",,
BFFIonBoardPlanOptsBuy,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_onBoardPlanBuy,"$global.bffi_preproposedBuyerOption = true
$option = BFFI_onBoardEnd 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","""You could."" Bornanew emphasizes 'you'. ""The Church refuses to acknowledge the false relic.""",,
BFFIonBoardEnd,DialogOptionSelected,$option == BFFI_onBoardEnd,"$global.bffi_goMeetMenesYaribay = true
Call $global.bffi_ref updateStage","""I propose you contact Menes directly. If you show interest in his pursuits, I believe he will be well-disposed toward someone of your... repute. He could provide us with information to plan our next move.""

Bornanew shuts his notebook.","bffi_onBoardEnd2:""To Olinadu, then.""
bffi_onBoardEnd2b:""My repute?""",
BFFIonBoardEnd2b,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_onBoardEnd2b,RemoveOption bffi_onBoardEnd2b,"""Your repute. As you well know,"" he says rather definitively. ""And so will Menes.""",,
