FireAll BFFImpBuyerHub3Opts","As you commit to the lie, Bornanew gives you a look of absolute weariness.

Menes turns to him, ""This is true? This is why you're here, isn't it. The backing of the Church, of course!""

""Yes,"" Bornanew says robotically, his attempt at a pleasant countenance looks like an appalling mask of pain.

Even Menes seems to sense something is off. ""Are you feeling well, Knight?"" he asks. ""Perhaps you aren't used to the quality of drink I serve.""",,
BFFImpBuyerConChurch1backOff,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_mpBuyerConChurchB,"$madeArgChurch = true
FireAll BFFImpBuyerHub3Opts","Bornanew closes his eyes, and you hear his sigh of relief.

Menes glances at him, giving a funny look, then back at you. ""Ah, of course. Ha-ha."" He clears his throat. ""Odd folk, you spacers,"" he says as if to himself.",,
,,,,,,
BFFImpBuyerHub3OptDep200k,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_mpBuyerHub3Dep200k,"AddCredits -200000
$option = bffi_mpBuyerHub3DepDone 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","Menes smirks, and holds out his TriPad, ready to accept your transfer code. Perhaps he feels like he's calling your bluff.",,
BFFImpBuyerHub3OptDep225k,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_mpBuyerHub3Dep225k,"AddCredits -225000
$option = bffi_mpBuyerHub3DepDone 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","Menes smirks, and holds out his TriPad, ready to accept your transfer code. Perhaps he feels like he's calling your bluff.",,
BFFImpBuyerHub3OptDep250k,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_mpBuyerHub3Dep250k,"
AddCredits -250000
$option = bffi_mpBuyerHub3DepDone 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","Menes smirks, and holds out his TriPad, ready to accept your transfer code. Perhaps he feels like he's calling your bluff.",,
BFFImpBuyerHub3OptDepDone,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_mpBuyerHub3DepDone,"$madeArgDeposit = true 0
$buyerArgsMade++
FireAll BFFImpBuyerHub3Opts","You tap your TriPad to his and it gives a happy little ping.

""Ah,"" Menes looks down to confirm. ""So you are serious. I must admit, your decisiveness is impressive. Most spacer captains, they're all talk. You,"" he lifts his eyebrows like a conspirator, ""mean business.""",,
BFFImpBuyerHub3OptDemarch,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_mpBuyerHub3OptDemarch,"$madeArgDemarch = true 0
$buyerArgsMade++
FireAll BFFImpBuyerHub3Opts","""But of course,"" Menes says, pouring on a gracious act. ""Silly me, so caught up in your reputation as a space captain... having a respectable title - you must understand - it is simply unexpected.""

""We're the League!"" He slaps a hand across your back. ""We have to stick together, you know. Or the Hegemony will get us - or, precious Ludd, the Church might roll in to force us all to pray night and day, ha!"" He looks toward Bornanew, ""Ha-ha! A joke, friend, a joke.""",,
BFFImpBuyerHub3OptDemarchB,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_mpBuyerHub3OptDemarch
!$player.isLeagueMember","$madeArgDemarch = true 0
$buyerArgsMade++
FireAll BFFImpBuyerHub3Opts","""But of course,"" Menes says, pouring on a gracious act. ""Silly me, so caught up in your reputation as just a space captain... having a respectable title - you must understand - it is simply unexpected.""

""Well, I'm sure you'll join the League soon enough!"" He slaps a hand across your back. ""We have to stick together, you know. Or the Hegemony will get us - or, precious Ludd, the Church might roll in to force us all to pray night and day, ha!"" He looks toward Bornanew, ""Ha-ha! A joke, friend, a joke.""",,
BFFImpBuyerHub3OptCommission,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_mpBuyerHub3OptCommission,"$madeArgCommission = true 0
$buyerArgsMade++
FireAll BFFImpBuyerHub3Opts","""No doubt!"" Menes exclaims, ""Why, I should have commended you earlier for your service to the League. I was so caught up in your reputation as a spacer - you know, adventures and schemes and the like - it completely slipped my mind that you're on our side."" 

He slaps a hand across your back. ""We appreciate your work, you know. Imagine if the Hegemony came for us - or, precious Ludd, imagine if the Church rolled in to force us all to pray night and day, ha!"" He looks toward Bornanew, ""Ha-ha! A joke, friend, a joke.""",,
BFFImpBuyerHub3OptArroyo,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_mpBuyerConArroyo,"$player.toldMenesYaribayArroyoBacksGlovePurchase = true
$player.ethosLiar++
$madeArgArroyo = true 0
$buyerArgsMade++
FireAll BFFImpBuyerHub3Opts","""Rayan Arroyo, you say?"" Menes perks up. ""Yes, I do believe I've met the man. An honest dealer. No-nonsense. Good head on his shoulders. Fantastic taste... have you met his tailor? Stars above, a wonder! I should have them cloned.""

""Well,"" he nods to himself, ""I admit this does change my perspective. You should have mentioned him before!""",,
BFFImpBuyerHub3OptHorus,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_mpBuyerHub3OptHorus,"$player.toldMenesYaribayAboutHorusCredentials = true
$madeArgHorus = true 0
$buyerArgsMade++
FireAll BFFImpBuyerHub3Opts","You draw your TriPad and demonstrate.

""By the stars, he did,"" Menes says, eyes wide. ""I knew I recognized your name from somewhere! There must have been a comms sent to the upper gens about this ploy Horus was running. That's cousin Horus for you, isn't it? Always pushing his little projects.""

""Well,"" he looks as if he's reappraising you, ""If you're good enough for cousin Horus, I suppose I could be convinced to make certain allowances.""",,
BFFImpBuyerHub3OptE2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_mpBuyerHub3OptE2,$madeArgBornanew = true 0,"""Captain $playerName trusts you implicitly,"" Bornanew explains, ""So as $playerHisOrHer advisor, I must act the skeptic. I assure you, Demarch Yaribay, it brings me no pleasure to appear to question and besmirch your fine reputation.""

He speaks with such sincerity, for just a moment you can almost believe $global.jethroName isn't lying.

""Consider it a policy of 'trust, but verify'. We trust you, of course. But what of your source? We would never wish to see you cheated, but alas, I know too well that sin which lives in the human heart... If anything, I believe your only weakness is being too kind a spirit, too generous a benefactor.""",bffi_mpBuyerHub3OptE3:Continue,
BFFImpBuyerHub3OptE3,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_mpBuyerHub3OptE3,"$buyerArgsMade++
FireAll BFFImpBuyerHub3Opts","Menes begins to nod, especially as Bornanew hits the last part of his 'explanation'.

""Yes,"" he exhales, ""I suppose you're right. I am, if anything, too giving. This was so true on Kazeron, where the resentful and dishonest sought to tear me down and entrap me in one scandal after another.""

""Out here, the social environment is more rarified, more, dare I say it? Honest. Even if it is a hopeless backwater, I do try to illuminate the locals with the light of Kazeronian culture...""",,
BFFImpBuyerHub3Sum4,BFFImpBuyerHub3Opts,$buyerArgsMade == 3,"$option = bffi_buyerSumOut 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","""Well, I suppose that does it!"" Menes claps his hands together.",,
BFFImpBuyerHub3Sum4out,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_buyerSumOut,,,"bffi_buyerSumOut2:""It does?""",
BFFImpBuyerHub3Sum4out2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_buyerSumOut2,,"""Certainly! I'll have my secretary make the arrangements. But first - a toast to the start of what I am sure will be a bountiful partnership! Back to the party!""

""Even you,"" he slaps a hand on Bornanew's shoulder, pulling him along, ""Surely you know how to celebrate a deal, my dour unbeliever? Perhaps not, so I'll show you!""",bffi_buyerOutro1:Continue,
BFFImpBuyerOutro1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_buyerOutro1,"HideSecondPerson
EndConversation DO_NOT_FIRE
BeginConversation bornanew","You and Bornanew are hauled back into the party, and the small crowd regaled with insinuations about a 'large purchase' by an unnamed 'wealthy spacer captain'.

Menes grows less discreet, winking and nudging with each retelling - and with each additional round of drinks. His dutiful entourage joins in to toast a 'new business deal' and theorize about extensions to Menes' complex.

You can see the skinny man, Ulmus Pond, watching you. He has a particularly manic, piercing laugh.

It is some time before you are able to get a quiet word in with $global.jethroName.","bffi_buyerOutro2a:""What's your read on Pond?""
bffi_buyerOutro2b:""$global.jethroName. $global.jethroName, can you finish my drink? I can't.""",
BFFImpBuyerOutro2a,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_buyerOutro2a,"$global.bffi_jethroCalledOutPond = true
$global.bffi_jethroCalledOutPondEarly = true","""He's a Pather agent,"" Bornanew says as if it were the most obvious thing in the world. He meets your look.

""We spoke briefly,"" he explains. ""The circumstantial evidence is convincing enough, but it was his heretical understanding of theology which I found truly damning.""

""I propose we retire from this, ah, celebration as soon as we can with the glove. Then investigate Pond.""",bffi_buyerOutro3b:Continue,
BFFImpBuyerOutro2b,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_buyerOutro2b,,"""Um,"" Bornanew shifts uncomfortably.

""I... Yes, I can take that for you, captain."" He carefully takes your drink from you without spilling, and then gently places it on a protruding piece of architecture.

""Did you bring any anti-inebriants? Perhaps we should get you back to your flagship. Here, just take my arm...""",bffi_buyerOutro3b:Continue,
BFFImpBuyerOutro3b,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_buyerOutro3a,EndConversation DO_NOT_FIRE,"* * *

It is a feat of diplomacy that you manage to extract yourself and Bornanew as quickly as you are able.

A faked containment failure alert from your chief engineer merely opens the door. Passing through requires shaking everyone's hand, exchanging pleasant words, and going through the motions of good-byes several times over - then each time the ritual is interrupted by some tangent or anecdote from Menes, he ensures that it is begun against from the start.

At last you find yourself back in your shuttle, a half-full glass still in your hand.",bffi_partyOutro1:Continue,
BFFImpBuyerOutro3a,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_buyerOutro3b,EndConversation DO_NOT_FIRE,"* * *

It is a feat of diplomacy that Bornanew manages to extract you as quickly as he does.

You have little difficulty playing up a state of stumbling drunkenness as Bornanew makes excuses, explaining that he will ""pray for the captain's intemperance"", much to the amusement of Menes' guests.

It is not your most dignified moment, but it ensures you can avoid the ritual of shaking everyone's hand, exchanging pleasant words, and going through the motions of good-byes.",bffi_partyOutro1:Continue,
,,,,,,
# BFFI Menes party Horus route,,,,,,
BFFIapHorusStartOption,PopulateOptions,"$market.id == olinadu
$menuState == main
$global.bffi_horusToParty
Call $global.bffi_ref updateData
$bffi_stage == ATTEND_A_PARTY",,,2:bffi_apHorus0:Shuttle down with Horus Yaribay to Menes' compound.,
BFFIapHorus0,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_apHorus0,ShowLargePlanet,"Horus transfers to your $shipOrFleet in orbit, greeting you and Bornanew tersely then making little in the way of conversation.

Menes' invitation provides you with a flight path and Demarch-level traffic control override codes. Horus would certainly receive similar treatment had he declared his presence openly.

As it is, it's probably a violation of Persean League ethical guidelines for you to be using these to attend a personal party, but from what you can overhear of the pilot's comms, the locals have a casual attitude toward the arrangement.",bffi_apHorus1:Continue,
BFFIapHorus1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_apHorus1,,"Menes Yaribay's compound is a scrubbed-looking slab of trendy architecture set on a bluff overlooking Olinadu's primary habitation cluster.

A smattering of outbuildings and hangars, attached by fat trunks of conduit and glowing walktubes, sprawl across the less-fashionable view-angles of the compound toward the refineries and holding tanks of the planet's industrial center.",bffi_apHorus2:Continue,
BFFIapHorus2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_apHorus2,,"One set of hangar bay doors dutifully open, and your shuttle descends through the glowing atmo-field. Such gadgetry is an ostentatious addition to a personal residence, but it avoids the bother of visitors (and their shuttles) having to undergo pressure-cycling.

An enthusiastic Menes is already approaching your shuttle's access ramp as it sets itself down and signals the all-clear.

Horus Yaribay puts out his hand in a 'you first' gesture.",bffi_apHorus3:Meet Menes Yaribay,
BFFIapHorus3,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_apHorus3,BeginConversation menes_yaribay,"""Captain $playerName - with your Knight of Ludd! Let me welcome you both to my humble...""

As Menes sees Horus step off the shuttle his face contorts through a fascinating sequence of expressions before settling into an alarmed rictus of welcome.

""C-cousin Horus. What an unexpected surprise!""

Menes' eyes, watery with a minor aspect of terror, dart to yours then away before the accusation fully solidifies.",bffi_apHorus4:Continue,
BFFIapHorus4,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_apHorus4,"ShowSecondPerson horus_yaribay
ShowThirdPerson bornanew","Horus' smile in return is cool as he steps forward to the offered hands with only one of his own. ""Menes. Where has the last cycle gone? It feels as though your inaugural flight to Olinadu was just yesterday.""

Menes manages to respond with an obliging laugh.

Bornanew, quite forgotten, follows you and the Yaribays.",bffi_apHorus5:Continue,
BFFIapHorus5,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_apHorus5,,"Menes leads your party past gilded statues guarding the portal to the main complex; the forms are evocative of splashes of molten gold frozen by happenstance into sensual humanoid figures.

You watch as Horus, lean and intense as some small predator, endures the patter from Menes, a man of more generous form and character. Menes plays down the 'frontier quality' of renovations, the poor selection of artworks, the difficulty of accessing the best artists and engineering firms to contribute to his home in 'all but exile'.

Occasionally a robotic or human servitor appears to offer drinks or nibbles, and you've a growing feeling that Menes has picked up a glass from one only to place it back on the tray of another without ever taking a sip.

A fresh glass in hand, Menes tentatively leads Horus into what can only be his prize entertaining space.",bffi_apHorus6:Follow,
BFFIapHorus6,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_apHorus6,,"The space is at once cavernous and intimate; the sightlines and carved, wrought, or woven details calculated to replicate a feeling of cozy warmth like the den of some thoughtful patron of art, history, and literature.

A double handful of well-dressed remoras mill about, interrupting their conversations to turn as Menes enters. They look to be a collection of industrialists, financiers, distant gens-relatives, and at least one officer from atop the local military detachment who appears a little worse for his drink.",bffi_apHorus7:Continue,
BFFIapHorus7,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_apHorus7,"HideThirdPerson
ShowThirdPerson ulmus_pond","Most start to give a politic nod and wave of acknowledgement at Menes' entrance, but stop and stare as they recognize Horus at his side. Few eyes linger on you and Bornanew, who steps apart as though he were a mere assistant or servitor.

One skinny man in a finely embroidered suit is not put off by Horus' entrance, and rushes to greet your party, eyes agog mostly at the gens patriarch, but sparing a glance at least for the newest additions to Menes' collection.",bffi_apHorus8:Continue,
BFFIapHorus8,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_apHorus8,,"He nearly trips over himself to speak. ""The great Horus Yaribay! Your reputation precedes you, if half of what-""

Horus holds up a hand, silencing the man, and turns aside. ""Menes, what is this?""

""Ha- ha, ah, this is Ulmus Pond,"" Menes replies quickly, his drinkless off-hand waving to shoo Pond away. ""Ulmus, not now. Perhaps see that Captain $playerLastName's Luddic friend here has a fresh drink? Thank-you.""

""Now, cousin Horus, I must offer a thousand apologies."" Menes himself turns, also cutting Pond out of the conversation. ""Had you signalled ahead we could have arranged for a proper reception...""",bffi_apHorus9:Watch the fallout,
BFFIapHorus9,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_apHorus9,"AdjustRepPerson ulmus_pond SUSPICIOUS -1
HideThirdPerson
$option = bffi_apHorus9b 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","""Never mind that,"" Horus says, looking around with a displeased curl to his lip. His gaze slips over Pond like he's nothing.

Ulmus Pond, for his part, hides the evil look that crossed his face in that moment to slink after Bornanew.",bffi_apHorus10:Continue,
BFFIapHorus9b,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_apHorus9b,,"Horus snaps his fingers, summoning a tray, and selects something effervescent. He takes a slow sip, not allowing his expression to display any sort of pleasure in the act. It seems to him more like a necessary palate-cleanser.

""Show it to me,"" he says to Menes. An order.",bffi_apHorus10:Continue,
BFFIapHorus10,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_apHorus10,,"""Captain $playerLastName shall attend,"" Horus adds quietly. ""So that we might fully resolve this matter.""

""Of course, cousin, of course!"" Menes, sweating, puts on a fragile grin in order to distribute reassuring nods to his extended entourage.

Menes leads you and Horus into his inner sanctum, flashing a grimace as he operates a series of obtrusive and, to your eyes, largely ornamental biometric checks.",bffi_apHorus11:Follow,
BFFIapHorus11,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_apHorus11,,"The air cools by a degree, perhaps two, the armored mass of the walls felt as a dullness through your feet. The subdued lighting, drapery, and framing of the space suggest the interior of a bank vault or a shrine, though not to the praise of any Luddic virtue.

Quite the contrary, depending on one's outlook.",bffi_apHorus12:Continue,
BFFIapHorus12,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_apHorus12,,"On a pedestal of carved wood, in a spot of light like holy revelation, a single glove is upthrust. Its fingers appear frozen in the midst of beginning to curl back toward a relaxed state after giving you a little wave.

After an appropriate pause, Menes speaks up, hopeful. ""What do you think, cousin?""",bffi_apHorus13:Continue,
BFFIapHorus13,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_apHorus13,,"""What's this supposed to be,"" says Horus, deadpan.

Menes clears his throat, then begins in a low, dramatic voice, ""The glove worn by Ludd when stepping upon the sacred Earth of Gilead. Ludd removed the glove and kissed the ground, according to the Luddic's religion.""","bffi_apHorus14:""And it's almost certainly a fake.""",
BFFIapHorus14,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_apHorus14,,"Menes looks shocked.

Horus gives you a look of his own. ""Of course it is,"" he says. ""And here I thought only a Luddie would be foolish enough to believe in this sort of thing.""

""Cousin!"" Menes exclaims, appalled.

""Do not 'cousin' me!"" Horus shouts, now, after an icy restraint held for so long.

""Remember how I saved you last time? The promises you made? And here, you've wasted stars-know how many credits on more nonsense, a bomb waiting to explode under the gens!""","bffi_apHorus15:Keep your mouth shut, for now",
BFFIapHorus15,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_apHorus15,,"""What would Reynard Hannan do if he knew what you were up to here, do you think?""

Menes shakes his head, speechless.

""He would loose the Church on us! And their bloody-minded Pathers! Think, think for once, 'cousin'."" Horus spits the word poisonously. ""Think of anyone in the Sector aside from yourself. Think of your gens!""

""The Chu- Path?"" Menes sputters pathetically. ""If Captain $playerLastName said it's a fake, it shouldn't be-""

""Oh, so now it's a fake?"" Horus cuts him off. ""Enough! Here is what will happen.""",bffi_apHorus16:Continue,
BFFIapHorus16,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_apHorus16,,"""Captain $playerLastName and $playerHisOrHer pet Knight of Ludd shall take possession of the damnable trinket. Immediately. As a sign of good faith to our Luddic 'friends' in the Church of Galactic Redemption.""

He gives you a look, ""See that they appreciate what I've done for them.""

Back to Menes. ""From now on I am taking personal control of your accounts. No frivolities without approval from my office.""

Menes begins to make a sound of objection but is cut off as Horus raises a single finger. A Reaper torpedo, armed and ready to launch into the unshielded breach.

""You and I,"" Horus says, ""Shall continue our conversation in private."" He doesn't turn to you again. ""Captain, if you would kindly?""",bffi_apHorus17:Take the glove,
BFFIapHorus17,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_apHorus17,,"Despite knowing what it is - or, rather, isn't - it feels almost like sacrilege to simply reach over to touch this object of such presumed expense and such evident disgrace. A vessel assigned such power and import, faith and violence, despite its reified deceit.

It is the glowing prize at the center of this temple, this shrine to the ego of Menes Yaribay bought with the lucre of the Kazeronian empire, fueled by faith and blood from over two hundred cycles since someone who took the name Ludd did something, probably, half-remembered then gilded in glorious myth on a planet named Gilead.","bffi_apHorus19:Just take the glove already
bffi_apHorus18:Hesitate",
BFFIapHorus18,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_apHorus18,,The quiet of the air circulation looms. Horus clears his throat.,bffi_apHorus19:Take the glove,
BFFIapHorus19,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_apHorus19,"AddTextSmall ""Acquired the false relic"" highlight
$player.bffi_betrayedMenesToHorus = true","As you touch it, a piercing alarm shatters the stillness of the treasury. Menes' hand slaps his other wrist with surprising speed. He raises it to his mouth to mumble a stand-down order to his security.

The alarm stops, leaving a painful echo in your ears.","bffi_apHorus20a:Tuck the glove into a pocket
bffi_apHorus20b:Carry it openly back to the party",
BFFIapHorus20a,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_apHorus20a,"EndConversation DO_NOT_FIRE
HideSecondPerson
HideVisual
AdjustRepPerson horus_yaribay COOPERATIVE 10
AdjustRepPerson menes_yaribay VENGEFUL -30","The cousins of Gens Yaribay watch you leave.

Horus' eyes are black. Menes's are red with betrayal.",bffi_apHorus21:Make your way back to the party to find Bornanew and leave,
BFFIapHorus20b,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_apHorus20b,"EndConversation DO_NOT_FIRE
HideSecondPerson
HideVisual
$player.bffi_carriedGloveOpenly = true
AdjustRepPerson horus_yaribay COOPERATIVE 10
AdjustRepPerson menes_yaribay VENGEFUL -30","The cousins of Gens Yaribay watch you leave.

Horus' eyes are cool, unblinking. Menes' are red with betrayal.",bffi_apHorus21:Make your way back to the party to find Bornanew,
BFFIapHorus21a,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_apHorus21,"BeginConversation bornanew
ShowSecondPerson ulmus_pond","Everyone turns and the conversation goes silent as you return to the main room. Alone.

You spot Bornanew, cornered by the man Ulmus Pond whose voice rings out for two words over-loudly as he realizes the fact of your entrance a moment later than the others.

His eyes are huge and bulging, like a fish.","bffi_apHorus22:""Hello $global.jethroName. I think we should go now.""",
BFFIapHorus21b,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_apHorus21
$player.bffi_carriedGloveOpenly","BeginConversation bornanew
ShowSecondPerson ulmus_pond","Everyone turns to stare at you as the conversation goes silent the instant you return to the main room. Alone.

You spot Bornanew, cornered by the man Ulmus Pond whose voice rings out for two words over-loudly because he realized the fact of your entrance a moment later than everyone else. His eyes are huge and bulging, like a fish.

They seem to widen even more as Pond sees that you are simply holding Menes' prize relic. Bornanew, even, struggles to maintain his composure as he realizes what you have in your hands.","bffi_apHorus22:""Hello $global.jethroName. I think we should go now.""",
BFFIapHorus22,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_apHorus22,HideSecondPerson,"Pond gapes, enhancing the piscine effect.

Bornanew places an untouched drink of something fizzy and golden into Pond's hand, then walks with you back toward the shuttle bay.

""I presume you have... it?"" he asks quietly, eyes forward.","bffi_apHorus23b:""Yes.""
bffi_apHorus23e:""Yup. Have a look for yourself."" (give him the glove)
bffi_apHorus23c:""I do. Did you see their faces, $global.jethroName?""",
BFFIapHorus22b,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_apHorus22
$player.bffi_carriedGloveOpenly",HideSecondPerson,"Pond gapes at you, furthering the piscine effect.

Bornanew places an untouched drink of something fizzy and golden into Pond's hand, then walks with you back to the shuttle bay.

""I think, perhaps,"" he says quietly, eyes forward, ""that you should have put the glove somewhere out of sight.""","bffi_apHorus23a:""Here, you take it.""
bffi_apHorus23b:""Perhaps you're right.""
bffi_apHorus23c:""Maybe. But did you see their faces, $global.jethroName?""",
BFFIapHorus23a,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_apHorus23a,$gaveGloveToBonranew = true 0,"He accepts the glove, a little surprised, quickly placing it within some hidden pocket of his robes.",bffi_partyOutro1:Continue,
BFFIapHorus23b,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_apHorus23b,,"He simply nods, placing his hands together. He doesn't do anything more, but you swear he's praying.",bffi_partyOutro1:Continue,
BFFIapHorus23c,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_apHorus23c,$player.ethosCocky++,"""I did,"" he says ruefully.",bffi_partyOutro1:Continue,
BFFIapHorus23e,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_apHorus23e,,"He accepts the glove, taking only a split second to suppress his look of shock. Bornanew quickly disappears the glove to some hidden pocket of his robes.

""I think, perhaps,"" he says in a whisper, ""that should have remained hidden.""","bffi_apHorus23b:""Perhaps you're right.""
bffi_apHorus23g:""Don't worry. Menes is going to be on his best good behavior from here on out.""",
BFFIapHorus23g,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_apHorus23g,$player.ethosCocky++,Bornanew spares you a single rueful look.,bffi_partyOutro1:Continue,
,,,,,,
# BFFI Menes party Raid,,,,,,
BFFImpRaidStart,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_mpEnterVault
$global.bffi_intendToRaid ",,"On a pedestal of carved wood, in a spot of light like holy revelation, a single glove is upthrust. Its fingers appear frozen in the midst of just starting to curl back toward a relaxed state after giving you a little wave.",bffi_mpRaid0:Continue,
BFFImpRaid0,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_mpRaid0,,"""Do you know what this is?"" Menes whispers to you. 

""It looks like a glove, demarch,"" Bornanew answers in feigned misunderstanding, stepping forward.",bffi_mpRaid1:Continue,
BFFImpRaid1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_mpRaid1,,"""Not any glove,"" Menes says with more than a hint of vexation.

He begins again in a reverent whisper, ""The glove worn by Ludd upon stepping upon the sacred Earth of Gilead. Ludd removed the glove and kissed the ground, according to the Luddic religion. Isn't that right, sir Knight? And this... is it.""

Bornanew looks at you, his eyebrows rising. ""Could it be?"" he asks, allowing some melodrama to enter his voice.","bffi_mpRaid2:""I'm impressed, Menes. A relic from a pivotal moment of the Sector's history!""
bffi_mpCallRaid:Call in the raid",
BFFImpRaid2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_mpRaid2,,"""Precisely my reaction upon first hearing word of this unique artifact!"" Menes beams, more than a little pleased that someone appreciates his trinket.

""Setting aside its purely religious significance,"" he gives a glance at Bornanew, ""it represents a, a heralding of the changing tides of history! The ebbing influence of the Domain-era megacorporations, the rising of what some call - not my words of course, sir Knight - an atavistic populism. Truly, it is this small piece of the vastness of the story of Humanity which called to me when it was first described to me...""

Menes seems prepared to continue this for quite some time.",bffi_mpCallRaid:Call in the raid,
BFFIraidGoBackOverride,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == mktRaidGoBack
$global.BFFIcommittedToRaid score:1000","$option = bffi_mpCallRaid 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected",Menes is blathering on about something or other while Bornanew pretends to listen.,,
#BFFIraidGoBackOverride,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == mktGoBack
$global.BFFIcommittedToRaid score:1000","$option = bffi_mpCallRaid 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected",Menes is blathering on about something or other while Bornanew pretends to listen.,,
BFFImpBuyerCallRaid,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_mpBuyerCallRaid,"$player.bffiChangedFromBuyerToRaid = true
$option = bffi_mpCallRaid 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","This isn't working. It's a good thing you prepared a backup plan.

You'll simply call in a marine raid while keeping Menes distracted. You give a grim nod to Bornanew and with only a small pause he follows your lead, asking Menes an insightful question about another item in his collection.",,
BFFIpartyBeginRaid,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_mpCallRaid,"$global.BFFIcommittedToRaid = true 0
$raidDifficulty = 100 0
$raidGoBackTrigger = BFFIapRaidBackHub 0
$raidRestrictToTrigger = BFFIattendPartyRaidFinishedA 0
$raidContinueTrigger = BFFIattendPartyRaidFinishedB 0
AddRaidObjective genericIcon ""Take the relic from Menes' compound"" MEDIUM 3000 BFFIattendPartyRaidFinishedA true
ShowImageVisual raid_prepare
RemoveOption mktRaidGoBack","You glance at your comms. Everything has been planned ahead of time, and care taken to hide tactical teams among the general population of offworld crew taking a bit of shore-leave. Signal discipline has been unerring.

The coded response, hidden in routine status reports, shows all teams are prepped and ready to move.",mktRaidNonMarket:Continue,
BFFIattendPartyRaidFinishedA,BFFIattendPartyRaidFinishedA,,"$option = bffi_mpRaidOutro1 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","Menes is describing another of his expensive acquisitions when the lights cut out.

A moment passes in absolute darkness, the crushing weight of silence falling as the ventilation whirs to a stop. This is the terrible abyss of spacers' death; a reminder that you exist by the whim of machines caught in deadly vacuum, in a precarious balance of temperature and artificial atmosphere.

The subdued red emergency lighting strips flicker to life. Menes produces a nervous smile, ""I'm sure it's just, um, a glitch."" He mumbles something into his cuff, then gives it a confused shake.

Comms down. By the plan.",,
BFFIapRaidOutro1,DialogOptionSelected,"$global.BFFIcommittedToRaid
$market.bffi_attendAParty
$option == mktRaidResult",,"""It's probably- I'm certain- I, I,"" Menes stutters, ""The power will come back soon. Those rad-addled Olinadu contractors,"" he attempts a nervous laugh.

You feel the dull thuds, nearly subsonic, through the armored mass of the vault. Breaching charges for the first layer of defense. You know the big one will come soon, and where.

Menes is in a growing panic.","bffi_mpRaidOutro2:""Perhaps, Menes, we should take cover...""",
BFFIapRaidOutro2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_mpRaidOutro2,"HideSecondPerson
EndConversation DO_NOT_FIRE
HideVisual","When the marines finally breach the vault proper, it is with overwhelming force of sound and light. No unprotected human can withstand this assault on the senses; you are blinded, shocked, and rendered immobile. All you can do is cling to the kernel of self at the center of a storm of pain.

* * *

The return is slow, an awakening from a terrible and drugged sleep to emergency medical personnel and Menes' somewhat tardy security teams in their gleaming armor.

You and Bornanew leave the compound among the other victims. Bandaged, bruised, head aching, ears ringing.",bffi_mpRaidOutro3:Continue,
BFFIapRaidOutro3,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_mpRaidOutro3,"BeginConversation bornanew
AddTextSmall ""Extracted the fake relic from collection of Menes Yaribay"" highlight
$global.bffi_raidedOlinaduForGlove = true
unset $global.BFFIcommittedToRaid","Hours later, after a series of transfers to obscure your movements from the heightened official surveillance, you step back onto your own shuttle - and the attentions of your personal medical team.

A chime on your TriPad confirms that the operation was a success. A holo of the simple work-glove that human beings fought and died over rotates mockingly. 

""Evidence,"" Bornanew says, tired but alert. His eyes are alarmingly bloodshot. ""The seed of schism and war. Now whence did this come?""","bffi_mpRaidOutro4a:""I don't suppose we could ask Menes.""
bffi_mpRaidOutro4b:""What did you make of that Ulmus Pond?""",
BFFIapRaidOutro4a,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_mpRaidOutro4a,,"""No,"" he manages a smile for just a moment. ""I would suppose not.""

He looks back down at the holo.",bffi_mpRaidOutro5:Continue,
BFFIapRaidOutro4b,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_mpRaidOutro4b,$global.bffi_jethroCalledOutPond = true,"""A Pather agent,"" he says conclusively.

""We spoke briefly,"" he says. ""In the aftermath. He insisted the medical team check him. Wasn't hurt."" 

Bornanew takes a deep breath, wincing. ""But he slipped up. Heretical theology. Devil in the details. You can tell where one learned the Word, or, rather, a corruption of the Word, from the details.""

""He may be connected, but first we should ask the glove."" He looks back down at the holo.",bffi_mpRaidOutro5:Continue,
BFFIapRaidOutro5,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_mpRaidOutro5,"unset $global.bffi_gotPartyInvite
$global.bffi_talkToEngineer = true
Call $global.bffi_ref updateStage","""A nanoforge engineer could tell us much of this object,"" he says. ""Who made it. When, and where. By the truths found in the false glove, we may judge answers we receive from those we... ask."" His last word is muted by the shuttle's maneuverings.

""The Church's nanoforge is on Asher. Canaan system. The techs there will submit to the authority I bear. Our inquiry will be secret.""

He pauses, and looks away. ""So far as anything is, in the Church.""","bffi_mpRaidOutro6:""We should confirm our hard evidence before Menes puts the pieces together here.""",
BFFIapRaidOutro6,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_mpRaidOutro6,"EndConversation DO_NOT_FIRE
ShowLargePlanet","Bornanew nods agreement.

The shuttle approaches your flagship and prepares to dock.",bffi_mpRaidOutro7:Continue,"# TODO: have some mention of local security wanting you to stick around while the investigation is underway

# ........ and you nope out"
BFFIapRaidOutro7,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_mpRaidOutro7,,"Your comms officer intercepts you on the way to the medbay looking determined but apologetic.

""$PlayerSirOrMadam. The local security authority has issued a blanket order for all fleets to stay in orbit pending an investigation into an, ah, attack against the demarch of Olinadu.""","bffi_mpRaidOutro8:""We're not registered with traffic control, correct?""",
BFFIapRaidOutro8,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_mpRaidOutro8,,"""Affirmative, $playerSirOrMadam,"" they reply. ""However we can assume that the present higher state of alert will detect the $shipOrFleet's de-orbit burn.""","bffi_mpRaidOutro9:""Then we'd better go fast when we go.""",
BFFIapRaidOutro9,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_mpRaidOutro9,"$player.bffi_postMenesParty = true
$player.bffi_raidedForRelic = true
IncreaseSmugglingSuspicion 2","""$PlayerSirOrMadam."" They salute and step back so the med tech can finish waving a scanner - the high-pitched hum just inside your hearing - in search of broken bones. $global.jethroName undergoes a similar procedure in the next bay.

Before the hour you are discharged with a smart stimpack strapped to your side, under your uniform jacket, to control the pain and keep you alert.

You're not out yet. You can easily see that the local authorities don't discover Menes' trinket if your $shipOrFleet is searched, but that search would waste valuable time and disrupt operations.",defaultLeave:Break orbit,
