Call $global.bffi_ref updateData
$bffi_stage == TALK_TO_ENGINEER",,,3:bffi_talkToEngineer0:Use Bornanew's authority to meet with a nanoforge engineer ,
BFFItalkToEngineer0,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_talkToEngineer0,,"Bornanew assists your comms officer in navigating through various levels of Church bureaucracy.

Before long, you have the senior nanoforge engineer of Asher on a comms-link.",bffi_talkToEngineer1:Continue,
BFFItalkToEngineer1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_talkToEngineer1,"BeginConversation nanoforge_engineer
$player.metTanaica = true","""Yes, hello? Uh, good day? I was told there was an investigation."" 

She seems to examine you through the link. ""You don't look much like a Knight of Ludd.""","bffi_talkToEngineer2:""I need an object analyzed. Very closely.""",
BFFItalkToEngineer2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_talkToEngineer2,,"""I see."" $PersonName takes a moment more to examine you, humming to herself.

""Forensic material analysis. Skilled work."" $HeOrShe frowns. ""It won't be cheap.""

She looks at some other display and starts tapping at an input. ""You'll have to bring the sample down, of course.""",bffi_talkToEngShuttle:Shuttle to the engineer's laboratory,
BFFItalkToEngShuttle,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_talkToEngShuttle,"EndConversation DO_NOT_FIRE
ShowLargePlanet","Bornanew's authority - that of the Archcurate Sophronia Jaspis, in truth - is as good with the local traffic authority as it is with the Manufactoria Guild bureaucrats.

Your shuttle descends into the atmosphere of Asher. The view shades toward a warm, murky gray as you descend through the stratospheric fines perpetually refreshed by towering dust storms. The display blots out entirely and switches to a false-rendering as you enter the lower atmosphere.

There is no hazard; the storms are impressive in scale but low in mass due to the deathly thin atmosphere.",bffi_talkToEngineer4:Continue,
BFFItalkToEngineer4,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_talkToEngineer4,"BeginConversation nanoforge_engineer
ShowSecondPerson bornanew
$player.met","Senior Engineer Tanaica places the glove and its containment vessel onto a shelf which retracts into the towering white casing of the analysis suite. Transparent panes, probably diamond-matrix, reveal arcane inner workings.

She hits a command to evacuate the atmo from the sample slot, and sets a manipulator to extract the glove and place it on the scanning bed. All of this she performs with a casual ease born of practice. She speaks as she taps away at the control interface.

""If it came from a high-quality nanoforge like what the Heggies or League's got, this might not tell us much."" 

Some kind of protective barrier shunts down, hiding the glove from view. A holo of the glove emerges from a display unit, gaining resolution until a doppelganger rotates in the air before you.",bffi_talkToEngineer5:Continue,
BFFItalkToEngineer5,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_talkToEngineer5,,"""Hm. Good output, this. But I'm thinking not good-perfect. Ludd...ics,"" her eyes dart at Bornanew, ""No offense, but they don't go in for training much native talent. S'why you lot pay me.""

""Anyway, when you get into really delicate products, your forge quality starts to matter. A work-rated vac-glove though?"" She rolls her eyes. ""This better be good.""

The analysis suite is making some kind of humming sound, and there's a clunk. The engineer doesn't react, so neither do you. Her display erupts with numbers and icons, then something she does pulls a cutaway from the holo-glove, which scales as the rest of it disappears. 

Another segmentation of scale iterates, then another.",bffi_talkToEngineer6:Watch closely,
BFFItalkToEngineer6,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_talkToEngineer6,,"""We can see signs of what we call 'drift' here,"" she says. A colored indicator ring flashes around an orderly pattern of small-scale structures deep within the glove, the representation of individual atoms, perhaps, just visible like the grain of sandstone.

""These defects are unique to the faults in an individual nanoforge. More or less."" 

""Like a fingerprint,"" Bornanew says.

""No."" The engineer shrugs. ""But sure, if you like.""","bffi_talkToEngineer7:""What's this tell us?""",
BFFItalkToEngineer7,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_talkToEngineer7,,"""Someone's been naughty,"" she says, sounding more delighted than upset. ""The glove is new, but the model is old. A closed-source pre-Collapse template. There are fabrication-rights codes embedded in its structure.""

With a tap, another colored indicator ring flashes on a sheared-square section of material containing a complex pattern. ""Tells the forge not to make unauthorized copies.""

""Closed products from the Domain-era tend to be far higher quality than forges running post-Collapse hacks."" She smiles, ""This isn't that, but it's close. Tells us two things.""","bffi_talkToEngineer8:""Which are?""",
BFFItalkToEngineer8,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_talkToEngineer8,,"""One, this was made by an industrial-grade Domain-era forge. Heavy industry stuff. Bit of a waste to use it to make a glove,"" she glances at you, ""If you ask me.""

""Two, either this forge is loaded with valid fabrication rights and it's damaged, or it's been hacked to bypass the embedded copy protections. And it's damaged. I mean, stars and ruin, look at this mess,"" she zooms in on the 'drift' patterns while making a disgusted look.

$global.jethroName speaks up now, ""Three, we're dealing with a sophisticated forgery operation.""

The engineer shoots a look back at him, ""Neat.""","bffi_talkToEngineer9:""What forge made this? Where's it from?""",
BFFItalkToEngineer9,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_talkToEngineer9,,"""Right,"" she manipulates the interface again.

The drift-pattern from the glove remains locked, and she brings up similar - but distinct - examples of patterns in an expanding grid. Small labels show a string of glyphs, most of which contain the names of industrial combines, shipyards, and polities known to you. Some you recognize as dating to the Collapse. Others are unfamiliar.

""This is the drift library we've got here on Asher. Useful stuff, but other factions got better.""","bffi_talkToEngineer10:""So you can match the 'drift' to the forge.""",
BFFItalkToEngineer10,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_talkToEngineer10,,"""Exactly,"" she's pleased that you put it together. ""Got bad news though, cap. Your glove doesn't match anything in this library.""","bffi_talkToEngineer11a:""Can drift be obscured, faked?""
bffi_talkToEngineer11b:""So it's not a known forge.""",
BFFItalkToEngineer11a,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_talkToEngineer11a,"$didFakeAsk = true 0
FireBest BFFItalkToEngineerAskCheck","""Could be,"" she admits. ""Takes a clever setup and a talented operator though. If this is fake drift, then it goes real high up. Don't know who'd be capable of it that'd waste that kind of effort on a glove.""",,
BFFItalkToEngineer11b,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_talkToEngineer11b,"$didKnownAsk = true 0
FireBest BFFItalkToEngineerAskCheck","""Maybe, maybe not,"" she says.

""The Church doesn't put much into material analysis. What you'd do, ideally, is collect statistically significant samples, run scans on every new product that shows up, put anything interesting through a detailed scan like this, build a library. It's not cheap,"" she says wistfully.

""But here they're mostly interested in making sure their hyperdrives work to min-spec. The Church of No-fun."" She looks at Bornanew, ""Sorry.""

He nods, untroubled.",,
BFFItalkToEngineer11c,BFFItalkToEngineerAskCheck,"!$didFakeAsk
$didKnownAsk ",,,"bffi_talkToEngineer11a:""Can drift be obscured, faked?""",
BFFItalkToEngineer11d,BFFItalkToEngineerAskCheck,"$didFakeAsk
!$didKnownAsk ",,,"bffi_talkToEngineer11b:""So it's not a known forge.""",
BFFItalkToEngineer11e,BFFItalkToEngineerAskCheck,"$didFakeAsk
$didKnownAsk ",,,"bffi_talkToEngineer12:""Anything else?""",
BFFItalkToEngineer12,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_talkToEngineer12,"SetTextHighlights 10,000
FireAll BFFItalkToEngineer12opts","""That's all I got, captain,"" she says, reversing the specimen insertion procedure and returning your containment vessel. ""Good mystery. Hope it doesn't get you shot.""

She hands the vessel to Bornanew, then claps her hands together. ""That'll be 10,000 credits.""",,
BFFItalkToEngineer12optDev1,BFFItalkToEngineer12opts,"$global.isDevMode
$player.ethosCynical < 2",SetOptionColor BFFI_talkToEngineer12optDev1sel gray,,BFFI_talkToEngineer12optDev1sel:DEV set player.ethosCynical to 2,
