SetTooltip bffi_talkToEngineer13corruption ""It may be cynical, but she's got a clever hustle and it'd be a shame to spoil it.""",,,
BFFItalkToEngineer12optCheck2,BFFItalkToEngineer12optsCheck,$player.ethosMercenary > 1,"SetEnabled bffi_talkToEngineer13corruption false
SetTooltip bffi_talkToEngineer13corruption ""You can easily understand that she's just trying to make some extra money. You're a mercenary too, as it serves you, and it'd be a shame to spoil a good hustle.""",,,
BFFItalkToEngineer13a,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_talkToEngineer13a,"$saidUh = true 0
FireAll BFFItalkToEngineer12opts","She looks between you and Bornanew.

""Didn't you tell your captain about the fee?"" She asks.

You'd swear, Bornanew is almost blushing.",,
BFFItalkToEngineer13b,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_talkToEngineer13b,AddCredits -10000,"You transfer the credits to Senior Engineer Tanaica's accounts while $global.jethroName holds the vessel.

Presumably she'll forward payment for lab expenses to the Church-approved Manufactoria Guild.",bffi_postEngJethroTalk1:Continue,
BFFItalkToEngineer13bMerc,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_talkToEngineer13b
$player.ethosMercenary > 2",AddCredits -10000,"You transfer the credits to Senior Engineer Tanaica's accounts while $global.jethroName holds the vessel.

Presumably she'll forward payment for lab expenses to the Church-approved Manufactoria Guild. Or not.",bffi_postEngJethroTalk1:Continue,
BFFItalkToEngineer13corruption,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_talkToEngineer13corruption,AdjustRepActivePerson SUSPICIOUS -1,"His neutral expression flickers.

""I... yes, the captain is correct. You are paid to serve the Church, and this,"" he hefts the ersatz reliquary, ""is business of the Church.""

""Right you are,"" says Senior Engineer Tanaica through a tight smile. ""Good day, captain.""

Her eyes flick at Bornanew. ""Novice.""",bffi_talkToEngineer13corruption2:Continue,
BFFItalkToEngineer13corruption2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_talkToEngineer13corruption2,"$player.ethosOrder++
EndConversation DO_NOT_FIRE
ShowLargePlanet","Bornanew's tone was righteous, but without heart. You suspect he was not going to make an issue of the 'payment' until you brought it up.

As you return to your shuttle he gives you a look- guilt?

""Such things are not uncommon even in the shadow of the Church,"" he says. ""And elsewhere. I'm sure you well know.""

Bornanew returns his attention to his datapad. He's making his 'thinking face'.""","bffi_postEngJethroTalk2:""Out with it, $global.jethroName.""",
BFFItalkToEngineer13c,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_talkToEngineer13c,,"He recovers quickly. ""I, of course,"" he awkwardly hands the ersatz reliquary to you then draws an off-brand datapad from his robes. Engineer $personLastName blinks at it.

""I can pay from the, uh, accounts of The Reverend Archcurate Sophronia Jaspis... here.""",bffi_postEngJethroTalk1:Continue,
BFFItpostEngJethroTalk1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_postEngJethroTalk1,"EndConversation DO_NOT_FIRE
ShowLargePlanet","You return to your shuttle. 

Bornanew's attention is uncharacteristically focused on his datapad. He's making his 'thinking face'.","bffi_postEngJethroTalk2:""Out with it, $global.jethroName.""",
BFFItpostEngJethroTalk2,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_postEngJethroTalk2
$global.bffi_jethroCalledOutPond",BeginConversation bornanew,"""Ulmus Pond,"" he says. Then looks up at you.

""That strange little man from Menes Yaribay's party. Obviously an agent for the Luddic Path. That the Path would have eyes and influence on Menes is no surprise. But if he's the one that supplied the glove...""

""We need to get to him,"" he says. ""Confront him. Compel him to talk.""","bffi_postEngJethroTalk3:""Guess we're going back to Olinadu.""",
BFFItpostEngJethroTalk2know,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_postEngJethroTalk2
!$global.bffi_jethroCalledOutPond",BeginConversation bornanew,"""Ulmus Pond,"" he says. Then looks up at you. ""He's a Pather agent,"" Bornanew says as if it were the most obvious thing in the world.

""We spoke briefly at Menes' party,"" he explains. ""The circumstantial evidence is convincing enough, but it was his heretical understanding of theology which I found truly damning.""

""We need to get to him,"" he says. ""Confront him. Compel him to talk.""","bffi_postEngJethroTalk3:""Guess we're going back to Olinadu.""",
BFFItpostEngJethroTalk3,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_postEngJethroTalk3,,"""Guess so,"" he replies. ""We may not wish to draw any attention from Menes, of course...""

The shuttle docks with your flagship.","bffi_postEngJethroTalk4:""I'll handle it. I can be very discreet.""",
BFFItpostEngJethroTalk3didRaid,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_postEngJethroTalk3
$player.bffi_raidedForRelic",,"""Guess so,"" he replies. ""But perhaps... Menes' might not be pleased to see us show up.""

The shuttle docks with your flagship.","bffi_postEngJethroTalk4:""I'll handle it. I can be very persuasive.""",
BFFItpostEngJethroTalk4,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_postEngJethroTalk4,"
unset $global.bffi_talkToEngineer
SetPersonHidden ulmus_pond false
$global.bffi_talkToUlmusPond = true
Call $global.bffi_ref updateStage
EndConversation",You step off the shuttle.,,
,,,,,,
# BFFI talk to Ulmus Pond,,# $bffi_stage == TALK_TO_ULMUS_POND,,,,
BFFIulmusPondGreeting,PickGreeting,"$id == ulmus_pond
Call $global.bffi_ref updateData
$bffi_stage == TALK_TO_ULMUS_POND",,"The comms signal hits a holding signal and waits. And waits. You have your comms officer take over to watch the link and make a few inquiries.

Within minutes, a comms request alert appears. It's Bornanew on an internal link.",bffi_ulmusPondNotHere:Open the comm link,
BFFIulmusPondNotHere,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusPondNotHere,BeginConversation bornanew,"""Captain,"" he says. ""I apologize for the interruption.""

""Ulmus Pond is not on Olinadu.""","bffi_ulmusPondNotHere2:""You're sure. How do you know this?""",
BFFIulmusPondNotHere2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusPondNotHere2,,"""The Knights have... sources,"" he says carefully. ""I am sworn not to reveal them.""","bffi_ulmusPondNotHere3:""Your oath. Of course.""",
BFFIulmusPondNotHere3,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusPondNotHere3,,"""Yes."" Bornanew clears his throat.

""The word is that he has fled to Chalcedon on a tramp freighter, a smuggler, known to move materiel for the Luddic Path.""","bffi_ulmusPondNotHere4a:""Does an innocent man run?""
bffi_ulmusPondNotHere4b:""Then we follow.""",
BFFIulmusPondNotHere4a,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusPondNotHere4a,"$option = bffi_ulmusPondNotHere4b 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","He turns his head. ""He might, if he had to. But I suspect that Ulmus is not an innocent man.""",,
BFFIulmusPondNotHere4b,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusPondNotHere4b,FireAll BFFIulmusNotHereOpts,"""I pray that if we move quickly, we can find him on Chalcedon.""",,
BFFIupNotHereConvOptA,BFFIulmusNotHereOpts,,,,"bffi_upNotHereSetCourse:""Nav, set a course.""",
BFFIupNotHereConvOptB,BFFIulmusNotHereOpts,!$saidAskRole,,,"bffi_upNotHereAskRole:""What's Ulmus Pond's role? What does finding him do for us?""",
BFFIupNotHereConvOptC,BFFIulmusNotHereOpts,!$saidSourcesB,,,"bffi_upNotHereSourcesB:""What if these are pirates, or a major faction misleading us?""",
BFFIupNotHereConvOptD,BFFIulmusNotHereOpts,!$saidSourcesA,,,"bffi_upNotHereSourcesA:""Before we act, let us speak of your Knights' 'sources'.""",
BFFIupNotHereConvOptE,BFFIulmusNotHereOpts,!$saidIntentions,,,"bffi_upNotHereIntentions:""Could your queries have revealed our intentions?""",
BFFIupNotHereWhatRole,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_upNotHereAskRole,"$saidAskRole = true 0
FireAll BFFIulmusNotHereOpts","""He would be - have been - well placed as a bridge for some element of the Luddic Path to influence Menes Yaribay. He would be the source of the relic.""",,
BFFIupNotHereSourcesA,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_upNotHereSourcesA,"$saidSourcesA = true 0
FireAll BFFIulmusNotHereOpts","""I cannot,"" he says. ""But I assure you they are as reliable as any heretic, guilty soul, or criminal."" His look softens, ""Do trust that I am not simply asking around a spacer bar for a lead.""

A moment, then he gives a nod, almost a bow. ""Um. I do not condemn your methods. Your directness has oft proven effectual.""",,
BFFIupNotHereSourcesB,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_upNotHereSourcesB,"$saidSourcesB = true 0
FireAll BFFIulmusNotHereOpts","""It could be either."" Bornanew folds his hands together. ""But we must look first where the light of truth shines brightest, dim though it may be, or known only by distinction against the shadow of deceit.""",,
BFFIupNotHereIntentions,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_upNotHereIntentions,"$saidIntentions = true 0
FireAll BFFIulmusNotHereOpts","""It is always possible."" Bornanew meets your eyes, steady. ""The Knights pursue heretics and criminals as routine, and my inquiries were worded to imply my interest lay not upon Ulmus Pond himself, nor the Menes situation. Though, of course, you and I are already known to be associated with both.""

""Expediency anticipates risk. I beg you trust my judgment in this matter.""",,
BFFIulmusPondNotHereOut,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_upNotHereSetCourse,"SetPersonHidden ulmus_pond true
Call $global.bffi_ref setCourseChalcedon
unset $global.bffi_talkToUlmusPond
$global.bffi_followUlmusPond = true
Call $global.bffi_ref updateStage","Nav responds instantly to your orders.

Bornanew's image flickers with compression-grain from his cheap datapad.

""I pray that Ulmus Pond's hasty flight has not unwittingly forewarned heretic militants...""","cutCommLink:""If we're quick, we won't need to pray."" (cut the link)",
,,,,,,
# BFFI go to Chalcedon and bully Ulmus Pond,,# $bffi_stage == GO_TO_CHALCEDON,,,,
BFFIulmusStartOption,PopulateOptions,"$market.bffi_followUlmusPond
$menuState == main
Call $global.bffi_ref updateData
$bffi_stage == GO_TO_CHALCEDON",$player.foundUlmusPondSafehouse = true,,3:bffi_ulmusPrestart1:Find where Ulmus Pond is hiding,
BFFIulmusPrestart1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusPrestart1,BeginConversation bornanew,"Chalcedon rotates in the primary display before you.

Bornanew is at your side, tapping at his off-brand datapad, looking for all the worlds like a toy in his large hands.

""My sources indicate that a man matching the description of Ulmus Pond is almost certainly in a safehouse... here.""

A highlighted point appears on the globe, some logistical center in the scablands trailing like a stain from the primary spaceport.",bffi_ulmusPrestart2:Continue,
BFFIulmusPrestart2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusPrestart2,,"Bornanew watches the point as the globe obligingly comes to a gentle stop. The highlighted section detaches from the globe, which collapses away, and spreads into a tactical overview.

""He acts like a man drowning, grasping for help without concern for his rescuers."" He turns from the globe toward you, ""In OPSEC terms, of course. He could have easily disappeared.""

A bitter smile appears, ""As once I did.""","bffi_ulmusPrestart3:""Tactical, prep a shuttle. Let's have a chat with Ulmus Pond.""",
BFFIulmusPrestart3,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusPrestart3,"ShowLargePlanet
SetTooltip bffi_ulmusPondYouBad ""Due to his criminal background, $global.jethroName must be familiar with the art of intimidation. He would perform the role well.""
SetTooltip bffi_ulmusPondMeBad ""In consideration of his criminal background, you don't want to put $global.jethroName back into playing a role he's worked so hard to leave behind.""","Bornanew has his notebook and cheap old datapad packed in a satchel made of what looks like leather. You've heard of the primitive process the Luddics are said to use to produce the material; the skin of an animal is stripped then stewed, somehow, with its own waste products. It sounded unbearably primitive when described. Anti-Luddic misinformation, perhaps, because you don't detect the smell of feces at all.

""How shall we approach this?"" Bornanew asks. ""Like in MuniSec dramas- one of us is friendly to the subject, the other hostile?""","bffi_ulmusPondMeBad:""I'll be the bad guy.""
bffi_ulmusPondYouBad:""You be the bad guy.""",
BFFIulmusPrestartBornGood,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusPondMeBad,"$player.ethosHumanitarian++
$player.toldBornanewHeIsGoodGuy = true
$option = bffi_ulmusPondLoadout1 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","Bornanew nods. Perhaps you're imagining it, but is that relief in the set of his eyes?",,
BFFIulmusPrestartBornBad,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusPondYouBad,"$global.bornanewBadBoy++
$player.ethosRuthless++
$player.toldBornanewHeIsBadGuy = true
$option = bffi_ulmusPondLoadout1 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","Bornanew nods. Perhaps you're imagining it, but you feel like a coldness comes into the set of his eyes.",,
BFFIulmusPrestartLoadout1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusPondLoadout1,"$option = bffi_ulmusPondLoadout2
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","Your personal security team has been briefed, and are dressed as a mix of common spacers, local techs, and Luddic laborers. Their arsenal is multitude and well-concealed.",,
BFFIulmusPrestartLoadout2a,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_ulmusPondLoadout2
#$player.sdtu_weaponPistol","$option = bffi_ulmusPondLoadout2done
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","Your own hand finds your trusty sidearm, a matte polycarbonate pistol. An ideal firearm for use in tight spaces, its mass rests securely in your holster.",,# default
BFFIulmusPrestartLoadout2b,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_ulmusPondLoadout2
$player.sdtu_weaponGrenade","$option = bffi_ulmusPondLoadout2done
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","You, of course, have your clutch of devilish little grenades built to resist milliradar detection. Fearful and unexpected, they trigger with a practiced twitch from your hand.",,
BFFIulmusPrestartLoadout2c,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_ulmusPondLoadout2
$player.sdtu_weaponKnife","$option = bffi_ulmusPondLoadout2done
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","And you have hidden a vicious ceramic vibroknife on your person. It is not a tool to be underestimated, for when deployed by surprise it can even disable light power-armored opponents.",,
BFFIulmusPrestartLoadout2d,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_ulmusPondLoadout2
$player.sdtu_weaponSpray","$option = bffi_ulmusPondLoadout2done
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","You are protected by a subtler weapon, a tiny capsule of spray-poison within your cuff. Hold your breath as it is deployed with a casual wave, and the target next to you will simply die as if of a massive, unexpected heart-attack.",,
BFFIulmusPrestartLoadout2e,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_ulmusPondLoadout2
$player.sdtu_weaponWire","$option = bffi_ulmusPondLoadout2done
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","You, of course, have a monomolecular wire hidden in a false fingertip, ready to deploy into an invisible cutting edge with but a short, sharp twist. It is a venerable weapon favored by assassins of a certain class.",,
BFFIulmusPrestartLoadout2f,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_ulmusPondLoadout2
$player.sdtu_weaponNone","$option = bffi_ulmusPondLoadout2done
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","You, of course, need trust nothing more than your limbs. Starship combat is mass and energy applied at scale; absurdly reduced to the scale of the human body, the mechanics applied are not completely dissimilar.",,
BFFIulmusPrestartLoadout2g,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_ulmusPondLoadout2
$player.sdtu_weaponSword","$option = bffi_ulmusPondLoadout2done
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","Your hand finds the hilt of your officers' sword at your side, the mass of a steel blade a comfort shared with warriors dating to the primitive conflicts of Old Earth.",,
BFFIulmusPrestartLoadout2done,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusPondLoadout2done,,,bffi_ulmusStart:Continue,
BFFIulmusStart,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusStart,"ShowPersonVisual
$option = bffi_ulmusStart2 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","You stand with Bornanew in an uncomfortably narrow alley. The sky above sends nasty rivulets of fluid down the conduits and moldy canopies that diffuse the light into a flattening murk.

Your security team is invisible, discreet in nearby alcoves and rooftops.

$global.jethroName runs his hands over a door, as if feeling under it's moisture-warped surface for a clue.",,
BFFIulmusStart2a,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_ulmusStart2
$player.toldBornanewHeIsBadGuy",,"""Ready, captain?"" he asks. ""Remember, you're the good guy.""","bffi_ulmusStart3:""I'm ready.""
bffi_ulmusStart3a:""You're sure he's here?""",
BFFIulmusStart2b,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_ulmusStart2
$player.toldBornanewHeIsGoodGuy",,"""Ready, captain?"" he asks. ""Remember, you're the bad guy.""","bffi_ulmusStart3:""Don't you forget it.""
bffi_ulmusStart3a:""You're sure he's here?""",
BFFIulmusStart3a,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusStart3a,"$option = bffi_ulmusStart3 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","""I am,"" he says.",,
BFFIulmusStart3,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusStart3,,"Bornanew takes a step back then slams a powerful leg into a worn spot, about waist-high. With a sharp crack, the entire door falls inward, crumbling hinges and locking mechanism still attached.",bffi_ulmusStart4:Follow,
BFFIulmusStart4,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusStart4,,"Bornanew charges inside. You follow his steps through an entryway, plastic rain cloaks mildewing, through a prefab kitchen and wash unit stained the yellow of old teeth. A sitting area, chair toppled. There's a muffled thump from above.

Bornanew glances at you, his eyes giving a bounce upwards. Ulmus Pond.",bffi_ulmusStart5:Find a way upstairs,
BFFIulmusStart5,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusStart5,ShowSecondPerson ulmus_pond,"A moment of frantic search reveals the narrow stairwell behind a loose wall-panel.

Bornanew pounds up the stairs, and you follow.

In his half-second lead, Bornanew has caught Ulmus Pond in a bearhug, Pond's skinny arms still grabbing at the loosened attachment-points of a sheet of translucent plastic which lies between him and the lightwell; escape. Pond loses his grip with a cry of despair as Bornanew pulls him away.

The window panel snaps back into place.",bffi_ulmusTalk0:Continue,
"# BFFI Ulmus
# Bornanew is Good cop",,,,,,
BFFIulmusTalkPcBad,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_ulmusTalk0
$player.toldBornanewHeIsGoodGuy",,"""Ulmus Pond,"" Bornanew roars with overbearing gusto, ""This is no season to be opening a window!""

""Sit, I insist, before you hurt yourself! We are doubly blessed to find you so well. You must understand our fear- no answer to comms, rumors of kidnappings... Menes has been worried sick about his very good friend.""

The bear-hug has turned into something like a side-grab as Bornanew sets Pond bodily onto the cot beside him. You're not sure if the creaking is from the cheap furniture or Pond' ribs.","bffi_ulmusTalkBad1a:""More than worried. He suspects you, Pond. We're going to get answers.""
bffi_ulmusTalkBad1b:""Easy $global.jethroName. Ulmus only had good intentions I'm sure.""",
BFFIulmusTalkPcBad1a,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusTalkBad1a,,"""A- answers?"" Pond's eyes go wider still as he gasps for breath. ""I, um, appreciate your concern but I'm fine, here. Nothing is the matter, truly!""

""Look at him, captain,"" Bornanew says. ""He's an innocent. He'd tell us straightaway if some ill-intentioned party were taking advantage of his good nature.""","bffi_ulmusTalkBad2a:""No, I think Ulmus is behind it. We should do an active scan on his brain.""
bffi_ulmusTalkBad2b:""Perhaps you're right, he does look pretty innocent.""",
BFFIulmusTalkPcBad2a,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusTalkBad2a,,"""Ulmus?"" Bornanew looks at you, shocked at the idea. 

""...'active' scan?"" Ulmus manages to squeak.

""The captain would never,"" insists Bornanew. ""You're a merchant, a middleman. You just wanted to help your friend Menes find a unique object for his collection. Isn't that right?"" He gives Ulmus another squeeze.

""Y-yes, that's right,"" Ulmus says, looking between you and Bornanew. ""I, uh, I set up connections. Deals. I help people!""","bffi_ulmusTalkBad3a:""So you admit you 'helped' Menes buy a fake relic from the Pathers!""",
BFFIulmusTalkPcBad1b,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusTalkBad1b,$messedUpOnce = true 0,"Bornanew tips his head, giving you a confused look. 

""The good captain here thought someone,"" he pauses to give you a consternated expression, ""-might be taking advantage of Menes. $PlayerHeOrShe wants to eliminate all suspects.""

""I, for one, insisted to Menes that you must be the victim of some terrible scheme, and that I would pray for you, and, better yet, as a Knight of Ludd carry out my sworn duty to protect the faithful and innocent alike.""

Bornanew gives Pond a squeeze to emphasize how safe he is, now.","bffi_ulmusTalkBad2a:""Ulmus is behind it. We should perform an active scan on his brain.""
bffi_ulmusTalkBad2b:""On second thought, I don't think Ulmus had anything to do with it.""",
BFFIulmusTalkPcBad2b,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusTalkBad2b,$messedUpOnce = true 0,"Bornanew tips his head, giving you a confused look.

""The captain here told me,"" he pauses to give you a consternated expression, ""-he thought you were working for Pathers, to sell Menes a fake relic to cause discord and make off with his credits. The captain told me $playerHeOrShe wanted to test an invasive brain-interfacer $playerHeOrShe found in some ruin on the fringe to discover the truth inside your head.""

Pond's eyes go wide at the mention of 'brain-interface'.

""I, for one,"" Bornanew says reassuringly, ""insisted that the plan was crude and unnecessary. Surely you're the victim of a terrible scheme...""","bffi_ulmusTalkBad3a:""Ah... yes, that's right. We really should try the brain-interfacer.""
bffi_ulmusTalkBad3b:""'Brain-interfacer'? What is this nonsense $global.jethroName?""",
BFFIulmusTalkPcBad2bmessedUp,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_ulmusTalkBad2b
$messedUpOnce","$option = bffi_ulmusTalkPcWrong1 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected",,,
BFFIulmusTalkPcBad3a,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusTalkBad3a,,"""I didn't know they were Pathers!"" Pond shouts.

Bornanew pretends shock at the notion, looking at Ulmus and shaking his head.

""Or that it was a fake! I swear, I'm a legitimate entrepreneur! I've been set up. I have enemies, Menes has enemies, they- they must have set me up!""","bffi_ulmusTalkBad4a:""Yet you ran. Right back to your Pather masters on Chalcedon.""",
BFFIulmusTalkPcBad3b,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusTalkBad3b,$messedUpOnce = true 0,"Bornanew tips his head, giving you a confused look.

""Now's not the time to play coy, captain. Your illegal brain-interfacer,"" he stresses the words, ""which you proposed could 'scientifically prove' Pond's connection to a Pather network with only 'minimal damage'.""

Pond looks rapidly between you and Bornanew, both scared and confused. ""Minimal da-"" he begins, then shifts course to avoid the subject entirely. ""I didn't know they were Pathers!"" he pleads.

""Or that it was a fake! I swear, I'm a legitimate entrepreneur. There's no need for brain-scans or, or- I've been set up! I have enemies, Menes has enemies, they- they must have set me up!""","bffi_ulmusTalkBad4a:""But you ran, Ulmus. Right back to your Pather masters here on Chalcedon.""",
BFFIulmusTalkPcBad3bmessedUp,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_ulmusTalkBad3b
$messedUpOnce","$option = bffi_ulmusTalkPcWrong1 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected",,,
BFFIulmusTalkPcBad4a,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusTalkBad4a,,"""I-I had no... you don't understand,"" Ulmus squirms.

Bornanew jumps in to direct Ulmus' narrative. ""He must have been threatened,"" he says. ""Blackmail! Of course. You help us find out who's really behind this! We'll make sure you're safe.""","bffi_ulmusTalkBad5a:""If, and only if, $global.jethroName, he helps us. Otherwise he goes to the Inquisitors.""",
BFFIulmusTalkPcBad5a,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusTalkBad5a,,"""Surely there is no need to bring them in it,"" Bornanew puts on a look of saintly compassion.

""I know in my heart that Ulmus wants to confess and be absolved of his sins, of his crimes. He wants to leave this terrible time behind him and live a good life.""

Pond's eyes go teary. ""Y-yes, yes. I'll confess! I'll do penance, I'll pray! I'll tell you whatever you need. By Ludd, I beg forgiveness!""",bffi_ulmusTalkBad6a:Continue,
BFFIulmusTalkPcBad6a,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusTalkBad6a,,"Pond sniffles.

""There was... a Walker of the Path. He asked me to talk to Menes, to, to, to make the offer. He said Menes couldn't resist an artifact of such quality. And- and I was to arrange transport. Then make it appear legitimate. Set the documents straight, make it look correct.""

Bornanew draws his cheap datapad from his satchel, the screen already set to a map of the greater Persean Sector.","bffi_ulmusTalkSedgeCheck:""Show him, Ulmus. It's us or the Inquisitors.""",
,,,,,,
"# BFFI Ulmus
# Bornanew is bad cop",,,,,,
BFFIulmusTalkPcGood0,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_ulmusTalk0
$player.toldBornanewHeIsBadGuy",,"""Are you man, or a bit of vermin slipping out the window?"" Bornanew bellows as he lifts Pond bodily, setting him on a sagging cot. You're not sure if the creak is the cheap furniture or Pond's ribs. 

""The Knights have sent me a long way,"" his voice lowers threateningly, ""to deal with you. Pray your answers are to my liking lest I deliver you unto the Knight Inquisitors. They have methods of seeking truth hidden far from God's merciful light.""","bffi_ulmusTalkGood1a:""Easy $global.jethroName. Ulmus only had good intentions I'm sure.""
bffi_ulmusTalkGood1b:""Why wait for them? My techs can simply open up his brain...""",
BFFIulmusTalkPcGood1a,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusTalkGood1a,,"Pond's eyes go large and pleading- with his escape closed off, you are his only salvation.

""Yes, yes,"" he speaks quickly. ""The captain has it right! Menes, he wanted something special. I'm just a middleman, a, a communicator. I just make deals!""

He licks his lips, looking between you and Bornanew, ""Menes was so pleased, I had no idea it wasn't real. I'm no relic-dealer or, or a curate or- you have to believe me, I'm innocent!""",bffi_ulmusTalkGood2:Continue,
BFFIulmusTalkPcGood1b,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusTalkGood1b,$messedUpOnce = true 0,"Pond's eyes go large, his face pale, his breaths coming in sharp gasps.

Bornanew tips his head at Pond and gives you a confused and consternated look. 

""No, no,"" Pond pleads at you, ""No, no need for that, I'll- you see, it wasn't me, this is all a misunderstanding. I make deals. I'm a great communicator. Menes will tell you. It was business, just business!"" ","bffi_ulmusTalkGood1a:""I apologize, Ulmus. It was a joke. I believe you.""
bffi_ulmusTalkSwitch1:""$global.jethroName, look, we're going to have to switch this up.""
#""Pathetic. How about I just shoot him?"" (reach for your sidearm)",
BFFIulmusTalkSwitch1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusTalkSwitch1,,"""You're sure?"" $global.jethroName's voice is flat.","bffi_ulmusTalkGood1a:""No. I, uh, believe Ulmus only ever had good intentions. Right?""
bffi_ulmusTalkPcWrong1:""Yes. I'm sure you can handle it.""",
BFFIulmusTalkPcGood2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusTalkGood2,,"""You confess you knew 'it' was fake,"" Bornanew growls. ""We haven't even told you of what you are accused. You are stained with guilt!""

Pond seems to shrink under Bornanew's accusations.","bffi_ulmusTalkGood3:""They must have threatened you, Ulmus. You wouldn't hurt anybody.""
bffi_ulmusTalkGood3b:""Knight Bornanew is right. You're guilty and deserve punishment.""",
BFFIulmusTalkPcGood3b,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusTalkGood3b,$messedUpOnce = true 0,"Bornanew gives a consternated shake of his head. Pond, terrified, looks between you and Bornanew. 

""The Captain,"" Bornanew says, ""wanted to put you into protective custody. Said you wouldn't hurt anyone, you were threatened."" Bornanew meets your eyes again and says, deliberately, ""I don't believe you.""

""But that's it!"" Pond cries, ""They said they'd- Pathers will do anything!""

""Pathers,"" Bornanew says, his voice icy. ""You do know, Ulmus Pond, how we Knights deal with those heretics."" Bornanew reaches into his satchel.

Pond goes paler, somehow. ""N-no, no. I'll confess! I'll do penance, I'll pray! Tell him!"" He looks to you.","bffi_ulmusTalkGood4a:""We want to help. Tell us who did this to you, Ulmus.""
bffi_ulmusTalkGood4b:""The Knights punish heretics. Forgiveness is for God.""",
BFFIulmusTalkPcGood3bMessedUp,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_ulmusTalkGood3b
$messedUpOnce","$option = bffi_ulmusTalkPcWrong1 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected",,,
BFFIulmusTalkPcGood3,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusTalkGood3,,"""Yes, that's it!"" Pond cries, ""They said they'd do terrible things if I didn't cooperate! Torture, murder, terrible things. Pathers will do anything!""

""Pather heretics,"" Bornanew says, his voice icy. ""You do know, Ulmus Pond, how we Knights deal with Pather heretics?"" Bornanew stands and reaches into his satchel.

Pond goes paler, somehow. ""N-no, no. I'll confess! I'll do penance, I'll pray! I'll tell you whatever you want. Tell him!"" He looks to you.","bffi_ulmusTalkGood4a:""We want to help. Tell us who did this to you, Ulmus.""
bffi_ulmusTalkGood4b:""The Knights punish heretics. Forgiveness is for God.""",
BFFIulmusTalkPcGood4,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusTalkGood4a,,"""There was... a Walker of the Path,"" Pond sputters. ""The Luddic Path.""

""He told me to talk to Menes, to, to make the offer. He said a Mammonite couldn't resist an object of such unique quality. And- and I was to arrange transport from the Fringe. Make it appear legitimate. Set the documents straight.""

Bornanew draws his cheap datapad from his satchel, the screen already set to a map of the greater Persean Sector.","bffi_ulmusTalkGood5a:""Show him, Ulmus. Who's behind this. Where.""
bffi_ulmusTalkGood5b:""This is how you make it out of here alive, Ulmus. Show him.""",
BFFIulmusTalkPcGood4b,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusTalkGood4b,$messedUpOnce = true 0,"Bornanew gives you a warning look. Pond simply deflates, looking utterly lost. ""There was... a Walker,"" he sputters. ""Of the Luddic Path.""

""He told me to talk to Menes, to, to make the offer. He said a Mammonite couldn't resist an object of such unique quality. And- and I was to arrange transport from the Fringe. Make it appear legitimate. Set the documents straight.""

Bornanew draws his cheap datapad from his satchel, the screen already set to a map of the greater Persean Sector.","bffi_ulmusTalkGood5a:""Show him, Ulmus. Who's behind this. Where.""
bffi_ulmusTalkGood5b:""This is how you make it out of here alive, Ulmus. Show him.""",
