$player.sdtu_weaponNone","EndConversation DO_NOT_FIRE
HideVisual","In a motion born of long hours of training, your leg snaps toward Sedge at the speed of thought. It meets the center of his head with full force, cracking his head back in a violent jerk.

A single shudder passes through his body, from his thick neck, already purpling from devastated bone and tissue, to his booted feet. His head slumps to the side at an unnatural angle, blood running from what remains of his nose, and his mouth and eyes.",bffi_ulmusSedge6:Check on Bornanew,"# not sure the drama works if you snap his neck or w/e?
# of course it does! let's do it"
BFFIulmusSedge6,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusSedge6,"$player.bffi_playerKilledSedgeAfterPond = true
$player.killedSedge = true
$global.bornanewWasShotBySedge = true
SetPersonHidden sedge true","Bornanew lives, by a thread.

In the moments since the exchange, a time hollowed out by violence and filled with the fleeting intensity of adrenaline, your security team appears.

Finding you unhurt, they attach stabilization packs and trauma strips to the fallen Knight. He's left an incredible pool of blood in the cheap apartment. It drips down the narrow stairs.

The other two bodies lie dead.

It is unclear how fully Ulmus Pond was exploited by or truly believed in the Pather cause, but his loyalty - if he ever had any - died with him.",bffi_ulmusSedge7:Continue,
BFFIulmusSedge7,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusSedge7,ShowLargePlanet,"You carry Bornanew's leather satchel to the shuttle. Your team carries his unconscious body. 

As it lifts, he is laid across several seats. The designated medic keeps close watch over the small ad-hoc network of medical machines.

Bornanew's datapad opens to your touch, allowing you to access the coordinates given by Ulmus Pond. And a recording of the brief interrogation. $global.jethroName planned for the possibility of his incapacitation, or death. And gave you access to his work.",bffi_ulmusSedge8:Continue,"# he trusts you, see!"
BFFIulmusSedge8,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_ulmusSedge8,"SetTextHighlights ""$bffi_patherStationSystem.""
ShowDefaultVisual
unset $global.bffi_followUlmusPond
Call $global.bffi_ref spawnPatherBase
$global.bffi_investigatePatherStation = true
Call $global.bffi_ref updateStage
FireAll PopulateOptions","A medical team rushes past you, to Bornanew, as you step out onto your flagship. 

He'll live, you are assured. But it'll hurt; this is left unsaid by your flagship's chief medical officer.

It is quite clear to you now that this is a Pather conspiracy, and they will kill to keep it from unravelling. Your next step is to the source of the fake relic: a lonely orbit on the fringe of the Persean Sector.

In the $bffi_patherStationSystem.",,
,,,,,,
"# BFFI ulmus end, no Sedge",,,,,,
BFFIulmusNoSedgeOutro0,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_ulmusTalkSedgeCheck
$player.shotSedge",,"Bornanew's datapad trembles in Pond's hands. He cannot designate a star system until Bornanew holds the pad steady for him. A target.

""This Pather, Ulmus,"" Bornanew says, glancing at the datapad then placing it in his satchel. The threat retreats from his voice. ""Tell us his name.""

Tears stream down Ponds' face; the man looks deflated, and absolutely defeated. ""Sedge,"" he says.

Bornanew shoots a look at you.","bffi_pondNoSedgeOutro1a:""Wrestling Sedge. But he's dead.""
bffi_pondNoSedgeOutro1b:""I recall handling that problem already.""",
BFFIpondNoSedgeOutro1a,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_pondNoSedgeOutro1a,"$option = bffi_pondNoSedgeOutro2 0
