ShowDefaultVisual","The Pather's face twists with anger.  ""Then burn with the rest, Molochian!"" $heOrShe says, then disappears in a haze of compression artifacts.

The link plays a crackling buzz of a suppressed electronic warfare signal for a moment before your comms officer, considerately, shuts it off for you.",,
BFFIstationTalk1honesty,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_stationTalk1honesty,"$saidHonesty = true 0
$madeCase++
FireAll BFFIstationTalkHub","""Question me not!"" True anger flashes across $hisOrHer eyes. ""What know you of verity? You are blind to God, blind to the Word, you worship only credits and power. This I see full well!"" 

""Would you have me submit to the creeping decay of the Church's heresy? Submit to the Knight-Inquisitors that I might be tortured into false confession?""

$HeOrShe pauses, breathing heavily for a moment, then more quietly says, ""I was not made for such skulduggery. It is a Mammonite's trade."" The words come more softly now. ""Will you now fight or no? Better to die a martyr than a hypocrite.""",,
BFFIstationTalk1sin,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_stationTalk1sin,"$saidSin = true 0
$madeCase++
FireAll BFFIstationTalkHub","""So you accuse me of sin, Molochian?"" Anger flashes across $hisOrHer eyes. ""What choice have I? Submit to the creeping decay of the Church's heresy? Submit to the Knight-Inquisitors that I be tortured into false confession?""

""Question not my piety, nor devotion. Give me arms, or none, and I shall face you or your brutes of the so-called Knights of Ludd to the end of my blood!""

$HeOrShe pauses a moment, almost overcome, to breathe heavily.

""I was not made for such skulduggery."" The words come softly now. ""It is a Mammonite's trade. But what choice is given?"" $HeOrShe glares at you. ""Will you make me a martyr now, or no?""",,
BFFIstationTalk1blind,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_stationTalk1blind,"$saidBlind = true 0
$madeCase++
FireAll BFFIstationTalkHub","True anger flashes through  $hisOrHer eyes. ""What choice have I? Shall I submit to the creeping decay of the Church's heresy? Submit to the Knight-Inquisitors that I might be tortured into false confession? It is they who slowly tear apart the Faith, not I! It is they who scorn the Word, not I!""

""Question not my piety, nor my devotion! Give me arms, or none, and I shall face you and your brutes of the so-called Knights of Ludd to the end of my blood!"" $HeOrShe pauses a moment, almost overcome, to breathe heavily. ""I was not made for such skulduggery."" The words come more softly now. ""It is a Mammonite's trade. But what choice is given? Will you make me a martyr now, or no?""",,
BFFIstationTalk2tracked,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_stationTalk2tracked,"$saidTracked = true 0
$madeCase++
FireAll BFFIstationTalkHub","""So you have,"" $heOrShe admits. ""I had thought that not possible - and assured it was not by Brother Sedge.""

The Pather looks away. ""That man would have told me anything to get his way, I think. And if somehow I didn't agree... I give thanks that it did not come to that.""",,
BFFIstationTalk2fight,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_stationTalk2fight,"$saidFight = true 0
$madeCase++
FireAll BFFIstationTalkHub","""We're all given our place,"" $heOrShe says, both annoyed and discouraged. ""The Path is not easy, nor does it provide comfort. For that, we were given the Word.""

$HisOrHer eyes are searching, $hisOrHer devotion to this aspect of the cause obviously wavering. ""Sedge was strong, and many followed him. Besides, he was backed by-"" $HeOrShe catches $himOrHerself. ""Backed by a better Walker by far, blessed be his Path.""

""Well, it's done now, isn't it? That scheme is dead, and you bring here the technology of death.""",,
BFFIstationTalk2sedge,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_stationTalk2sedge,"$madeCase++
$saidSedge = true 0","$HisOrHer eyes narrow. ""It doesn't matter now; I hear he was murdered, shot in the back by some spacer mercenary who is more machine than flesh.""

""Merciful Providence forgive me,"" $hisOrHer tone softens slightly, ""for to speak ill of the dead, and a martyr to our cause at that, but. The man was a beast and I am better pleased to find him on the other side of the infinite."" ","bffi_stationTalk2sedgeA:""Then praise the Path! You're free of the beast and his schemes.""
bffi_stationTalk2sedgeB:""It is I who shot Sedge. Though I'm less machine than you'd hope.""",
BFFIstationTalk2sedgeZ,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_stationTalk2sedge
$player.bffi_playerKilledSedgeAfterPond","$madeCase++
$saidSedge = true 0","$HisOrHer eyes narrow. ""It doesn't matter now; I hear he was murdered, shot in the back by some spacer mercenary who is more machine than flesh.""

""Merciful Providence forgive me,"" $hisOrHer tone softens slightly, ""for to speak ill of the dead, and a martyr to our cause at that, but. The man was a beast and I am better pleased to find him on the other side of the infinite."" ","bffi_stationTalk2sedgeA:""Then praise the Path! You're free of the beast and his schemes.""
bffi_stationTalk2sedgeB:""It is I who killed Sedge. After he murdered the man I was speaking to.""",
BFFIstationTalk2sedgeA,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_stationTalk2sedgeA,FireAll BFFIstationTalkHub,"""Mind, do hide your forked tongue."" The Pather has a mean smile. ""I see your obvious ploy, to turn me from the Path. But as is said by teachers wiser than I, 'the devil will lie by the truth itself'."" $HeOrShe makes a show of looking you over through the comms.

""Nonetheless. I do find myself free of his... customs of leadership.""",,
BFFIstationTalk2sedgeB,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_stationTalk2sedgeB,"FireAll BFFIstationTalkHub
$saidKilledSedge = true 0","""Hah!"" The Pather has a mean smile. ""An obvious boast, typical of a Molochian."" $HeOrShe makes a show of looking at you through the comms, ""You couldn't have taken Sedge. He was a greater warrior than you or I, by far.""

""Nonetheless, I weep not to be free of his... leadership.""",,
BFFIstationTalk2sedgeBZ,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_stationTalk2sedgeB
$player.bffi_playerKilledSedgeAfterPond","FireAll BFFIstationTalkHub
$saidKilledSedge = true 0","""Hah!"" The Pather has a mean smile. ""An obvious boast, typical of a Molochian."" $HeOrShe makes a show of looking at you through the comms, ""You couldn't have taken Sedge... except by cowardly ambush, or some other deception. He was a greater warrior than you or I, by far.""

""Nonetheless, I weep not to be free of his... leadership.""",,
BFFIpsRuseNiceSetup,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_psRuseNiceSetup,,"You explain that no devotion or zealotry, however righteous, can overcome the power of your $shipOrFleet, or the others that would follow if you failed to win the day.

Is $heOrShe so loyal to Sedge's plan that $heOrShe is willing to die for it - even after it's fallen apart? Besides, a schism across the whole of the ecumene of the Luddic faith would lead to a sectarian war which could see millions of Faithful dead. And not even for the cause of the Path, but for a falsehood!

$HeOrShe has a choice, you explain. Call it a Molochian bargain. Either this is a major loss of personnel, materiel, and the station, or it can be a minor loss of certain assets - for a failed barbaric scheme $heOrShe doesn't even really believe in.",bffi_psRuseOpenNice:Propose terms,
BFFIpsRuseMeanSetup,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_psRuseMeanSetup,,"You explain that there's one way that this is going to go, no devotion or zealotry can overcome the truth of the power of your $shipOrFleet - all ends result in $hisOrHer annihilation, and that of $hisOrHer followers, and of the station.

$HeOrShe has a choice, you explain. Call it a Molochian bargain, if it makes them feel better. Either this is a major loss of personnel, materiel, and the station, or it can be a minor loss of certain assets for a scheme $heOrShe doesn't even really believe in.

Is $heOrShe so loyal to Sedge's sect that $heOrShe is willing to die for it - even after it's already falling apart?",bffi_psRuseOpenMean:Propose terms,
