Call $global.bffi_ref cleanUpPatherBase","The primary defenses are destroyed, the command and control section holed and venting fiery atmo. The superstructure's own spin is pulling the station apart like slow butchery.

You destroyed the nanoforge, but did not secure the evidence Bornanew needed to find the mole in the Cathedral of Holy Exodus on Tartessus.

""It is the best that could be done,"" Bornanew says, eyes downcast. His notebook is closed, before him. ""I must submit myself to the Excubitor Orbis for judgment. On Hesperus.""",,# only get one line to do this; can't interrupt flow of post-combat loot -dgb
#BFFIpatherStationDefeatedNone,BFFIpatherStationDefeated,,,,,
# BFFI raid Pather station,,,,,,
BFFIaddStationRaidOption,PopulateOptions,"$bffi_patherStationTarget
$menuState == main
Call $global.bffi_ref updateData
$bffi_stage == INVESTIGATE_PATHER_STATION",FireBest BFFIpatherStationRaidCheckHostilesNearby,,2:bffi_stationRaidStart:Assemble your officers to plan a raid to capture the nanoforge,
BFFIdisableStationRaidOption,BFFIpatherStationRaidCheckHostilesNearby,HostileFleetNearbyAndAware,"SetEnabled bffi_stationRaidStart false
SetTooltip bffi_stationRaidStart ""A nearby hostile fleet is tracking your movements, making a raid impossible.""",,,
BFFIpatherStationRaidStart,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_stationRaidStart,"$raidDifficulty = 200 0
$raidGoBackTrigger = PopulateOptions 0
$raidRestrictToTrigger =  BFFIpatherStationRaidFinished 0
$raidContinueTrigger = BFFIpatherStationRaidDescription 0
AddRaidObjective genericIcon ""Capture datastores then destroy the nanoforge"" HIGH 3000 BFFIpatherStationRaidFinished true
ShowImageVisual raid_prepare","You convene your officers, and Bornanew, to evaluate the situation.

Pather resistance is expected to be fierce; the core of their militants have a zealous faith, little fear of death, and are often experienced fighters. However they eschew top of the line technology and combat enhancement, whether cybernetic or biochemical.

Bornanew clears his throat and speaks. ""Certain classes of combat drugs are accepted among Luddic Path militants. They favor, ah, 'natural' sources."" He takes in the confused looks. ""Plants,"" he adds.

Capturing high-value datastores before they're wiped creates exceptional difficulties. The assault must be lightning-quick, and disabling rather than destructive as much as possible.",mktRaidNonMarket:Continue,
BFFIpatherStationRaidStartNoBorn,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_stationRaidStart
$global.bornanewWasShotBySedge","$raidDifficulty = 200 0
$raidGoBackTrigger = PopulateOptions 0
$raidRestrictToTrigger =  BFFIpatherStationRaidFinished 0
$raidContinueTrigger = BFFIpatherStationRaidDescription 0
AddRaidObjective genericIcon ""Capture datastores then destroy the nanoforge"" HIGH 3000 BFFIpatherStationRaidFinished true
ShowImageVisual raid_prepare","You convene your officers to evaluate the situation.

Pather resistance is expected to be fierce; the core of their militants have a zealous faith, little fear of death, and are often experienced fighters. However they eschew top of the line technology and combat enhancement, whether cybernetic or biochemical.

Capturing high-value datastores before they're wiped creates exceptional difficulties. The assault must be lightning-quick, and disabling rather than destructive so much as possible.",mktRaidNonMarket:Continue,
BFFIpatherStationRaidOutro1,BFFIpatherStationRaidFinished,,,"You watch from the command center as marine squads launch the opening salvo from seemingly innocuous cargo containers. Powered armor units burst forth like locusts; combat techs inject malware into the station network, demolitions breach emergency blast doors, and assault teams cut a swath to key targets.

Nodes on the adaptive objective graph, woven through the station tactical display, are achieved one after another. Points blink from blood-red to amber or green, depending on found conditions. Indeed, some comms relays and data clusters auto-destruct upon unauthorized access, but others quietly fail, allowing techs to seize the contents.

The last red-indicated volume is the industrial section housing what is indeed the station's nanoforge; the Pathers had regrouped for a last stand. And so it is.",,
BFFIpatherStationRaidOutro2,BFFIpatherStationRaidDescription,,"AddTextSmall ""Extracted datacores"" highlight
AddTextSmall ""Destroyed nanoforge"" highlight
$global.bffi_raidedPatherStation = true
Call $global.bffi_ref cleanUpPatherBase","They were caught off-guard. Despite the large numbers of armed zealots of the Path, your strike teams concentrated force where their defenses, fighting to the death, could not hold.

Teams return to waiting evac drones and shuttles, trailed by tethered spoils: memory blocks torn from their cradles, a few bagged prisoners.

A blue-white flash illuminates the returning victors. Behind them, the industrial section spins itself apart, structural plates shattered into glowing shards, struts tortuously bent, and that atmo which hasn't burned off in a glowing plume forms a rapidly expanding, dissipating cloud, illuminated from within by dying light.",bffi_psDestroyed:Continue,
,,,,,,
BFFIpatherStationRaidDestroyed,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_psDestroyed,,"The prize, turned over to your Tech officer's analysis team by a crew of sweating salvors, is a largely uncorrupted backup archive. Standard Domain tech, it hardly looks like the Pathers even knew it was quietly doing its job behind a thin access panel.

The technicians descend upon it with a suite of interfacers, passing every scrap of data to the analysts working in an isolated computing environment to reconstruct the system, starting with comms buffers and metadata.",bffi_psDestroyed0:Continue,
BFFIpsDestroyed0a,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_psDestroyed0,BeginConversation bornanew,"A cloud of icons, sigils, words forms. Names, front companies, ships, codewords, and references to theological agitprop. Bornanew follows closely, his hands not nearly as deft with the interface as your dedicated techs.

You can see in his body language the exact moment that he finds something he recognizes.","bffi_psDestroyed1:""$global.jethroName. What is it?""",
BFFIpsDestroyed1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_psDestroyed1,,"""Keepfaith,"" Bornanew says. Fumbling with his datapad, the shared workspace highlights all references to that string of letters, then focuses, arranging comms logs and metadata into blocks, compressing everything else down into unobtrusive corners.

He leans back, his eyes darting around some internal catalogue. His paper notebook appears in his hands and he flips to a page as if to check something. ",bffi_psDestroyed2:Continue,
BFFIpsDestroyed2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_psDestroyed2,,"""Cedra Keepfaith,"" he explains. ""A subcurate of the Holy Cathedral of Exodus on Tartessus, in the Eos Exodus system. She has authority over the scriptorium.""

He sees your look, then explains. ""Books. They repair and reproduce books for the library. And,"" his voice drops, ""the vaults. She would have access.""","bffi_psDestroyed3:""So this Keepfaith is your Pather mole?""",
BFFIpsDestroyed3,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_psDestroyed3,"$global.bffi_arrestTheCurate = true
Call $global.bffi_ref updateStage
Call $global.bffi_ref cleanUpPatherBase","""She would fit,"" he says, thinking. ""My impression was that her ambitions in the Church have not been satisfied for many years, be that fair or no. She was not humble upon or meeting."" 

""These logs appear to reference correspondence with her. She turned down credits, it appears. Would gratification of spite be payment enough?"" 

He turns to you, done with speculation. ""Certainly she did not act alone, but this connects her to the act. She must be arrested and taken to the Inquisitors for investigation and judgment.""",bffi_psDestroyed4:Continue,
BFFIpsDestroyed4,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_psDestroyed4,,"A junior officer pokes their head into the briefing room, ""$PlayerSirOrMadam, my apologies. The chief thought you'd want to see this.""

Two burly salvors, still in their sweaty suit-liners, haul a crate and set it on the deckplates with a solid thump. With an impish grin, one of them looses the catches and together they pull the top-cover away.

It's filled with work-gloves. All of like chirality.",bffi_psDestroyed5:Continue,
BFFIpsDestroyed5,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_psDestroyed5,,"Bornanew lets out a breath.

""I ought to have anticipated this."" He sounds annoyed with himself. ""Costs no more to run a batch of one than of..."" He reaches in, picking up a glove, then pressing into the cargo container to feel for density. ""Five-twelve?"" He turns to you. ""Perhaps five hundred eleven, without our other hard-won specimen?""

He wipes his hands, as if something unpleasant had got on them. ""These will need to be destroyed.""",bffi_psDestroyed6:Order it done,
BFFIpsDestroyed6,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_psDestroyed6,"AddTextSmall ""Additional false relics destroyed"" highlight
EndConversation
ShowDefaultVisual","It is done with swift enthusiasm by a crew monitored by your ops chief.

The last step is the capture of Bornanew's mole on Tartessus.",,
BFFIpsDestroyedBornMed0,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_psDestroyed0
$global.bornanewShotDuringBFFI",,"A cloud of icons, sigils, words forms. Names, front companies, ships, codewords, and references to theological agitprop. Your tech officer's hands blur as they manipulate an interface invisible to you; his subtle cybermods blink rapidly. And then stop, steady.

""Captain, we may have something.""

Their eyes refocus on the real world again, taking a moment to adapt to mundanity. ""Something for your, ah, consultant. The Knight.""","bffi_psDestroyedBornMed1:""What have you found?""",
BFFIpsDestroyedBornMed1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_psDestroyedBornMed1,,"""A word. Maybe a code? A name? It comes up several times, relating to Tartessus and the template they fed into the forge.""

""The word is 'Keepfaith'. One word. Maybe it means something special to the Ludd... ics?""","bffi_psDestroyedBornMed2:""Clean up some representative samples for me.""",
BFFIpsDestroyedBornMed2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_psDestroyedBornMed2,,"""Aye, $playerSirOrMadam,"" they reply, and their eyes become unfocused, face slack, cybermods blinking rapidly once more.

You turn, bracing yourself for a negotiation with your medical chief to allow a brief conversation with Bornanew.",bffi_psDestroyedBornMed3:Go to the medbay,
BFFIpsDestroyedBornMed3,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_psDestroyedBornMed3,BeginConversation bornanew,"""Keepfaith,"" Bornanew says, repeating the last word of your question.

He leans back in his bed, his eyes darting around some internal catalogue. His notebook appears in his hands - it is impressive to have snuck an outside object past the wary eye of your senior medical officer - and he flips to a page to check something. 

""Subcurate Cedra Keepfaith. Authority over the scriptorium of the Holy Cathedral of Exodus, on Tartessus, in the Eos Exodus system.""","bffi_psDestroyedBornMed4:""Over the what?""",
BFFIpsDestroyedBornMed4,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_psDestroyedBornMed4,,"""Apologies,"" he says, closing the notebook, then tapping its cover. ""Books. They repair and reproduce books for the library. And,"" his voice drops, ""the vaults. She would have access.""","bffi_psDestroyedBornMed5:""So this Keepfaith is your Pather mole.""",
BFFIpsDestroyedBornMed5,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_psDestroyedBornMed5,"$global.bffi_arrestTheCurate = true
Call $global.bffi_ref updateStage
Call $global.bffi_ref cleanUpPatherBase","""She would fit,"" he says, thinking. ""Her ambitions... were great, and unfulfilled.""

""These logs show correspondence. She turned down a payment of credits from the Path."" He takes several slow breaths. ""Would spite be payment enough for her?""

""Didn't act alone."" His eyes close, his breaths coming roughly now. ""But she was their access. Must be arrested. Taken to the Inquisitors.""

The distinct sound of your chief medical officer clearing their throat sounds from the doorway.","bffi_psDestroyedBornMed6:""Get some rest. We're going to Tartessus.""",
BFFIpsDestroyedBornMed6,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_psDestroyedBornMed6,"EndConversation
