BFFIarrestCurate1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestCurate1,ShowLargePlanet,"Bornanew's credentials - in truth, those of Archcurate Jaspis - fell the meddling traffic control bureaucrats who stand in your way, one after another.

A Knight-novice, of equal rank but rather lesser age than $global.jethroName, puts on a grimace as he is forced to reassign the shuttle-slot of some curate from the landing pad nearest to the Cathedral of Holy Exodus.    

Nearest is a relative term. On Tartessus, the Church of Galactic Redemption takes the view that spaceborn traffic is a shameful act to be hidden away from the eyes of land-dwellers. As your shuttle lands, Bornanew observes that the cathedral is somewhat over the horizon.",bffi_idolTalkIntro1:Board what passes for transport on Tartessus,
BFFIidolTalkIntro1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_idolTalkIntro1,ShowDefaultVisual,"* * *

You step off the rickety bus, a boxy thing of agriplastic and mold-pressed wood scrap hiding a battery and motor, with a crowd of day-laborers and pilgrims.

This is not one of the major shrines of the Pilgrim's Path, of course, but the Cathedral of Holy Exodus is held in high esteem in the local system and beyond.",bffi_idolTalkIntro2:Continue,"# Thank you, thank you. I'll see myself out. -dgb"
BFFIidolTalkIntro1Shot,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_idolTalkIntro1
$global.bornanewWasShotBySedge score:2",ShowDefaultVisual,"* * *

You step off the rickety bus, a boxy thing of agriplastic and mold-pressed wood scrap hiding a battery and motor, with a crowd of sweating day-laborers and pilgrims. Bornanew, still shaky on his feet as he recovers from his injuries, takes your arm as he steps down to the road.

This is not one of the major shrines of the Pilgrim's Path, of course, but the Cathedral of Holy Exodus is held in high esteem in the local system and beyond.",bffi_idolTalkIntro2:Continue,
BFFIidolTalkIntro2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_idolTalkIntro2,"BeginConversation bornanew
FireAll BFFIidolTalkHubOpts","""And it is the seat of not more than a few 'divergent' notions of doctrine,"" Bornanew tells you in a low voice.

""At least according to the 'Ineffablist' school backed by the Reverend Archcurate Jaspis, among others. Here, though a minority of the Church ecumene, there is a local majority of so-called 'Mundanians'. Do not misunderstand me; they are not schismatics."" He lets a moment of silence pass.

""Nonetheless.""",,
BFFIidolTalkHubIntroBB,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_idolTalkIntro2
$global.bornanewBadBoy > 1","BeginConversation bornanew
FireAll BFFIidolTalkHubOpts","""And it is the seat of not more than a few heretical notions of doctrine, I'm afraid,"" Bornanew tells you in a low voice.

""At least according to the 'Ineffablist' school backed by the Reverend Archcurate Jaspis, among others. Here, though a minority of the Church ecumene, there is a local majority of so-called 'Mundanians'. Do not misunderstand me, they are not schismatics. Yet."" He lets a moment of silence pass.

""Nonetheless.""",,
BFFIidolTalkHubOptB,BFFIidolTalkHubOpts,$askedMundanian,,,"bffi_idolTalkTrouble:""Are you telling me there is going to be trouble?""",
BFFIidolTalkHubOptC,BFFIidolTalkHubOpts,!$askedMundanian,,,"bffi_idolTalkMundanianMore:""So what's wrong with the 'Mundanians'?""",
BFFIidolTalkHubOptD,BFFIidolTalkHubOpts,!$askedIneffablist,,,"bffi_idolTalkIneffablistMore:""What distinguishes the Ineffablist doctrine?""",
BFFIidolTalkHubOptE,BFFIidolTalkHubOpts,"!$askedIdolators
$mentionedIdolators",,,"bffi_idolTalkIdolators:""'Idolators', huh. And what do they call you?""",
BFFIidolTalkHubOptF,BFFIidolTalkHubOpts,,,,"bffi_idolTalkBoring:""You fight over this? It sounds interminable.""",
BFFIidolTalkMundanianMore,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_idolTalkMundanianMore,"$askedMundanian = true 0
FireAll BFFIidolTalkHubOpts","""The Mundanians,"" he continues, ""hold that Ludd's individual humanity provides a... spiritual focus. A manner of relation, a holy sympathy. Physical objects said to be associated with Ludd may play a role, hence the practice of veneration through - not of - relics. At least that is how they would describe it.""

""The ban on venerating the worldly individual of Ludd is clear, but what of proximal objects? The Word is not so definitive.""",,
BFFIidolTalkMundanianMoreBB,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_idolTalkMundanianMore
$global.bornanewBadBoy > 1","$askedMundanian = true 0
$mentionedIdolators = true 0
FireAll BFFIidolTalkHubOpts","""Mundanians,"" he continues, ""hold that Ludd's individual humanity provides a... spiritual focus. A manner of relation, a holy sympathy. Physical objects said to be associated with Ludd may play a role, hence the practice of veneration through - not of - relics. At least that is how they would describe such heresy. It is the apologia of Idolators.""

""The ban on venerating the worldly individual of Ludd is clear, but the Word is less direct on the matter of proximal objects.""",,
BFFIidolTalkIneffablistMore,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_idolTalkIneffablistMore,"$mentionedIdolators = true 0
$askedIneffablist = true 0
FireAll BFFIidolTalkHubOpts","""We consider the conscious unknowing of Ludd's secular individuality a sign of devotion and a functional virtue.""

He gives you a look. ""Meaning we view the veneration of relics as idolatry. Some amongst us call the Mundanians 'Idolators' for their views. There are other... conflicts of practice, as well.""",,
BFFIidolTalkIneffablistMoreBB,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_idolTalkIneffablistMore
$global.bornanewBadBoy > 1","$mentionedIdolators = true 0
$askedIneffablist = true 0
FireAll BFFIidolTalkHubOpts","""We consider the conscious unknowing of Ludd's secular individuality a sign of devotion and a functional virtue. This is as the Word tells it.""

He gives you a look. ""Meaning we view the veneration of relics as idolatry. Some amongst us call the Mundanians 'Idolators' for their views, and not without justification.""",,
BFFIidolTalkIdolators,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_idolTalkIdolators,"$askedIdolators = true 0
FireAll BFFIidolTalkHubOpts","""Ah."" Bornanew looks a little embarrassed.

""They call us 'Ignorants'. For we choose to wallow in our own ignorance. From a certain point of view.""",,
BFFIidolTalkNameCallingOut,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_idolTalkNameCalling,"$didNameCallOut = true 0
FireAll FireAll BFFIidolTalkHubOpts","""And, ah,"" Bornanew's brow furrows. ""Mind your use of such nomenclature. It would be inconvenient to cause offense at some inopportune moment.""

""Besides, name-calling is unseemly for a Knight who ought hold himself to higher standards. I am sworn to face conflict directly by the truth of the path illuminated by faith.""",,
BFFIidolTalkNameCallingOut2,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_idolTalkNameCalling
$didNameCallOut",FireAll FireAll BFFIidolTalkHubOpts,"""Best not to cast such words about thoughtlessly.""",,
