FireBest DialogOptionSelected","He laughs. ""Boldly spoken from yourself, captain.""",,
BFFIarrestOppo3d,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestOppo3d,"$option = bffi_arrestEnter 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","""I am,"" he says with a laugh, ""aren't I.""

His expression grows serious after a moment. ""And yes, it must.""",,
BFFIarrestEnter,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestEnter,,"You stand together at last in the plaza under the huge archway of the cathedral's entrance. Bornanew meets a uniformed though unarmored Knight to exchange a few words. Bornanew shows the Knight something in his hand which he returns to pocket in his robes.

The Knight steps aside, and allows you to enter, bypassing the lines of pilgrims awaiting the mid-morning prayer.",bffi_arrest1:Enter the Cathedral of Holy Exodus,
BFFIarrest1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrest1,"EndConversation DO_NOT_FIRE
ShowImageVisual cathedral_skyline
PlayCustomMusic music_luddite_shrine","You enter the great nave of the Cathedral of Holy Exodus.

Among towering columns are affixed recovered landing pods of the early Luddic refugee ships, now integrated into the vaults, painted with gilt and green, bedecked with candles and hanging glass ornaments which break the beams of the sun - filtered through ranks of high windows - into thousands of rainbow shards, endlessly refracting.

It is an ecstasy of light, a galaxy unto itself.

Bornanew pauses beside you, looking upward. Could one old work-glove and a lie tip all of this down to shatter upon the ground?",bffi_arrest2:Continue,
BFFIarrest1b,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_arrest1
$global.bornanewWasShotBySedge","EndConversation DO_NOT_FIRE
ShowImageVisual cathedral_skyline
PlayCustomMusic music_luddite_shrine","You enter the great nave of the Cathedral of Holy Exodus.

Among towering columns are affixed recovered landing pods of the early Luddic refugee ships, now integrated into the vaults, painted with gilt and green, bedecked with candles and hanging glass ornament which break the beams of the sun - filtered through ranks of high windows - into thousands of rainbow shards endlessly refracting.

It is an ecstasy of light, a galaxy unto itself.

Bornanew pauses beside you, catching his breath, looking upward. Could one old work-glove and a lie tip all of this down to shatter upon the ground?",bffi_arrest2:Continue,
BFFIarrest2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrest2,,"He leads you to a small alcove, invisible at the foot of the luminous architectural forest of cut stone and carved wood. And there, after exchanging words with an attendant, a door is revealed in the ornately carved wall.

You follow Bornanew's lead, stepping out of the glory of light into a cool, dark space. Your eyes take a moment to adjust to the dimness and relatively mundane - though still ornately hand-wrought - decor.",bffi_arrest3:Continue,
BFFIarrest3,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrest3,,"There are halls and offices here, lit not by candles but humble glowplates belched legion from Asher's nanoforge. The walls of cut stone are trimmed with alternating panels and mouldings of wood.

Bornanew's words and the token, presumably provided by the Archcurate Jaspis, clear a path through frowning oblate-secretaries and young Knight-novices on guard duty.

Not all are so dour; one or two initiates, scurrying by with armloads of books, greet Bornanew by name.",bffi_arrest4:Follow,
BFFIarrest4,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrest4,#PauseMusic,"You follow Bornanew into a long room, a gallery of columns intermingled with bookcases; cleverly designed lightwells - and, surely, a series of mirrors - provide shafts of sunlight, motes dancing with little concern in their small world within this analog archive. 

Heads turn to follow your progress past desks stacked with paper books, writing implements, and even the occasional low-fidelity interface terminal.

Your tactical sense notes the figures at side-doors who disappear purposefully, clearly headed off to spread this news and summon gawkers - or allies.

Your weapon-hand twitches.",bffi_arrest5:Steady...,
BFFIarrest5,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrest5,"PlayCustomMusic music_luddite_market_hostile
EndConversation DO_NOT_FIRE
BeginConversation cedra_keepfaith
ShowSecondPerson bornanew","Bornanew approaches a proud figure all in holy vestments at the head of the room.

""Subcurate Cedra Keepfaith."" $global.jethroName's voice is confident.

The figure turns, finally. ""Novice,"" she replies, tone intent on the gradient of authority. ""Why have you returned to my scriptorium? Have you been assigned additional penitential duties?""

A mocking smile flits upon her lip.",bffi_arrest6:Watch him work,
BFFIarrest6,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrest6,,"""It was you,"" Bornanew says with perfect earnestness.

""You scanned the glove said to be of Ludd. You did this in the vault of this cathedral, and you knowingly passed that scan data to an agent of the heretics called the Luddic Path. Their aim, and yours, was to sow discord within the Church of Galactic Redemption. This I shall prove before the judgement of the Inquisitors.""

""For these crimes,"" he raises his voice against the growing murmurs, ""against the Holy Church, by the authority of the Reverend Archcurate Sophronia Jaspis, as a Knight of Ludd, I do now place you under arrest.""",bffi_arrest7:Continue,
BFFIarrest6bb,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_arrest6
$global.bornanewBadBoy > 2",,"""It was you,"" Bornanew says with perfect earnestness. ""Traitor.""

""You scanned the glove said to be of Ludd. You did this in the vault of this cathedral, and you knowingly passed that scan data to an agent of the heretics called the Luddic Path. Their aim, and yours, was to sow discord within the Church of Galactic Redemption. This I know, and this truth the Inquisitors shall pull from you!""

""For these crimes,"" he raises his voice against the growing murmurs, ""against the Holy Church, by the authority of the Reverend Archcurate Sophronia Jaspis, as a Knight of Ludd, I do now place you under arrest.""",bffi_arrest7:Continue,
BFFIarrest7,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrest7,,"There are gasps, and a muffled clatter as some initiate drops their work. Keepfaith's gaze, already chilly, turns poisonous upon Bornanew.

""Blind Jaspis has no power here,"" she says. ""And you, a mere novice of a Knight, making ungodly accusations against a superior? I shall assign you further penance if a full apology is not made... instantly!""",bffi_arrest8:Continue,
BFFIarrest8,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrest8,,"""Brother Bornanew,"" a Knight-Captain appears behind the angry subcurate.

He attempts a comradely tone, his carbine slung at his side.

""Please,"" he says. ""Let us go together to resolve this misunderstanding with the archcurate of this cathedral. There is no need to herein bear the hammer and the sword-""",bffi_arrest9:Continue,
BFFIarrest9,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrest9,,"""There is no misunderstanding, brother,"" Bornanew cuts off the Knight-Captain's words, keeping his eyes on Keepfaith. ""I bear my quest not lightly, and seek to fulfill my duty sworn to the Excubitor Orbis.""

He reaches into his robes.

""Knight-Captain,"" says Keepfaith, drawing her breath. ""Arrest your novice! He's to be punished for irreverence toward the authority of the Church and, and for these wild accusations!""",bffi_arrest10:Continue,
BFFIarrest10,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrest10,,"Bornanew steps forward, prompting the Knight-Captain to raise the carbine he had held at his side. A hint of victory settles into Keepfaith's eyes.

""You dare assault a curate in this holy place?"" she says, projecting her voice to all corners of the room, ringing harshly. ""Is there no low to which this too-old novice won't sink?""",bffi_arrest12:Continue,"# intentional use of ""curate"" instead of subcurate btw -dgb"
#BFFIarrest11,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrest11,,"Bornanew draws his hand from his robes. You see dangling the token you glimpsed only briefly before: carved in wood, on a string, is a flower growing out of an oddly shaped shoe. A token of Jaspis?

""Beg hear me, Faithful!"" Bornanew's head turns; he meets the eyes of those assembled, from the apprentices of the scriptorium to the Knight-Captain and, finally, the subcurate before him.

""Cedra Keepfaith invited the serpent of heresy into this holy place that it might spread a venom in the heart of the Church. Already it has poisoned one among us.""",bffi_arrest12:Continue,# cut to move scene along faster
#BFFIarrest12,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrest12,,"He steps forward again, pushing the barrel of the Knight-captain's carbine into his chest. The Knight-Captain looks desperately uncomfortable. ""Brother,"" he says again, pleading.

""Do your duty, Knight-Captain!"" shouts Keepfaith. 

Bornanew takes another step, bodily pushing back the Knight-Captain, still cradling the carbine. Finger on the trigger.",bffi_arrest13:Continue,
BFFIarrest13,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrest12,,"He steps forward again, pushing the barrel of the Knight-Captain's carbine into his chest. The Knight-Captain looks desperately uncomfortable. ""Brother,"" he says again, pleading.

""Do your duty, Knight-Captain!"" shouts Keepfaith. 

Bornanew takes another step, bodily pushing back the Knight-Captain, still cradling the carbine. Finger on the trigger.","bffi_arrestNoMove0:Make no sudden movements
bffi_arrestShotBorn0:Draw your own weapon
bffi_arrestShove0:Push Bornanew aside",
BFFIarrest13bb,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_arrest13
$global.bornanewBadBoy > 3",,"He steps forward again, pushing the barrel of the Knight-Captain's carbine into his chest. The Knight-Captain looks desperately uncomfortable. ""Brother,"" he says again, pleading.

""Do your duty, Knight-Captain!"" shouts Keepfaith. 

Bornanew takes another step, bodily pushing back the Knight-Captain, still cradling the carbine. Finger on the trigger.","bffi_arrestShotBorn0:Draw your own weapon
bffi_arrestShove0:Push Bornanew aside
bffi_arrestNoMove0:Make no sudden movements",
BFFIarrestNoMove0,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestNoMove0,,"A pathetic struggle ensues, Keepfaith's hands locked around the Knight-Captain's, who struggles to keep the weapon under his control.

Bornanew simply watches until, finally, both Curate and Knight-captain tumble into a workdesk, sending papers and tools flying.",bffi_arrestNoMove1:Continue,
BFFIarrestNoMove1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestNoMove1,,"Expressions among the apprentices range from appalled second-hand embarrassment to impish delight.

Red-faced, the Knight-Captain, regains his feet with Subcurate Keepfaith restrained in his arms. There is little dignity remaining for either.

Bornanew, meanwhile, remains standing in a stray beam of sunlight - a product of the clever arrangement of lightwells. The effect places him as the glowing centerpiece to an instructive tableau.

This can't have been happenstance; Bornanew's insistence on pushing forward, toward the light...",bffi_arrestNoMove2:Continue,
BFFIarrestNoMove2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestNoMove2,# TODO show larix?,"Coincidence or performance, the invisible consensus is irrevocably turned against Keepfaith.

""It was under control!"" she screams. ""It would never have been necessary if you Knights attended your duties. You're lax, lax and blind!""

""Come now, sister,"" says the Knight-Captain, leading her away. ""Be not careless with your words, for the Inquisitors shall hear all...""",bffi_arrestOutro1:Continue,
BFFIarrestShotBorn0,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestShotBorn0,"PauseMusic
Call $global.bffi_ref shootEm
AddTextSmall ""Bornanew is shot"" highlight
HideSecondPerson
$global.bornanewShotOnTartessus = true
$global.bornanewShotDuringBFFI = true","The Knight-Captain's eyes go wide, taking in your action.

A shot erupts from the carbine and you are anointed by a spray of blood.",bffi_arrestShotBorn1:Continue,
BFFIarrestShotBorn1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestShotBorn1,,"Horrified, the Knight-Captain shoves Subcurate Keepfaith aside and safeties his weapon. She crashes into a workdesk, papers and tools and dignity scattered all around.

There are screams. Is there a doctor? Orders are shouted. The Knight-Captain is tearing his robe, holding a piece of cloth to Bornanew's wound. The red bubbles up into the white.","bffi_arrestShotBorn2a:Help Bornanew
bffi_arrestShotBorn2b:Restrain the subcurate",
BFFIarrestShotBorn2a,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestShotBorn2a,"$player.bffi_helpedBornanewAfterShotTartessus = true
PlayCustomMusic music_luddite_encounter_friendly","Ignoring the chaos surrounding, you rush to Bornanew's aid, assisting the Knight-Captain in attempting to staunch the flow of blood.

The Knight-Captain appears trained for this, working with grim determination, directing you without hesitation as needed.",bffi_arrestShotBorn3:Continue,
BFFIarrestShotBorn2b,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestShotBorn2b,"$player.bffi_caughtKeepfaithAfterShotTartessus = true
PlayCustomMusic music_luddite_encounter_friendly","Pulling your eyes away from the bloody scene, you see Subcurate Keepfaith realizing that the chaos she has caused presents her with the perfect opportunity to slip away.

It takes just two long strides and you catch her arm. Bornanew's blood is slick on your hand, and she pulls, hard, screaming admonitions but does not manage escape.",bffi_arrestShotBorn3:Continue,
BFFIarrestShotBornEscape,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_arrestShotBorn3
$player.bffi_helpedBornanewAfterShotTartessus","HideSecondPerson
EndConversation DO_NOT_FIRE
ShowImageVisual cathedral_skyline","It is a close thing, that line between life and death. Like the thin line of atmo when looking down upon a breathing planet; nothing more than a razor's edge from the deathly black.

You notice the Knight-Captain's arms are red up to his elbows. And yours, too, as you assist. 

There are shouts, and running footsteps. A doctor arrives, with assistent, who shoves you and the Knight-Captain aside after only the briefest exchange. ",bffi_arrestShotBornEscape1:Continue,
BFFIarrestShotBornEscape2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestShotBornEscape1,,"You stand back, dripping. The Knight-Captain is shaken, and, with a despairing look, fully removes the magazine of his carbine.

The bloody scene is illuminated by a ray of sunlight, a violent tableau. Shocked apprentices are recruited to help carry Bornanew elsewhere. Some kind of on-site infirmary.

You and the Knight-Captain turn toward one another to exchange a look. His eyes are wide.

Subcurate Keepfaith has disappeared.","bffi_arrestOutroEscape:""Find her!""",
BFFIarrestShotBornCaught,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_arrestShotBorn3
$player.bffi_caughtKeepfaithAfterShotTartessus",HideSecondPerson,"The rogue subcurate's shouts are quelled by the horrified faces of her apprentices.

""I had it under control!"" she says, not quite pleading. ""It would never have been necessary if the Knights attended their duties. They're lax, lax and blind!""

Shouts, and running steps. A doctor arrives to take over from the Knight-Captain, who, shaken, stands back from the bloody scene illuminated in a ray of sunlight. Shocked apprentices are recruited to help carry Bornanew elsewhere; some kind of on-site infirmary.",bffi_arrestShotBornCaught2:Continue,
BFFIarrestShotBornCaught2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestShotBornCaught2,"EndConversation DO_NOT_FIRE
HideVisual","The Knight-Captain spots you, finally, and approaches. His arms are red to the elbows, his robes turn and spattered with the blood of his brother Knight.

""Come now, sister,"" he says coldly. ""Be not careless with your words, for the Inquisitors shall hear all of it. All of it.""",bffi_arrestOutroCaught:Continue,
BFFIarrestShotBornDeadCaught,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_arrestShotBorn3
$player.bffi_caughtKeepfaithAfterShotTartessus
$global.bornanewWasShotBySedge","AddTextSmall ""Bornanew is dead"" highlight
HideSecondPerson
EndConversation DO_NOT_FIRE
HideVisual","You know it is over when the Knight-Captain goes quiet and still. His forearms are red with blood. Everywhere, blood, alit by the shaft of sunlight. Pale faces of apprentices look on, horrified.

Bornanew's body, weakened by Sedge's brutal attack, simply cannot hold out. In a matter of seconds, his life is spilled out of him onto the floor of the scriptorium.

""I had it under control,"" Keepfaith says, not quite pleading now. ""It would never have been necessary if the Knights attended their duties. They're lax, lax and blind!""

No one is listening.",bffi_arrestOutroDead:Continue,
BFFIarrestShotBornDead,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_arrestShotBorn3
$player.bffi_helpedBornanewAfterShotTartessus
$global.bornanewWasShotBySedge","AddTextSmall ""Bornanew is dead"" highlight
HideSecondPerson
EndConversation DO_NOT_FIRE
HideVisual","You know it is over when the Knight-Captain goes quiet and still. His forearms are red with blood. Everywhere, blood, alit by the shaft of sunlight. Pale faces of apprentices look on, horrified.

Bornanew's body, weakened by Sedge's brutal attack, simply cannot hold out. In a matter of seconds, his life is spilled out of him onto the floor of the scriptorium.

Distant calls and shouts - a doctor arrives, too late.

Subcurate Keepfaith is nowhere to be seen.",bffi_arrestOutroDead:Continue,
BFFIarrestShotShove0,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestShove0,"PauseMusic
Call $global.bffi_ref shootEm
AddTextSmall ""You are shot"" highlight","You shove into Bornanew, your speed making up for his mass, tumbling him away from the barrel of the gun. 

A shot erupts from the carbine.

Later, you watch a recording of the incident and see your blood anoint an arc of junior assistants of the scriptoria. A fine rain of droplets stains their papers and books.

In the moment, however, the world has become indistinct. A feeling like the familiar drift of zero-g overcomes you.",bffi_arrestShove1:Float upward,
BFFIarrestShotShove1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestShove1,"HideSecondPerson
EndConversation DO_NOT_FIRE
HideVisual","You fall back, ears buzzing, your eyes brought into line with the mural on the ceiling. Painted clouds and stars dance above you, attached to interlocking toothed wheels. The turning spheres of creation, the orbits and movements of celestial mechanics given literal form.

It's funny to you, the spacer, but you cannot laugh.

Your body is not responding to your commands. Your ship is adrift. Fluxed out. Vent.

Darkness.",bffi_arrestOutroPCshot:Sleep dreamless and cold,
,,,,,,
BFFIarrestOutro1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestOutro1,"EndConversation DO_NOT_FIRE
ShowDefaultVisual
$global.bffi_arrestedKeepfaith = true","* * *

The cadre of Luddic Knights guarding the Cathedral of Holy Exodus defer to Bornanew's authority.

Keepfaith is delivered to your shuttle, restrained, and now - away from her small kingdom - is timid but glowering.

""I will be absolved,"" she says. ""You shall witness my righteousness before the end.""

Bornanew shakes his head but does not reply. One of your guards switches on the dampening field so that you will not be troubled by Keepfaith's words.",bffi_arrestOutro2:Return to your $shipOrFleet,
BFFIarrestOutro2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestOutro2,"ShowLargePlanet
ResumeNormalMusic",You return to your $shipOrFleet. After the rogue subcurate is placed in the brig you meet with Bornanew in a briefing room.,"bffi_arrestOutro3:""What now?""",
BFFIarrestOutro3,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestOutro3,"unset $global.bffi_learnedAboutKeepfaith
BeginConversation bornanew
Call $global.bffi_ref updateStage","""We must take her to Hesperus,"" he says. ""To the Knight Inquisitors and their justice.""

He stares out at a display of starry space, subdued.

""I shall submit my evidence, then the Inquisitors will question her before a quorum of authority determined by the severity of her crime. I suspect more than one archcurate shall be required.""","bffi_arrestOutroAskPenance:""Are you not pleased? Won't your penance be complete?""
bffi_arrestCurateEnd:Leave him to his thoughts",
BFFIarrestOutroAskPenance,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestOutroAskPenance,,"He turns to you.

""Pleased? That is difficult. What we have uncovered is deeply concerning. As for my penance,"" he grimaces. ""You have not met the Excubitor Orbis of Hesperus.""

He turns back to the stars.",bffi_arrestCurateEnd:Leave him to his thoughts,
BFFIarrestOutroAskPenanceBB,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_arrestOutroAskPenance
$global.bornanewBadBoy > 2",,"He turns to you.

""Pleased? That is difficult. What we have uncovered is deeply concerning. As for my penance,"" he grimaces. ""The Excubitor Orbis of Hesperus would have me punished for the sins he imagines of the Reverend Archcurate Jaspis, and others who do not fully agree with him besides, I am sure. There will be little wordly relief within his domain. But to there I must return.""

He turns back to the stars.",bffi_arrestCurateEnd:Leave him to his thoughts,
BFFIarrestOutroAskPenanceB,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_arrestOutroAskPenance
$player.metGideonOak",,"He turns to you.

""Pleased? That is difficult. What we have uncovered is deeply concerning. As for my penance,"" he grimaces. ""You have met Excubitor Orbis Oak, yes?""","bffi_arrestOutroPenUnderstand:""Yes. I understand your concern.""
bffi_arrestOutroPenForgive:""Maybe he'll be in a forgiving mood after you deliver a traitor and the false relic.""",
BFFIarrestOutroAskPenUnderstand,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestOutroPenUnderstand,,"He nods, then turns back to the stars.",bffi_arrestCurateEnd:Leave $global.jethroName to his thoughts,
BFFIarrestOutroAskPenForgive,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestOutroPenForgive,,"""Maybe,"" he says. He is quiet for a moment, nods, then turns back to the stars.",bffi_arrestCurateEnd:Leave $global.jethroName to his thoughts,
BFFIarrestCurateEnd,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestCurateEnd,"EndConversation DO_NOT_FIRE
