$player.bffi_gotShotOnTartessus","EndConversation DO_NOT_FIRE
ShowDefaultVisual
FireAll PopulateOptions
ResumeNormalMusic","You dream of stars, but they flit and dance in the tapestry of the night to music you can't quite hear.",,
BFFIarrestOutroPCshot,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestOutroPCshot,"ShowLargePlanet
FireBest BFFIarrestOutroPCshotArroyoCheck","* * *

You awake to the familiar hum of your flagship, in orbit.

For a moment, your mind drifts without context. A machine chirps helpfully somewhere.

Your vision is a blur, slowly resolving like a bad comm-link signal running poorly-adjusted inference algorithms.

There's a human-shaped blob. The details come rushing back.","bffi_arrestOutroPCshotA:""$global.jethroName?""
bffi_arrestOutroPCshotB:""I feel like I've been shot.""
bffi_arrestOutroPCshotC:""...did you catch her?""
bffi_arrestOutroPCshotArroyo:""...Arroyo?""",
BFFIarrestOutroPCshotArroyoCheck,BFFIarrestOutroPCshotArroyoCheck,!$global.metArroyo,RemoveOption bffi_arrestOutroPCshotArroyo,,,
BFFIarrestOutroPCshotA,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestOutroPCshotA,"BeginConversation bornanew
ResumeNormalMusic","The shape leans forward and turns into Bornanew.

""Yes, captain,"" he says. ""And you are alive, thank Providence. And your medical team, of course.""",bffi_arrestOutroPCshot2:Continue,
BFFIarrestOutroPCshotB,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestOutroPCshotB,"BeginConversation bornanew
ResumeNormalMusic","At least, that's what you try to say. What leaves your mouth is an indeterminate mush of phonemes.

The shape leans forward and turns into Bornanew.

""You've been shot,"" he says. ""Try not to move.""",bffi_arrestOutroPCshot2:Continue,
BFFIarrestOutroPCshotC,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestOutroPCshotC,"BeginConversation bornanew
ResumeNormalMusic","At least, that's what you try to say. What leaves your mouth is an indetermine mush of phonemes.

The shape leans forward and turns into Bornanew.

""Good morning, captain,"" he says. ""By local reference, anyway.""",bffi_arrestOutroPCshot2:Continue,
BFFIarrestOutroPCshotArroyoA,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestOutroPCshotArroyo,"BeginConversation bornanew
ResumeNormalMusic","The shape leans forward and turns into Bornanew.

""It's just me. Jethro,"" he says. ""Good morning captain. By ah, local reference, anyway.""",bffi_arrestOutroPCshot2:Continue,
BFFIarrestOutroPCshotArroyoAj,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_arrestOutroPCshotArroyo
$global.jethroName == ""Jeff""","BeginConversation bornanew
ResumeNormalMusic","The shape leans forward and turns into Bornanew.

""It's just me. Jeth... um, Jeff,"" he says. ""Good morning captain. By ah, local reference, anyway.""",bffi_arrestOutroPCshot2:Continue,
BFFIarrestOutroPCshot2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestOutroPCshot2,$global.bffi_arrestedKeepfaith = true,"""Knight-Captain Larix applied first aid to you."" Bornanew speaks softly. ""I do think he saved your life."" 

He leans back. ""And I, I managed to catch Keepfaith before she could flee. She's in the brig, now. And no longer a subcurate. The Reverend Archcurate of the Cathedral of Holy Exodus - Bywater, his name is - was quite distraught about the shooting. He revoked her curateship.""

He pauses a moment to let everything sink in.",bffi_arrestOutroPCshot3:Attempt to speak,
BFFIarrestOutroPCshot3,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestOutroPCshot3,"unset $global.bffi_learnedAboutKeepfaith
Call $global.bffi_ref updateStage","""Please, not yet,"" he says. ""Be at ease.""

""Keepfaith should be given over to the Knight-Inquisitors, on Hesperus. She still must be investigated for her crimes and put before a quorum of appropriate authority for judgement."" He pauses. ""Her other crimes, I mean. We have a score of witnesses for the shooting, and...""

He trails off, knowing little need be said of that just now. Another voice speaks, from outside the room - the medical recovery bay.",bffi_arrestOutroPCshot4:Do not attempt to speak,
BFFIarrestOutroPCshot4,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestOutroPCshot4,"$global.bornanewBadBoy--
AdjustRepPerson bornanew FRIENDLY 5
$player.bffi_gotShotOnTartessus","Bornanew nods at some instruction then, standing up, looks back to you.

""Thank you, captain. For my life, again.""",bffi_arrestCurateEnd:Sleep for a while,
BFFIarrestOutroEscape,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestOutroEscape,$global.bffi_keepfaithEscaped = true,"You are of little use in the search, being unfamiliar with the cathedral. The Knight-Captain whose name you almost forgot to ask - ""Larix,"" he said, ""Knight-Captain Dejan Larix"" before shouting orders to a hastily assembled squad of Knight-Novices, all obviously far younger than Bornanew.

Bornanew, for one, is stabilized in the infirmary, part of the sprawling church infrastructure spilling from the cathedral. ",bffi_arrestOutroInjured:Continue,
BFFIarrestOutroCaught,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestOutroCaught,$global.bffi_arrestedKeepfaith = true,"* * *

You are nearly forgotten in the chaos. Before long, a meek apprentice directs you to the offices of the Luddic Knights where you make a statement and discuss the incident with the Knight-Captain. You only just remember to ask him his name. 

""Larix,"" he says, ""Knight-Captain Dejan Larix"" before shouting orders to a hastily assembled squad of Knight-novices, all obviously far younger than Bornanew.

Who, for one, is stabilized in the infirmary, part of the sprawling church infrastructure spilling from the cathedral. ",bffi_arrestOutroInjured:Continue,
BFFIarrestOutroInjured,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestOutroInjured,"HideSecondPerson
ShowImageVisual cathedral_skyline","The resident physician is more practical than traditional, and sees fit to consult with your own chief medical officer. A patient transfer is arranged, and even a special dispensation (granted by the embarrassed archcurate) to land a shuttle on a field near to the Cathedral of Holy Exodus.

The implicit use of technologies which would be awkward to employ on Church grounds to save Bornanew's life is left unsaid.",bffi_arrestOutroInjured2:Return to your $shipOrFleet in orbit,
BFFIarrestOutroInjured2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestOutroInjured2,"ShowLargePlanet
$global.bffi_arrestedKeepfaith = true","The cadre of Luddic Knights guarding the Cathedral of Holy Exodus defer to Bornanew's authority, despite his unconsciousness.

Keepfaith, just Cedra now that her subcurateship has been summarily revoked by order of the archcurate, is delivered to you flagship. She is restrained, and now - away from her small kingdom - timid, though still glowering.

""I will be absolved,"" she says hoarsely. ""You shall witness my righteousness before the end.""

One of your guards closes the brig door, its weight silent.",bffi_arrestOutroInjured3:Check on Bornanew,
BFFIarrestOutroInjured2escape,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_arrestOutroInjured2
$player.bffi_helpedBornanewAfterShotTartessus","ShowLargePlanet
$global.bffi_keepfaithEscapedTartessus = true","The cadre of Luddic Knights guarding the Cathedral of Holy Exodus defer to Bornanew's authority, despite his unconsciousness.

Keepfaith, just Cedra now that her subcurateship has been summarily revoked by order of the archcurate, is nowhere to be found. You can only speculate that she called upon her Pather contacts for assistance.",bffi_arrestOutroInjured3escape:Check on Bornanew,
BFFIarrestOutroInjured3,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestOutroInjured3,,"It is some time before Bornanew regains consciousness.

Your chief medical officer hovers nearby, giving you a stern look. You know you will not be allowed to overtrouble their patient.","bffi_arrestOutroInjured4:""What now?""",
BFFIarrestOutroInjured3escape,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestOutroInjured3escape,,"It is some time before Bornanew regains consciousness.

Your chief medical officer hovers nearby, giving you a stern look. You know you will not be allowed to overtrouble their patient.","bffi_arrestOutroInjured4:""What now?""",
BFFIarrestOutroInjured4,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestOutroInjured4,"ResumeNormalMusic
unset $global.bffi_learnedAboutKeepfaith
BeginConversation bornanew
Call $global.bffi_ref updateStage","Bornanew is pale, his breathing shallow. ""To Hesperus,"" he says. ""To the Knights of Ludd.""

""Inquisitors,"" he whispers, then carefully turns his head toward a display of starry space and the orb of Tartessus. ""Justice."" 

He closes his eyes. Mouth open, still breathing.

You feel a movement in the air. Your chief medical officer hovers meaningfully, waiting for you to choose to leave, now.",bffi_arrestCurateEnd:Leave,
BFFIarrestOutroInjured4escape,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestOutroInjured4escape,"ResumeNormalMusic
unset $global.bffi_learnedAboutKeepfaith
BeginConversation bornanew
Call $global.bffi_ref updateStage","Bornanew is pale, his breathing shallow. ""To Hesperus,"" he says. ""To the Knights of Ludd.""

""Excubitor Orbis,"" he whispers, then carefully turns his head toward a display of starry space and the orb of Tartessus. ""Penance."" 

He closes his eyes. Mouth open, still breathing.

You feel a movement in the air. Your chief medical officer hovers meaningfully, waiting for you to choose to leave, now.",bffi_arrestCurateEnd:Leave,
BFFIarrestOutroDead,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestOutroDead,"HideVisual
PlayCustomMusic music_luddite_shrine","Later, back on your flagship in orbit, you find instructions on Bornanew's cheap datapad.

""If you hear these words, then I am returned to the arms of Providence,"" it begins.

You are to take his mortal remains to Hesperus, to the Knights of Ludd, so that it may rest with the fellow-walkers he knew for only a short time.",bffi_arrestOutroDead2:Continue,
BFFIarrestOutroDead2caught,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_arrestOutroDead2
$player.bffi_caughtKeepfaithAfterShotTartessus",,"* * *

You are nearly forgotten in the chaos. Before long, a meek apprentice directs you to the offices of the Luddic Knights where you make a statement and discuss the incident with the Knight-Captain. You only just remember to ask him his name. 

""Larix,"" he says, ""Knight-Captain Dejan Larix"" before shouting orders to a hastily assembled squad of Knight-novices, all obviously far younger than Bornanew is.

Than Bornanew was.",bffi_arrestOutroDead3:Continue,
BFFIarrestOutroDead2,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == bffi_arrestOutroDead2
$player.bffi_helpedBornanewAfterShotTartessus",,"The Knight-Captain helped organize a search for Keepfaith.

You had almost forgotten to ask his name - ""Larix,"" he said, drained of emotion. ""Dejan Larix.""

""For the small moment I knew him, I knew he was a good man. A good Knight. Damned but that it had to be my hand..."" he trailed off then, hiding his eyes.

You left him to return to your shuttle.",bffi_arrestOutroDead3:Continue,
BFFIarrestOutroDead3,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_arrestOutroDead3,"HideVisual
unset $global.bffi_learnedAboutKeepfaith
$global.bffi_returnBornanewBody = true
Call $global.bffi_ref updateStage
$global.bffi_returnBodyWithoutPrisoner = true","The Pather plot is foiled, perhaps, for now.

Cedra Keepfaith, a murderer before a score of witnesses, was stripped of her rank before the set of the sun by Archcurate Bywater of the Cathedral of Holy Exodus.

The Knight-Inquisitors will pursue their brand of justice against her, you are assured.

Bornanew's quest is over.",bffi_arrestCurateEnd:Leave,
