BFFIdeliverToOakBodyOnly,BFFIdeliverToOakMore,$global.bffi_returnBodyWithoutPrisoner score:10,,"The simple spacer's coffin holding Bornanew's body is loaded onto the shuttle. One of the spacers briefly puts their hands together, head bowed, after setting it down. A small sign of Luddic devotion.",,
BFFIdeliverToOak2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_deliverToOak2,ShowDefaultVisual,"Your shuttle approaches an almost floral arrangement of pads set in the midst of a former mine pit.

Heavy doors open from the rockface inviting your landing party into the dimly lit hangar beyond.

A score of armored Knights march forth - like small, segmented dolls compared with the scale of the door, but as you approach you note their height. They must be the tallest farm-fed children of Gilead and Tartessus, all aclad in polished white armor, half-capes slack in the near-vacuum.

They turn precisely aside, weapons held vertical. ",bffi_deliverToOak3:Enter the hangar,
BFFIdeliverToOak3,DialogOptionSelected,$option == bffi_deliverToOak3,"BeginConversation oak
$player.metGideonOak = true
SetPersonHidden oak false
$option = bffi_deliverToOak3born 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","You enter, the guards reverse their process, and the hangar is pressurized. 

A far door cracks open, casting a long wedge of light. Spots snap on, converted shuttles and fightercraft loom in all corners.

The Excubitor Orbis enters. 

Gideon Oak is a brick of a man, squat but powerful. Perhaps the product of a forgotten high-G world. He is accompanied by a weedy clerk.",,
