# AVIPT - Angry VIP Transport,,,,,,
AVIPTblurbBar,avipt_blurbBar,!$market.toldAVIPTtoGoAway,,A very well-dressed $manOrWoman is regaling the subdued bartender with complaints about a missed transport of some kind.,,
AVIPToptionBar,avipt_optionBar,!$market.toldAVIPTtoGoAway,,,avipt_textBar1:Try to calm the well-dressed $manOrWoman bothering the bartender,
AVIPTtextBar1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == avipt_textBar1,,"You manage to insert yourself into the $manOrWoman's field of attention with a friendly greeting. The bartender gives you a thankful nod behind $hisOrHer back.

""These people, these space-pilots, are so addled by rocket fuel and zero-g that they simply cannot comprehend respectful! Customer! Service!""

Each of these three words is accompanied by an open handed slap on the bar. You watch as a small splash leaps over the rim of an otherwise untouched drink at each impact.","avipt_textBar2:Perform an act of leadership
avipt_textBarDecline:Disengage while you still can",
AVIPTtextBar2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == avipt_textBar2,"$missionId = avipt
SetTextHighlights $avipt_reward $avipt_reward $avipt_timelimit $avipt_marketName terrible
Call $avipt_ref showMap ""Destination: $avipt_marketName""","You put on a look of stern and stoic authority, that look your bridge officers whisper about as your 'captain face' when they think you can't hear them.

This seems to do the trick.

This individual - wealthy, important, and well-connected, by their own description - paid $avipt_reward credits upfront for priority transport within $avipt_timelimit days to $avipt_marketName, but the ship left port early last night without a word for reasons you cannot fathom. This is 'a shocking disgrace' which 'besmirches the already dubious name of all space-captainry'.

You nod, your expression suitably grim at hearing of such terrible treatment.","avipt_textBarAccept:Offer to transport the VIP for the same fee
avipt_textBarDecline:Try to withdraw from the conversation
avipt_textBarDeclineRude:Explain to the VIP that they probably deserved this",
AVIPTtextBarAccept,DialogOptionSelected,$option == avipt_textBarAccept,"BarCMD accept $missionId
FireBest ContactPostAccept
BarCMD returnFromEvent true","Your offer manages to stop the $manOrWoman from talking at you for several seconds as $heOrShe considers your demeanor and your offer. 

""I accept,"" $heOrShe says with the enunciation of royalty, ""Though I shall only be paying after we arrive at $avipt_marketName. And I shall require some of your crew to handle my luggage. I need not remind you that these are my valuable personal goods, not crates of... of common space-bolts to be tossed about by half-drunken dockworkers.""

As you confirm final details over a free round from the bartender, you consider which of your junior officers to assign to babysitting duty...",,
AVIPTtextBarDecline,DialogOptionSelected,$option == avipt_textBarDecline,,"You stand as if at attention, give the alleged VIP a formal farewell, and march to the other end of the bar without a backward glance. 

$HeOrShe is too confused by your formality to express outrage until it is too late and you are well out of range.

From the corner of your eye, you can see the well-dressed $manOrWoman slowly start working $himOrHerself into another, slightly different rage.",contact_declineBarNoContinue:Avert your eyes before you are forced to re-engage,
AVIPTtextBarDeclineRude,DialogOptionSelected,$option == avipt_textBarDeclineRude,"$market.toldAVIPTtoGoAway = true 30
AdjustRep faction.id INHOSPITABLE -1","The VIP stares at you, appalled at your manners. Behind, the bartender is doing an admirable job suppressing a grin. 

The well-dressed $manOrWoman, confronted directly, seems to be at a complete loss. $HisOrHer mouth opens, then closes, opens again - and then $heOrShe storms out of the bar. 

There's a pause as your ears adjust to the relatively muted din of the establishment before cheers and hurrahs erupt from the other patrons.",contact_declineBarNoContinue:Continue,
AVIPTcheckCompletion,MarketPostDock,"$market.avipt_target score:100
Call $market.avipt_ref updateData
!$avipt_noCompleteShown
!$avipt_didEnding",$market.avipt_completed = true 0,,avipt_deliverContinue:Continue,
AVIPTcompletedButNoDocking,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == avipt_deliverContinue
!$avipt_noCompleteShown
$tradeMode == NONE","$avipt_noCompleteShown = true 0
FireBest MarketPostDock",You're unable to safely deliver your very important passenger right now.,marketArrivalEventContinue:Continue,
AVIPTcheckCompletionCont,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == avipt_deliverContinue
$tradeMode != NONE","$avipt_didEnding = true 0
Call $avipt_ref updateStage
FireBest MarketPostDock","You meet the VIP on the way out the airlock to a waiting private shuttle. It seems the politick thing to do, especially because the promised payment just cleared.

""The commander here,"" $heOrShe indicates the officer you assigned to the VIP (an officer-trainee, in fact, who drew the short straw and was given a fancy uniform), ""Performed acceptably, such that I might endorse a commendation.""

With that, $heOrShe says merely, ""Captain,"" then turns on $hisOrHer heel and exits the ship, the small fleet of $hisOrHer luggage wheeling itself behind obediently. The airlock seals mercifully shut.",,
,,,,,,
"# MOTR 
# Mercs On The Run bar event",,,,,,
MOTRblurbBar,motr_blurbBar,!$market.arrestedMercs,,A table of tattooed marine mercenaries bearing mil-grade cybermods are drinking alarming amounts of liquor.,,
MOTRoptionBar,motr_optionBar,!$market.arrestedMercs,,,motr_textBar1:Join the table of tattooed mercs and see if their contract is up,
MOTRstart,DialogOptionSelected,$option == motr_textBar1,"$missionId = motr
Highlight $motr_numberOfMarines $motr_priceText
DoCanAffordCheck $motr_price motr_accept false
FireAll MOTRcrewCheck","You prove yourself worthy of association by partaking in a round of 'Atmo Drops', a drink centered around consuming eye-watering liquor as quickly as possible.

The mercs are drunk, for sure, but composed enough to speak around the details of why they're being investigated by local authorities.

After a couple of the mercs head up to order a round of 'Orbital Bombardments' their leader pulls you aside and sketches out a proposal. ""We've got $motr_numberOfMarines suits, experienced operators. We can fight in vac or atmo, one to five gee."" He smirks at the look you give, ""Okay, three. Four if it's quick and there's a bonus."" A scarred hand dismisses this, ""Details!""

""What matters is I'll offer our contract for $motr_priceText credits. Practically charity, isn't it? Put us to work, or sell it off elsewhere, doesn't matter to me if you can get us outta this fix. What'dya say?""","motr_accept:Buy the mercenary marine contract and sneak them off $entity.name
motr_declineDrink:Decline the proposal, but stay for an 'Orbital Bombardment' to soften the blow
contact_declineBarNoContinue:Decline",
MOTRcrewCheck,MOTRcrewCheck,$player.crewRoom < $motr_numberOfMarines,"SetEnabled motr_accept false
SetTooltip motr_accept ""Requires at least $motr_numberOfMarines free crew berths.""",,,
MOTRaccept,DialogOptionSelected,$option == motr_accept,"$option = contact_acceptBar 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","Some clever device provided by the mercs convinces the port authority automated scanners that two particular cargo containers are half-filled with mildly radioactive silicate gravel and nothing else.

Your logistics officer sneaks them aboard your $shipOrFleet without inconvenience.",,
MOTRplayerColonyAccept,DialogOptionSelected,$option == motr_playerColonyAccept,"$option = contact_acceptBar 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","With a word, any objections from the port authority disappear and your logistics officer arranges to have the mercs, looking worse from the night of drinking, board your $shipOrFleet the next morning.",,
