TseenKeAskRao,PopulateOptions,"$id == heg_ga_officer
#$global.metOrcusRao
!$saidRao",,,"tseenKe_askRao:""What's your impression of Admiral Orcus Rao?""",
TseenKeAskDaud,PopulateOptions,"$id == heg_ga_officer
#$player.metDaud
!$saidDaud",,,"tseenKe_askDaud:""What do you think of the High Hegemon, Baikal Daud?""",
TseenKeAskRao2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == tseenKe_askRao,$saidRao = true,"""Admiral Rao?"" Tseen Ke rubs his chin. ""He's a bit of a fancy lad, is Rao. Out of Eventide, did you know? Of course you do, it's right there in the name, ha-ha. They're rich, beyond rich. He's not a bad one though, not bad.""

""He does things his own way to win, and he's won plenty."" He lowers his voice - not that it particularly matters over the comms-link, which automatically compensates for volume.

""I tell you, if he weren't a Rao...""",tseenKe_askRao2:Continue,
TseenKeAskRao3,DialogOptionSelected,$option == tseenKe_askRao2,FireAll PopulateOptions,"""If he weren't a Rao, he wouldn't have got away with half of what he did. It'd be court martial, stripped of command and rank. If I tried what he did, my only command would be over disinfection duty for the next 10 cycles.""

He shrugs. ""That's how it is though. Like I said, he's not bad.""",,
TseenKeAskDaud2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == tseenKe_askDaud,"FireAll TseenKeAskDaudOpts
$saidDaud = true","""What is this question, did INTSEC send you to check my loyalty? Ha-ha."" 

Does the jocular affect cover an edge in his voice?","

",
TseenKeAskDaudOptA,TseenKeAskDaudOpts,"!$gaveINTSECopinion
!$gaveDaudOpinion",,,"tseenKe_askDaudSelA:""Ha-ha, of course not."" (stare intently)",
TseenKeAskDaudOptB,TseenKeAskDaudOpts,"!$saidINTSECreally
!$gaveDaudOpinion",,,"tseenKe_askDaudSelB:""Do they really send INTSEC to check on your loyalty?""",
TseenKeAskDaudOptC,TseenKeAskDaudOpts,!$gaveDaudOpinion,,,"tseenKe_askDaudSelC:""No, I'm really interested in your perspective on the man.""",
TseenKeAskDaudOptD,TseenKeAskDaudOpts,"$gaveDaudOpinion
!$saidDaudOp",,"""How about yourself, captain?"" He turns the question around with cheerful bluster.

""Are you up or down on the Old Man? Not like we get a vote on it, ha-ha.""","tseenKe_askDaudOpA:""It's not my place to judge.""
tseenKe_askDaudOpB:""He's practical. Knows how to keep his feet on the deck.""
tseenKe_askDaudOpC:""He should be bolder. The Hegemony has great power, he should use it!""
tseenKe_askDaudOpD:""I think he's in over his head. Maybe it's his background, maybe his character.""
tseenKe_askDaudOpE:""Honestly, I could do a better job as High Hegemon.""
tseenKe_askDaudOpF:""Someone like Orcus Rao should be in charge. He knows when to bend the rules.""",
TseenKeAskDaudOptE,TseenKeAskDaudOpts,"$gaveDaudOpinion
!$global.metOrcusRao",RemoveOption tseenKe_askDaudOpF,,,
TseenKeAskDaudOptF,TseenKeAskDaudOpts,$saidDaudOp,FireAll PopulateOptions,"""Let's leave the old man alone,"" he says. ""He's got enough problems.""",,
TseenKeAskDaudSelA,DialogOptionSelected,$option == tseenKe_askDaudSelA,"$gaveINTSECopinion = true
FireAll TseenKeAskDaudOpts","""Ha... ha.""

His half-hearted chuckle dies into an awkward silence.

""Captain, you're not... no,"" he shakes his head. ""You were saying something about the Hegemon?""",,
TseenKeAskDaudSelB,DialogOptionSelected,$option == tseenKe_askDaudSelB,"$saidINTSECreally = true
$gaveINTSECopinion = true
FireAll TseenKeAskDaudOpts","""They, uh..."" He glances to the side.

""Well, not like that. INTSEC does... I believe track certain queries, communications, and so on to combat, you know, the usual sort of thing. Terrorists, mutiny, treason...""

He trails off with a distant look. Then shakes his head.

""They're a bunch of grim sticks, that's a truth for you. But they're not going to bother battering my hatch for making a joke or two. If they did, half the brass and all the hands'd be traitors, ha-ha.""",,
TseenKeAskDaudSelC,DialogOptionSelected,$option == tseenKe_askDaudSelC,"$gaveDaudOpinion = true
FireAll TseenKeAskDaudOpts","""Ah, he's my Hegemon!"" He thumps his chest for emphasis.

""Old Man Daud came up from the bottom of Chicomoztoc and climbed all the way to the top. Didn't matter what the aristos on Eventide thought, there was a war on, and he went about winning it. Not on his lonesome, of course, but it was him that saved the big Mozzy. Without Mozzy, there's no Hegemony. Without Mozzy, there's no Persean Sector, no future at all. That's not something to shake your head at.""",,
TseenKeAskDaudOpA,DialogOptionSelected,$option == tseenKe_askDaudOpA,"$saidDaudOp = true
FireAll TseenKeAskDaudOpts","""Oh, ho- you're a diplomat now, are you? Suit yourself.""",,
TseenKeAskDaudOpB,DialogOptionSelected,$option == tseenKe_askDaudOpB,"$saidDaudOp = true
FireAll TseenKeAskDaudOpts","""Aye, that's right!"" Caliban thumps his console. ""That's why he's the old man! None of those flighty notions aristos and academicians love dreaming up.""",,
TseenKeAskDaudOpC,DialogOptionSelected,$option == tseenKe_askDaudOpC,,"""Well..."" Caliban rubs his head. ""You're right on that, the Hegemony- we've got the guns, the best minds to aim 'em, and the best hands to fire 'em!""

""And,"" he grins, ""If they're not the best, no matter. We've got more of all of 'em than anyone else in the big Mozzy alone!""

""As for the old man..."" He settles down a little as your subtle criticism of Daud sinks in. ""See, even if we've got more than anyone, he cares about us, right? He won't throw us away. The aristos might be inclined, but we're his people.""","tseenKe_askDaudOpC2:""You don't think sacrifices are ever necessary?""",
TseenKeAskDaudOpC2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == tseenKe_askDaudOpC2,"$saidDaudOp = true
FireAll TseenKeAskDaudOpts","He sits back, puffs his cheeks out and blows air. As if to dispense with the heavy implications.

""That's above my pay-grade, captain. And I'm thankful for it."" A grim look crosses his face. ""If Daud asks it, I'll do it. That much I'll say.""",,
TseenKeAskDaudOpD,DialogOptionSelected,$option == tseenKe_askDaudOpD,"$saidDaudOp = true
FireAll TseenKeAskDaudOpts","""Captain,"" Caliban shakes his head. ""I don't think that's fair to the old man.""

""Now, you're entitled to your opinion on the matter, don't get me wrong. That's part of the Hegemony, we can have our own thoughts and our words- within reasonable limits considering the emergency of course.""

""But Daud? He's given everything and made the best of a bad situation, and,"" he pre-emptively raises a hand to ward off any objections. ""He's done it under pressure.""",,
TseenKeAskDaudOpE,DialogOptionSelected,$option == tseenKe_askDaudOpE,"$saidDaudOp = true
FireAll TseenKeAskDaudOpts","""Ha-ha! Could you now? I've heard that said often enough in the mess over one thing or another.""

""Those are easy words when there's a logistics mixup or you're on the short end of command policy,"" Caliban says, taking on a philosophical tone. ""But to be up there and have to make the call that's most right for all the millions? The higher you are, the more someone's always on the short end of your decision.""",,
TseenKeAskDaudOpE2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == tseenKe_askDaudOpE2,"$saidDaudOp = true
FireAll TseenKeAskDaudOpts"," ""Lot of stress, that. No right decision, sometimes. It makes enemies no matter what you do, sometimes."" He shakes his head. ""No, I'm best pleased where Command decides I should be. My problems are small and I can set 'em aside after a liter of beer and get a good sleep.""

""Hear me, captain,"" he looks at you more seriously. ""You don't want that.""",,
TseenKeAskDaudOpF,DialogOptionSelected,$option == tseenKe_askDaudOpF,"$saidDaudOp = true
FireAll TseenKeAskDaudOpts","""Ohhh, well now..."" He rubs his chin. ""He's a bit of a fancy lad, is Admiral Rao. Though not a bad one, not bad.""

""Maybe when it's the old man's time to step aside,"" Caliban speaks with a shrug. ""Rao wouldn't be so bad, maybe.""",,
