ZGRthreatTechAskDone,ZGRaskQuestionsOpts,$askedAnyQuestion,,,"zgr_askQuestionsHubDone:""That's all I wanted to ask.""",
ZGRthreatTechAskNM,ZGRaskQuestionsOpts,!$askedAnyQuestion,,,"zgr_askQuestionsHubDone:""Actually, never mind.""",
ZGRthreatTechAskDone2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == zgr_askQuestionsHubDone,FireAll PopulateOptions,"""Good,"" she says.",,
ZGRthreatTechAskNone,ZGRaskQuestionsOpts,$noQuestions,"$doneWithQuestions = true 0
FireAll PopulateOptions","""You've asked quite enough for today,"" she says. ""Captain.""",,
ZGRthreatTechAskThreatDo1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == zgr_askQuestionsThreatDo,"$askedAnyQuestion = true 0
$askedThreatDo = true
FireAll ZGRaskQuestionsOpts","""Research and development,"" she says. Her expression isn't quite a smirk.

""These components are obviously derived from a neglected branch of Domain-era technology. This makes them fundamentally human technology. The path to profitable exploitation is fundamentally open, albeit complex. The Tri-Tachyon corporation is ideally placed to exploit them.""",,
ZGRthreatTechAskThreatAre1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == zgr_askQuestionsThreatAre,"$askedAnyQuestion = true 0
$askedThreatAre = true
FireAll ZGRaskQuestionsOpts","""In the simplest terms,"" her voice contains more than a hint of condescension, ""they are autonomous self-fabricating, self-modifying constructs derived from ancient Domain designs. Their intent, so far as they could be said to have intent, is destructive toward our technological base.""

""'Why' is a more difficult question.""

Her dead eyes move oddly. ""I find it amusing that the Luddics would recoil in horror, but they could not find a better ally to their cause.""",,
ZGRthreatTechAskThreatAI1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == zgr_askQuestionsThreatAI,"$askedThreatAIwar = true
$askedAnyQuestion = true 0
FireAll ZGRaskQuestionsOpts","""These are not artificial intelligences,"" she says decisively.

""Not that such distinction is necessary to Hegemony regulators. Whatever future war the Hegemony initiates, whatever new oppressions they conceive, it will be a consequence of leadership as paranoid as their masses are ignorant.""

""Besides,"" she says, self-satisfied, ""if I am right about everything, there will be no need for a war.""",,
ZGRthreatTechAskThreatAlive1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == zgr_askQuestionsThreatAlive,"$askedThreatAlive = true
$askedAnyQuestion = true 0","""Is a machine alive? Is a virus?"" She pauses for a fraction of a second before providing her own answer.

""I don't care.""",zgr_askQuestionsThreatAlive2:Continue,
ZGRthreatTechAskThreatAlive2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == zgr_askQuestionsThreatAlive2,FireAll ZGRaskQuestionsOpts,"""Functionally the 'Threat' phenomenon demonstrates no attempt to present a sense of selfhood, collective or otherwise. What passes for communication is hostile and garbled; the loose ends of automatic warnings and obsolete Domain decrees. If it is conscious in any form, it is impossibly solipsistic.""

""Which is just as well,"" the Director produces a robotic half-smile. ""It will be a better tool that way.""",,
ZGRmonsterTechAskMonsterDo1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == zgr_askQuestionsMonsterDo,"$askedAnyQuestion = true 0
$askedMonsterDo = true
FireAll ZGRaskQuestionsOpts","""Research and development."" 

The Director releases a deliberate breath.

""We know it isn't human. We know it is powerful. The return on investment, therefore, is beyond human imagination.""

She looks satisfied with the thought.",,
ZGRmonsterTechAskMonsterAre1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == zgr_askQuestionsMonsterAre,"$askedAnyQuestion = true 0
$askedMonsterAre = true
FireAll ZGRaskQuestionsOpts","""That is speculation for the research division. Or perhaps you would care to ask a philosopher? Or a curate?"" This last idea appears to amuse her, insofar as she is capable of expressing that, or any, emotion.

""My interest is in what these specimens, these phenomena, can DO. For me. Or the Company.""

She pulls her glassy eyes back to the comm-link. 

""For humanity. At least that small percentage of it willing to accept the radical and necessary future.""",,
,,,,,,
# ZGR first visit,,,,,,
ZGRpreFirstVisitGreeting,PickGreeting,"$id == glamor_rotanev score:1000
$player.receivedGlamorRotanevInvite
!$player.didZGRfirstMeeting","SetShortcut cutCommLink ""ESCAPE""","The link settles on feed of volatiles futures scrolling across the crest of the Tri-Tachyon corporation for just a moment before the comm-link connects you with a perfectly coiffed junior secretary.

""The Tri-Tachyon Corporation welcomes you to Eochu Bres. Their smile is uncannily bright. May we presume you wish to accept Director Glamor-Rotanev's invitation?""","preVisitZGR_resp1:""Yes, I'd like to hear her proposal.""
cutCommLinkPolite:Cut the comm link",
ZGRpreVisitResp1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == preVisitZGR_resp1,"$global.firstGlamorRotanevVisitInvite = true
SetShortcut cutCommLink ""ESCAPE""","""Fantastic. A priority flight path has been pre-approved for your convenience. The Tri-Tachyon Corporation is pleased to wish you a most profitable meeting with the Director of Special Acquisitions.""

The uncanny smile re-appears, perfectly, once more. It's a little unsettling.","ZGR_visitOptDirect:Take a shuttle to visit Director of Special Acquisitions Glamor-Rotanev
cutCommLinkPolite:Cut the comm link",
ZGRpreVisitResp1Hostile,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == preVisitZGR_resp1
$faction.isHostile","$global.firstGlamorRotanevVisitInvite = true
SetShortcut cutCommLink ""ESCAPE""","""Fantastic."" The face maintains an uncanny smile. ""The Director is most eager to meet you.""

An apologetic - but not guilty - expression forms. ""Unfortunately, the automated defenses of the Tri-Tachyon Corporation have flagged your ID as a hostile and your shuttle would be gunned down upon approach. Please contact customer service to resolve this misunderstanding.""

""We hope you have a pleasant and profitable day.""

The smile re-appears.",cutCommLinkPolite:Cut the comm link,
ZGRfirstVisitOption,PopulateOptions,"$hasMarket
$market.id == eochu_bres
$menuState == main
$global.firstGlamorRotanevVisitInvite
!$player.didZGRfirstMeeting",FireBest ZGRfirstVisitOptionCheck,,2:ZGR_visitOptDirect:Take a shuttle to visit Director of Special Acquisitions Glamor-Rotanev,
ZGRfirstVisitOptionCheck,ZGRfirstVisitOptionCheck,"$faction.isHostile
$player.transponderOn","SetEnabled ZGR_visitOptDirect false
SetTooltip ZGR_visitOptDirect ""You have been flagged as a hostile by Tri-Tachyon automated defenses and would be gunned down upon approach.""",,,
ZGRfirstVisitStart,DialogOptionSelected,$option == ZGR_visitOptDirect,ShowLargePlanet,"Your shuttle descends into the young atmosphere of Eochu Bres, through towering battlements of clouds. A spray of rain darkens your viewport for a moment before it is wiped clean by the heat and speed of your descent.

The flight path immediately deviates from the general approach corridor which had started ticking off minor use-fees from the Tri-Tachyon owned flight control: general volume access fee, priority flight lane fee, service fee, customer satisfaction insurance charge, advertisement bypass fee.

The notifications self-delete, their fees automatically refunded, as the towering central arcologies of Xanadu emerge from the mist.",ZGR_firstVisitIntro1:Continue,
ZGRfirstVisitIntro1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == ZGR_firstVisitIntro1,ShowImageVisual eochu_bres_landing,"Jagged mountain peaks ring the horizon. Gleaming monoliths glitter, spears of capital upthrust through the glowering flesh of the world. Skyarco II grows before you, prismatic.

Your shuttle alights on a landing pad held at some distance from the facade by an airy support rib. It looks impossibly thin, but on touch down feels as solid as a coherent M-type asteroid.",ZGR_firstVisitIntro2:Continue,
ZGRfirstVisitIntro2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == ZGR_firstVisitIntro2,,"You step onto a perfectly dry pad. A shimmer as wind drives a burst of rain into the atmo-field betrays the artifice of this pocket of calm.

You are invited inside by an obsequious corporate usher.",ZGR_firstVisitIntro3:Follow,
ZGRfirstVisitIntro3,DialogOptionSelected,$option == ZGR_firstVisitIntro3,,"The architecture of Skyarco II's interior and its integrated art-installations are titanic in scale and inhuman in affect. Your attention is subtly drawn toward geometric motifs suggestive of a mathematical intricacy which would reward close study with nothing less than delight, and...

""It was designed by an Artificial Intelligence,"" the cheerful secretary behind the reception desk informs you, breaking the trance. ""Before the ban imposed by the Hegemony, of course."" 

""The piece is explicitly referent-free to reflect the pure universe of interstellar markets which invite every new partner to participate in Tri-Tachyon's enterprise!""","ZGR_firstVisitIntro4:""I'm here to see Director Glamor-Rotenev.""
ZGR_firstVisitIntro3b:""Isn't that nice.""",
ZGRfirstVisitIntro3b,DialogOptionSelected,$option == ZGR_firstVisitIntro3b,"$player.ethosSarcastic++
RemoveOption ZGR_firstVisitIntro3b","""It is, isn't it?"" the secretary agrees cheerfully.",,
ZGRfirstVisitIntro4,DialogOptionSelected,$option == ZGR_firstVisitIntro4,,"""Of course, $playerSirOrMadam,"" the secretary says with a smile. ""The Director asked that you head right in.""

The lighting of the richly furnished entryway - is that a mercury fountain? - warms slightly, inviting you to proceed.",ZGR_firstVisitIntro5:Enter the office of the Director of Special Acquisitions,
ZGRfirstVisitIntro5,DialogOptionSelected,$option == ZGR_firstVisitIntro5,PauseMusic,"A plane of glass - diamond-matrix, naturally - stretches in both directions to the edge of your peripheral vision, its extent blocked only by a set of cyclopean interior columns. Misty mountains and towering arcologies wreathed in rain clouds hang in the vista beyond.

Before you, a figure sits - now stands - behind a monolithic desk stark as a planetoid scraped bare by pulsar beam.

The Director of ""Special Acquisitions"".

A hand raises, open, to invite you to sit. A seat appears.","ZGR_firstVisitIntro6:Sit
ZGR_firstVisitIntro6stand:Stand",
ZGRfirstVisitIntro6stand,DialogOptionSelected,$option == ZGR_firstVisitIntro6stand,"$standing = true 0
$option = ZGR_firstVisitIntro6 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected",Glamor-Rotanev remains standing to match.,,
ZGRfirstVisitIntro6,DialogOptionSelected,$option == ZGR_firstVisitIntro6,"$player.metZGR = true
BeginConversation glamor_rotanev
PlayCustomMusic music_tritach_market_hostile","""Captain $playerName. I offer vast wealth in exchange for your unique facility in navigating exceptional scenarios.""

She blinks once. Her gaze is fixed on you, but you can't help but feel it is slightly vague, apparently attentive but not present in spirit. The look of a cyber-aug.

Her tech must be absolutely top-of-the-line, of course.","ZGR_firstVisit7a:""I'll hear you out. What's the proposal?""
ZGR_firstVisit7b:""What's the catch?""
ZGR_firstVisit7c:""Directly to business, huh? No small-talk?""",
ZGRfirstVisit7a,DialogOptionSelected,$option == ZGR_firstVisit7a,"$option = ZGR_firstVisit8 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","""Fitting to your talents, I think,"" she says. ""Allow me to iterate your accomplishments briefly so that you know where we stand.""",,
ZGRfirstVisit7b,DialogOptionSelected,$option == ZGR_firstVisit7b,"$option = ZGR_firstVisit8 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","""Risk of annihilation,"" she answers placidly. ""For which you'll be appropriately compensated.""

""Allow me to iterate your accomplishments briefly so that you know I do not make my offer without consideration.""",,
ZGRfirstVisit7c,DialogOptionSelected,$option == ZGR_firstVisit7c,"$option = ZGR_firstVisit8 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","""The demand for my time is great, thus its premium.""

Her lip quirks; not quite worth a smile.

""You must appreciate what I've already invested in you. Further to that point: allow me to iterate your accomplishments briefly so that you know where we stand.""",,
