RemoveOption bqfs_askForSupplies","You make the arrangements, and before the passing of a workshift, a small batch of emergency supplies is transferred to your $shipOrFleet for repairs.

""The funds you receive from $theFaction are meant to cover operational expenses,"" $personName says brusquely. ""Your commission ID will be flagged for one full cycle due to this emergency supply transfer, so don't make a habit of not having a backup plan.""",,
,,,,,,
# Abandoned Station salvage narratives,,,,,,
# salvage Station Mining Outland,,,,,,
salSMOLstart,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == salExplore
$tag:salvageable
$customType == station_mining_remnant
!$hasDefenders
!$defenderFleetDefeated
$salvageSpecialData == null
!$didSpecialExploreStory
!$player.exploredStationMiningOutland
RollProbability 0.3",ShowImageVisual salvor_explore_hull,"Your salvors spread out through the $nameInText in teams under the gruff direction of your Ops Chief. Salvage is rapidly identified, assessed, logged, and tagged with trackers, when appropriate, for follow-up teams to extract.

Computers and datastores are accessed via disposable interfacers, rough and quick hardware jobs that send back any information they can lift from poorly shielded databanks. Back on your $shipOrFleet, your tech teams crack security and decrypts anything they can, forwarding useful information - maps, cargo manifests, engineering diagrams - back to the salvors to use.",salSMOL_story1:Continue,
salSMOLstory1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == salSMOL_story1,AddCommodity drugs 100,"These teams are experts at rapidly reconstructing the relevant events of a starship or space station's demise; such a narrative provides useful information about dangers and valuables.

Here, comms logs and surveillance gives meaning to the evidence of scattered damage caused by light firearms - local security was in the process of a major crackdown on a drug smuggling operation, and in an explosive confrontation appears to have caused a blowout of the primary hab section. This seems to have tipped the state of the station, already precarious, into a full evacuation.

The rest of the story is mere salvage for your waiting holds.",salSMOL_out:Continue,
salSMOLout,DialogOptionSelected,$option == salSMOL_out,"$player.exploredStationMiningOutland = true
$didSpecialExploreStory = true
FireBest CheckSalvageSpecial",,,
# salvage Station Mining Dead Strikers,,,,,,
salSMDSstart,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == salExplore
$tag:salvageable
$customType == station_mining_remnant
!$hasDefenders
!$defenderFleetDefeated
$salvageSpecialData == null
!$didSpecialExploreStory
!$player.exploredStationMiningDeadStrikers
RollProbability 0.3",ShowImageVisual dead_zero_g,"Your salvors fan out through the station, discovering makeshift barricades around the access tubes to the executive and security modules. There's interior combat damage caused by handheld weapons, many of which appear to have been adapted from mining tools. A strike turned deadly.

The security forces employed riot-suppression armaments at first, then rapidly escalated to their cache of ""vac-safe"" weapons intended for boarding and infantry action within ship hulls or station modules. 

The miners appear to have responded by up-armoring standard haz suits, adding breastplates worked from mining drones' blast panels, slotted visors cut from rolls of nuke-rated anti-spall sheeting, and much other imaginative makeshift panoply.",salSMDS_story1:Continue,
salSMDSstory1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == salSMDS_story1,,"With the tides turning against them once more, security forces fought a break-out action toward central life support.

Successful, they choked off atmo and water to those modules held by the strikers. This won the fight, if the heavily armored but nonetheless desiccated corpses floating through the corridors have anything to say about it, but the war was still lost.

The station appears to have been abandoned as-is, too much of a scandal to reactivate or, perhaps, merely a write-off.",salSMDS_out:Continue,
salSMDSout,DialogOptionSelected,$option == salSMDS_out,"$player.exploredStationMiningDeadStrikers = true
$didSpecialExploreStory = true
FireBest CheckSalvageSpecial",,,
# salvage Station Mining Pirate Attack,,,,,,
salSMPAstart,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == salExplore
$tag:salvageable
$customType == station_mining_remnant
!$hasDefenders
!$defenderFleetDefeated
$salvageSpecialData == null
!$didSpecialExploreStory
!$player.exploredStationMiningPirateAttack
RollProbability 0.3",ShowImageVisual dead_zero_g,"Your salvors discover that comms and anti-collision weapon emplacements have been deliberately destroyed by careful strikes.

Closer examination shows evidence that a pirate ship docked - the brutal hull markings and garish paint job of the gutted hulk are a giveaway - but was completely disabled in the cargo bay by some kind of makeshift explosive adapted from on-hand mining equipment.

Their plundering mothership destroyed, the remaining pirates - operating a handful of light frigates and a wing of fighters - appear to have taken out their anger by strafing the station's hab modules and life support before going on their way.

The few miners who survived the immediate attack were doomed to a slow death.",salSMPA_out:Continue,
salSMPAout,DialogOptionSelected,$option == salSMPA_out,"$player.exploredStationMiningPirateAttack = true
$didSpecialExploreStory = true
FireBest CheckSalvageSpecial",,,
# salvage Station Research bioweapons,,,,,,
salSRBWstart,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == salExplore
$tag:salvageable
$customType == station_research_remnant
!$hasDefenders
!$defenderFleetDefeated
$salvageSpecialData == null
!$didSpecialExploreStory
!$player.exploredStationResearchBioweapons
RollProbability 0.3","ShowImageVisual salvor_explore_hull
$option = salSRBW_start2 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","Your salvors proceed with a routine ingress, by-the-book under the suspicious eyes of your ops chief.

An atmo sample of a trapped pocket - a tedious checklist task - pull up bright orange and green on the shared display: extreme biohazard. The salvor working the derelict almost drops the sampler-drill in surprise; Ops barks sharp orders, reiterating the hazardous environment recovery ingress checklist with effortless recall.",,
salSRBWstartA,DialogOptionSelected,$option == salSRBW_start2,,"It's an unusual reading, but not dangerous if containment procedures are followed to the letter.",salSRBW_story1:Continue,
salSRBWstartB,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == salSRBW_start2
$player.jangalaWentMaskOn",,"It's an unusual reading, and you recall the harsh words Ops gave you after returning to your $shipOrFleet after you exposed yourself to the xenolife of Jangala, albeit wearing a mask.

You also remember...","salSRBW_opsRespA:Interrupting the tirade to inform them that you are the sole executive authority on this $shipOrFleet.
salSRBW_opsRespB:Thanking them for emphasizing procedure, but to be mindful of their tone in front of crew.
salSRBW_opsRespC:Making a crack about 'containment procedures' and visiting spacer bars which made the crew laugh.",
salSRBWstartC,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == salSRBW_start2
$player.jangalaWentMaskOff",,"It's an unusual reading, and you'll never forget the dressing-down Ops gave you after returning to your $shipOrFleet after you exposed yourself to the xenolife of Jangala without even the benefit of a mask.

You also remember...","salSRBW_opsRespA:Interrupting the tirade to inform them that you are the sole executive authority on this $shipOrFleet.
salSRBW_opsRespB:Thanking them for emphasizing procedure, but to be mindful of their tone in front of crew.
salSRBW_opsRespC:Making a crack about 'containment procedures' and visiting spacer bars which made the crew laugh.",
salSRBWopsRespA,DialogOptionSelected,$option == salSRBW_opsRespA,$player.ethosOrder++,"Your ops chief also remembers, it seems, for they meet your eye just briefly as they give orders for the savlor teams to adjust dispositions in response to this discovery.",salSRBW_story1:Continue,
salSRBWopsRespB,DialogOptionSelected,$option == salSRBW_opsRespB,$player.ethosHumble++,"Your ops chief also remembers, it seems, for they meet your eye just briefly as they give orders for the savlor teams to adjust dispositions in response to this discovery.",salSRBW_story1:Continue,
salSRBWopsRespC,DialogOptionSelected,$option == salSRBW_opsRespC,$player.ethosSarcastic++,"Your ops chief also remembers, it seems, for they meet your eye just briefly as they give orders for the savlor teams to adjust dispositions in response to this discovery. As you recall, Ops didn't even smile. They never joke about procedure.

Never.",salSRBW_story1:Continue,
salSRBWstory1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == salSRBW_story1,,"One particular module of this research station appears to have been a bioweapons laboratory. The lab is - rather, was - hermetically sealed, and contains the ruins of state-of-the-art containment and decontamination facilities.

Naturally, something went terribly wrong. 

And as your techies analyze telemetry and what raw surveillance buffers the salvors on-station are able to transmit back to your $shipOrFleet, the disaster begins to look distinctly unnatural.","salSRBW_story2:""Ops, what caused this?""",
salSRBWstory2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == salSRBW_story2,,"""Sabotage,"" your ops chief mutters darkly.

The patchy surveillance shows a rapid spread of violent, painful demise beginning in atmospheric processing and spreading outward at the speed of fresh air through atmo conduits, tripping the broad-spectrum biohazard sensors one by one as the agent suffused through the station. But no alarm sounded for human ears.

Your salvage chief orders all remaining pockets of atmo purged, and strict quarantine procedures followed.

The bioweapons lab's computer core destroyed itself with a small bomb when a timed dead man's switch was not reset, so nothing of salable value remains, if indeed a buyer could be found for whatever biochemical horror was conjured here.",salSRBW_out:Continue,
salSRBWout,DialogOptionSelected,$option == salSRBW_out,"$player.exploredStationResearchBioweapons = true
$didSpecialExploreStory = true
FireBest CheckSalvageSpecial",,,
# salvage Station Research Radiation Surge,,,,,,
salSRRSstart,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == salExplore
$tag:salvageable
$customType == station_research_remnant
!$hasDefenders
!$defenderFleetDefeated
$salvageSpecialData == null
!$didSpecialExploreStory
!$player.exploredStationRadiationSurge
RollProbability 0.3",ShowImageVisual salvor_explore_hull,"Salvor teams cut through fused locks and infiltrate the station. They find researchers, administrators, technicians down to the lowliest access-tunnel scrubber at their work-stations, or near enough. Quite dead, however. And even those who remained in pockets of viable atmo are surprisingly undecayed.

Their end was not pleasant, but it appears to have at least been very, very quick.

Your salvors and tech teams assemble evidence to reconstruct the event: a massive radiation pulse centered on Experiment Module B, which, judging from the gap between the ruins of Modules A and C, was almost entirely vaporized by the event.","salSRRS_story1:""Any sign of what they were trying to do?""",
salSRRSstory1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == salSRRS_story1,,"Your tech officer shakes their head, showing characteristic frustration at having their curiosity unfulfilled.

No relevant monitoring and computer system from Module B survived, and the general practice of this station appears to have involved heavy siloing of information even up to the level of the executive command section, so it's impossible to say what exactly the research being pursued involved or, indeed, whether the event was an accident or something more sinister.

Whatever it was, at least it happened a long time ago.",salSRRS_out:Continue,
salSRRSout,DialogOptionSelected,$option == salSRRS_out,"$player.exploredStationRadiationSurge = true
$didSpecialExploreStory = true
FireBest CheckSalvageSpecial",,,
# salvage Station Research Security Fritz,,,,,,
salSRSFstart,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == salExplore
$tag:salvageable
$customType == station_research_remnant
!$hasDefenders
!$defenderFleetDefeated
!$salvageSpecialData
!$didSpecialExploreStory
!$player.exploredStationSecurityFritz
RollProbability 0.3",ShowImageVisual salvor_explore_hull,"Although superficially intact, salvor teams soon find evidence of light weapons fire and the resulting carnage, thankfully long desiccated, decayed, and/or frozen depending on the run-down time of life support in any particular sector. 

The seemingly random spread and directionlessness of the violence suggests that the security systems of this station turned on its occupants all at once. The catastrophic results were not helped by the unusually strong internal security measures: hidden autoturrets set to kill, powered lockdown curtains which indiscriminately scissored obstructions, and nests of mobile suppression drones which could traverse small conduits and air ducts to find and ""neutralize"" any survivors.

Thankfully, the last of these measures has long run out of power.",salSRSF_story1:Continue,
salSRSFstory1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == salSRSF_story1,,"Despite the station's reactor being run down, and the power network itself highly degraded, your salvors are understandably paranoid. Your Ops Chief is more than satisfied to use their fear to emphasize the necessity of strict and systematic recovery protocols in this - and indeed every - recovery operation.

Try as they might to piece something together from station logs, it remains unclear to your tech team what precisely used the chief administrator's executive access codes to turn the security systems inward. ",salSRSF_out:Continue,
salSRSFout,DialogOptionSelected,$option == salSRSF_out,"$player.exploredStationSecurityFritz = true
$didSpecialExploreStory = true
FireBest CheckSalvageSpecial",,,
# salvage Station Research Decapitation Strike,,,,,,
salSRDSstart,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == salExplore
$tag:salvageable
$customType == station_research_remnant
!$hasDefenders
!$defenderFleetDefeated
!$salvageSpecialData
!$didSpecialExploreStory
!$player.exploredStationDecapitationStrike
RollProbability 0.3",ShowImageVisual dead_zero_g,"A precise decapitation strike appears to have targeted the command and control module of this station, likely a clutch of military-grade torpedoes unleashed at close range by an unsuspected vessel.

Security systems were tight and highly hierarchical; once the central C&C went down, automatic lockdown procedures trapped the occupants of the station in their sections - habitation, labs, research, recreation, life support, cargo handling, storage, engineering, cooling, and so on.

Now each is a locked tomb preserving evidence of the final hours, sometimes days, of the occupants.",salSRDS_story1:Continue,
salSRDSstory1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == salSRDS_story1,,"Your salvor teams do not tarry to ponder the fate of these unfortunate souls, each miserable in its own way, as they cut through the lockdown doors to assess valuables.",salSRDS_out:Continue,
salSRDSout,DialogOptionSelected,$option == salSRDS_out,"$player.exploredStationDecapitationStrike = true
$didSpecialExploreStory = true
FireBest CheckSalvageSpecial",,,
# salvage Orbital Habitat Ozymandias,,,,,,
salOHOZstart,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == salExplore
$tag:salvageable
$customType == orbital_habitat_remnant
!$hasDefenders
!$defenderFleetDefeated
!$salvageSpecialData
!$didSpecialExploreStory
!$player.exploredStationOzymandias
RollProbability 0.3",ShowImageVisual salvor_explore_hull,"Upon entry, your salvors discover first one, then many of the same portrait adorning the interior sections of the hab. Smashed busts line the primary reception concourse. Above all stood a statue of the selfsame likeness churned out of a simple rock-foam fabricator, polished, and gilded; it now lies face-planted into the deckplates, the gilding half-stripped.

All bear the face of a strong-jawed man who looks down upon the empty halls and dead plazas of the hab, his gaze fatherly; stern, and proud. And in all cases defaced: the nose smashed off, crude words painted or, more often, burnt across his image.

Even his name, whatever it was, has been erased from every databank by a spitefully determined noise-wipe virus.",salOHOZ_story1:Continue,
salOHOZstory1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == salOHOZ_story1,,"Exploring further, the salvor teams discover the remains of a palace dominating an entire section of the hab.

Once a vast construction, now just two blackened support legs remain amidst the rubble of its shattered visage. Parklands, now reduced to lone and level ash, follow the curve of the habitat's shell.

Whoever the man was, he was first exalted and then hated in equal measure.",salOHOZ_out:Continue,
salOHOZout,DialogOptionSelected,$option == salOHOZ_out,"$player.exploredStationOzymandias= true
$didSpecialExploreStory = true
FireBest CheckSalvageSpecial",,,
# salvage Orbital Habitat Overgrown,,,,,,
salOHOGstart,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == salExplore
$tag:salvageable
$customType == orbital_habitat_remnant
!$hasDefenders
!$defenderFleetDefeated
!$salvageSpecialData
!$didSpecialExploreStory
!$player.exploredStationOvergrown
RollProbability 0.3","ShowImageVisual cache_large
FireAll MostLuddicEthosRefresh","A close approach by salvor teams shows a heat source, and glint of artificial light. An anomalous pocket of operational life-support, the emergency subsection backup of a backup somehow running for tens, hundreds of cycles? It is unlikely.

Your officers always perform the standard transponder pings at the start of a salvage operation; it is part of the ritual of legal salvage (though records of legality are fabricated easily enough, when required, and doing a good job of it is a sign of respect appreciated by customs officers across the Persean Sector).

It would be awkward to stumble into some hermit's cell, ideologue's oubliette, or pirate holdfast unannounced, so your comms officer takes charge of a new signalling attempt with a full range of communication protocols, from an overpowered standard holo-link to mere radio, laser staccato, and even an esoteric grav-pulse relay.","salOHOG_story1:""Comms, anything to report?""",
salOHOGstory1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == salOHOG_story1,,"""No, $playerSirOrMadam,"" Comms replies. ""Nothing. With your permission, I've got an idea...""

An acoustic inducer-transponder, normally used in mining surveys, is tenderly attached to the hab's structure by a discreet remote probe. It thuds out a code, and detects only a tiny, noisy, rhythmic vibration in return. Something tapping on the hullplate with slow, clock-like regularity.

It doesn't change.","salOHOG_story2:""Ops, it's your turn.""",
salOHOGstory2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == salOHOG_story2,ShowImageVisual salvor_explore_hull,"Your Ops chief oversees a careful breach of the habitat, wary both for traps and the need to not disrupt the surviving bubble of life-support. Survivors make salvage rights more complex, but they're generally thankful enough for rescue to come to a profitable accommodation.

Salvors attach temporary bubble-locks around the entry points, inflate them with the ubiquitous portable atmo units, and perform a cold-cut on sealed emergency doors. Slow and safe. Ops nods, satisfied with the work proceeding on the shared display.",salOHOG_story3:Continue,
salOHOGstory3,DialogOptionSelected,$option == salOHOG_story3,FireAll salOHOGstoryChoice,"A spot of green-yellow brightness at the end of a foggy corridor; the image stabilizer kicks in, cancelling the jerky hop-step of the lead salvor's micro-g movement.

A tiny garden grows wild within this celestial tomb. Some kind of fissile backup battery has survived, clicking away the decay of heavy elements to heat and light a tiny bubble of life. Moisture condenses in a murky lens of slush on a hubward window, then falls slowly in huge drops through the micro-g of the habitat's spin, past the glowplates, toward the mosses and molds and tiny flowers growing on the warm heaps of droppings and husks of vermin.

On a life-giving terran world, this would be nothing more than a dank pit. Here, it is a miracle.",,
salOHOGstory3resp1,salOHOGstoryChoice,$player.luddicAttitudeFaithfulOrPather,"SetTooltip salOHOG_story3luddic ""'... and all that is good can be found there.' - Sacred Texts of Ludd""",,"salOHOG_story3luddic:""'Where there is life, that is the throne of God...'""",
salOHOGstory3resp2,salOHOGstoryChoice,,,,salOHOG_story3secular:Continue,
salOHOGstory3secular,DialogOptionSelected,$option == salOHOG_story3secular,$player.luddicAttitudeSecular++,"""$PlayerSirOrMadam."" Your ops chief acknowledges your command and begins ordering the dance of surveying, inventorying, extraction, and transport.",salOHOG_out:Continue,
salOHOGstory3luddic,DialogOptionSelected,$option == salOHOG_story3luddic,,"""$PlayerSirOrMadam,"" your ops chief responds, the very hint of a question in their tone.","salOHOG_story3luddic2:""We shall leave this place as it is. No salvage.""
salOHOG_story3secular:""You may proceed with the operation.""",
salOHOGstory3luddic2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == salOHOG_story3luddic2,,"""$PlayerSirOrMadam."" Your ops chief acknowledges your command as a law unyielding as gravity itself, and orders the salvors to withdraw without disturbing anything. They know better than to clutter the chief's comms with questions, so they respond quietly and efficiently.",salOHOG_outLuddic:Continue,
salOHOGout,DialogOptionSelected,$option == salOHOG_out,"$player.exploredStationOvergrown = true
$didSpecialExploreStory = true
FireBest CheckSalvageSpecial",,,
