$customType == wreck
$onslaughtMkI score:1000",SalvageSpecialInteraction,,,
mk1_exploreFirstTime,CheckSalvageSpecial,"$salvageSpecialData != null
$customType == wreck
$onslaughtMkI score:1000
!$explored","$explored = true
$global.foundOneslaught = true
$player.encounteredWeird = true","Your sensors officer begins a preliminary high-power scan of the dark mass as your operations chief preps salvor teams.

""$PlayerSirOrMadam, this looks... there's nothing quite like this on file, but..."" Sensors gives up on words and pull a detailed false-color scan into the primary display.

Someone lets out a gasp. 

The database assistant algorithm won't provide a positive ID, but that form is unmistakable to the human eye.

This is the Onslaught Mk.I, the ship of legend.",mk1_continue0:Continue,
mk1_explore0,DialogOptionSelected,$option == mk1_continue0,ShowImageVisual cache_large,"How old must it be, thousands of cycles?

If you had been asked a shift ago, your reasonable reply would have been to call it a myth. The Onslaught Mk.I could easily be a just-so founding narrative element of the Human Domain, a story about united struggle and hardship against an implacable Other with a shiny bit of military kit in center stage. An imagined avatar of the empire's holy trinity: military, industry, gate system.

Yet here that avatar appears, unbelievably far and wayward from the heart of the Human Domain - or even what was once the Domain's frontiers a thousand cycles ago.

Your ops chief, unperturbed, looks to you for confirmation. Words are unneeded, the question is clear: send in the salvors?","mk1_continue1:""Proceed.""",
mk1_explore1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == mk1_continue1,,"Ops nods, then turns to bark commands on the salvors' command frequency.

Junior officers scurry to cajole crew prepping cargo-handling drones while Sensors puts one analysis team on careful outward watch and another on the hulk to ensure there are no surprises.   

Within short minutes, the first salvors dock their open-vacuum shuttle frames and utility drones at various entry points identified along the vessel's massive hull.

Ops gives the go-order.",mk1_continue2:Continue,
mk1_explore2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == mk1_continue2,"ShowImageVisual salvor_explore_hull
AddTextSmall ""T H R E A T  D E T E C T E D"" bad","You notice your comms officer furiously working their interface, then turn and call a report to you.

""$PlayerSirOrMadam! Salvor-four is picking up something on an open frequency- um, radio-only. Very low power. Some kind of analogue encoding? We did this in... training...""

A few more taps, and a message is formed from noise, letter by letter, across your display. ",mk1_continue3:Continue,
mk1_explore3,DialogOptionSelected,$option == mk1_continue3,"AddTextSmall ""T H R E A T  D E T E C T E D"" bad","This gives your officers pause - Ops calls a hold order while the situation is assessed. Internal self-defense systems activating? War-drone deployment?

Only silence.

Then acoustics picks up a few taps as salvors secure themselves to bulkheads, powering down their tools and, no doubt, reaching for what small-arms they do carry.

Still, no movement.

Low, steady EM activity - just the repeater, a chorus of them in fact, mechanically intoning the same message to one another.",mk1_continue4:Continue,
mk1_explore4,DialogOptionSelected,$option == mk1_continue4,,"Fevered analysis proceeds. In the midst of what appears to be structured noise buried in the analog waveform - datasets which are insensible without context - analysis teams discover a set of coordinates; a position at some distance from the small gravity well you're orbiting in archaic but parseable Domain astrogation units. The message still repeats itself.

""The signal is weak,"" your sensors officer says. ""Unlikely to be picked up by anything that isn't in close-order formation with the... the hull. Tactical telemetry to coordinate distributed systems?""",mk1_continue5:Continue,
mk1_explore5,DialogOptionSelected,$option == mk1_continue5,,"Cautiously, team by team, your operations chief reactivates exploration and assessment of the hulk.

Bafflingly crude automation is wormed throughout the ship, whispering to itself. Interfaces are built on familiar fundamental principles, but aesthetically red-shifted, seeming from an alien culture.

What records remain are damaged where they aren't missing entirely. The logs tell of aeons of war in the darkness between the stars. Human crew in and out of cryo, continually diminished, replaced by the augmented wounded, then the cyborg rebuilds, and then, and then... this exhausted humming, clicking thing threaded throughout the ship.",mk1_continue6:Continue,
mk1_explore6,DialogOptionSelected,$option == mk1_continue6,"AddTextSmall ""Sensor calibration data acquired"" highlight","The logs are empty for long periods- dark, hibernating leaps. Then there is a noted uptick in activity less than 200 standard cycles ago. The enemy is only identified as ""Threat"". A datastore reference leads to blocks of information decayed by time. But the reconstruction algorithms leap into action and, despite troublingly low reliability ratings, sew together a set of files. 

Patch notes.

The hardware specs are arcane, the software obtuse and plagued by null library calls, but the common language of human mathematics sketches out the intent. There, your technology officer's team assembles a new spec of the sensor modifications required to detect this ""Threat"".

Adapting these requirements on your relatively modern systems is a far easier task than the labors described by the ancients.",mk1_continue7:Continue,
mk1_explore7,DialogOptionSelected,$option == mk1_continue7,"$player.hasThreatDetectionSensorMods = true
AddTextSmall ""T H R E A T  D E T E C T E D"" bad
AddTextSmall ""T H R E A T  D E T E C T E D"" bad
AddTextSmall ""T H R E A T  D E T E C T E D"" bad
AddText ""\""I think it's working.\"" Their words are almost a whisper.""
MiscCMD mk1_spawnThreatFleet","""$PlayerSirOrMadam, I'm not sure it's working."" Your sensors officer speaks, standing at a control console to demonstrate a first test of the adaptations. Line after line is dumped into an output log.

The characters sprout and repeat. Your technology officer's face is underlit by their glow.",mk1_continue8:Continue,
mk1_explore8,DialogOptionSelected,$option == mk1_continue8,"AddTextSmall ""T H R E A T  D E T E C T E D"" bad
AddTextSmall ""T H R E A T  D E T E C T E D"" bad
