BeginConversation elek
SetPersonPortrait elek ""elek2""","A man appears. The resolution is poor, the audio patchy. It appears that he didn't pay for premium-grade transmission and caching.

""Ahem. Yes, hello? I assume that icon means it's recording.""

He clears his throat, turning to fully face the imager.",gaDHO_hook1:Continue,
gaDHOhook0met,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == gaDHO_hook0
$player.metElek","$global.gaDHO_didInvite= true
BeginConversation elek
SetPersonPortrait elek ""elek2""","Academician Cornelius Elek appears before you. The resolution is poor, the audio patchy. It appears that he didn't pay for premium-grade transmission and caching.

""Ahem. Yes, hello? I assume that icon means it's recording.""

He clears his throat, turning to fully face the imager.",gaDHO_hook1:Continue,
gaDHOhook1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gaDHO_hook1,,"""I am Academician Cornelius Elek."" He waits a moment to allow his name to sink in.

""You may have heard of my seminal work, 'A New Survey of Planetology on the Fringe of the Persean Sector' which achieved a new standard for the field, if I may say so, despite tepid reactions from certain of my narrow-minded colleagues. Now, as I was saying...""",gaDHO_hook2:Continue,
gaDHOhook1metBefore,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == gaDHO_hook1
$player.metElek",,"""I am Academician Cornelius Elek."" He waits a moment to allow his name to sink in.

""You may have heard of my seminal work, 'A New Survey of Planetology on the Fringe of the Persean Sector' which achieved a new standard for the field, if I may say so, despite tepid reactions from certain of my narrow-minded colleagues. Now, as I was saying...""

His self-important speech is as droning as you recall from your previous conversation, when you returned a planetology datacore to the Academy.",gaDHO_hook2:Continue,
gaDHOhook2aside,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == gaDHO_hook2
$player.heardElekWasAJerk
!$didDHOhook2aside",$didDHOhook2aside = true 0,"So this is Cornelius Elek. 

You recall discussing him with Alviss Sebestyen when you returned a planetology datacore to the Galatia Academy for a reward. Sebestyen wouldn't say it outright, but it seems that Elek is a man who tends toward a certain amount of interpersonal friction.

Judging by the self-important delivery of this speech, this is that same Elek.",gaDHO_hook2:Continue,
gaDHOhook2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gaDHO_hook2,$global.gaDHO_elekMentionedPatron = true,"He pauses a moment, probably to evoke gravitas.

""It is my desire that this missive finds you receptive, Captain...""

Elek glances down, reading from a datapad.

""$PlayerName. It has been strongly emphasized to me by... a patron of the sciences who has seen fit to fund my work that you are the perfect facilitator to the solution of an old mystery I found in the archives. I-""

He squints again at something on his datapad, then says under his breath ""Is that the cost per second? Stars above!""",gaDHO_hook3:Continue,"# no, he won't remember you even if you met him before"
gaDHOhook3,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gaDHO_hook3,"Highlight ""vast fortune"" highlight","Elek clears his throat again, then speaks quickly.

""In summary, my patron offers a vast fortune in credits for services which I shall be pleased to enumerate in detail upon your visit to my offices at the Galatia Academy, which may be found in orbit of P-"" 

The message cuts off.",gaDHO_hook4:Continue,
