$global.gaDHO_playerAgreedTo200k = true
FireAll gaDHOvisitElekHub","""Whyever not? Say what you will about business ethics, they're unmatched in their commitment to advancing unrestricted basic research. And Director Glamor-Rotanev has a particular understanding of the importance of...""

He stops, seeming to realize for once that he's belaboring the point.

""Let's agree on 200,000 credits, yes?"" He looks at you accusingly. ""It should be spent on primary research, not gilding rocket ships, but."" He holds up a hand, as if to contain the outburst he presumes will come. ""I shall hold my tongue, and so will you. If the expedition is as much of a success as I believe it will be, the dear price shall be worth it and I'm certain that... that my patron will pay.""",,
gaDHOvisitElekAskPatron,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gaDHO_visitElekHubSelB,$askedWhoFriend = true 0,"""Mm,"" he frowns, carefully maintaining a thoughtful expression.

""They have asked me not to reveal their identity. I believe, if anything, the humility they show in not taking public credit for their contributions to this great academy - and my department in particular - are a sign of dedication to pure scientific advancement. Truly, it is a noble undertaking.""","gaDHO_visitElekAskPatron2a:""More noble, by far, is your willingness to take up this cause."" (lie)
gaDHO_visitElekAskPatron2b:""As I am key to this expedition, I'd like to know more of your patron and my benefactor.""",
gaDHOvisitElekAskPatron2a,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gaDHO_visitElekAskPatron2a,"$askedWhoFriend2 = true 0
FireAll gaDHOvisitElekHub","""You're too kind, $playerSirOrMadam."" Elek smiles, quite pleased with himself. ""I believe that Director- that my patron expressed a similar sentiment.""

He looks up and away, ""Not that I have not had to make sacrifices. Great sacrifices, indeed. It is a lonely calling at times, but I hearten myself with the knowledge that I am enriching the...""

Despite your attempt at winning his favor, he's lost the thread and taken a whole new course. Eventually he drifts off into what looks like thoughtful silence.",,
gaDHOvisitElekAskPatron2b,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gaDHO_visitElekAskPatron2b,,"""A not unreasonable request,"" Elek says, making a show of thinking over your words.

""You will, after all, be bound bodily to the project more than any other, even if you do not possess the theoretical background to fully understand its importance. I suppose it is the least I could do. After all, girding with knowing of the greater purposes you serve might enhance and embolden your spirit of exploration...""",gaDHO_visitElekAskPatron3:Nod enthusiastically as if you are entranced by his words,
gaDHOvisitElekAskPatron3,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gaDHO_visitElekAskPatron3,"Highlight ""Zunya Glamor-Rotanev""
$global.gaDHO_elekRevealedZGRasPatron = true
$global.gaDHO_elekRevealedTriTachyonAsPatron
FireAll gaDHOvisitElekHub","Something breaks in his expression.

""Zunya Glamor-Rotanev, the Director of Special Acquisitions for the Tri-Tachyon corporation, in fact, is the patron of my project. She is a woman of great vision, far greater than I would have expected from such a lofty position in an ostensibly profit-driven enterprise.""

""By revealing this to you, captain, I am trusting in your discretion,"" he says with a solemn nod.",,
gaDHOvisitElekHubSelC,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gaDHO_visitElekHubSelC,,"""An excellent question."" Elek taps at his datapad, and turns toward his holodisplay.

The spinning moons have disappeared to be replaced by a map of the Persean Sector, a broad swath of stars. The Core Worlds are highlighted, the fringe stars somewhat dimmed.

""Here you see - or do not see, for it is in the crudest sense a sort of absence - the Orion-Persean Abyss. It is far from a nothingness, however. And it is that not-nothingness with which we are concerned.""","gaDHO_visitElekHubSelC2a:""So... there's something in the Abyss.""
gaDHO_visitElekHubSelC2b:""Aren't you a planetologist? This seems outside your field.""",
gaDHOvisitElekHubSelC2a,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gaDHO_visitElekHubSelC2a,"AdjustRepPerson elek FRIENDLY 1
$option = gaDHO_visitElekHubSelC3 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","""Correct, dear captain!"" Elek sounds pleased that you have followed the trajectory of his lesson.

""There are indeed planets to be found there. Cold, dark, and alone; bereft of their parent stars, flung into the sparse wastes between the arms of our galaxy.""",,
gaDHOvisitElekHubSelC2b,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gaDHO_visitElekHubSelC2b,"AdjustRepPerson elek SUSPICIOUS -1
$option = gaDHO_visitElekHubSelC3 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","""Pah,"" Elek waves a dismissal.

""I shan't fully enumerate the errors in your statement. It is enough that there are indeed planets to be found there. Cold, dark, and alone; bereft of their parent stars, flung into the sparse wastes between the arms of our galaxy.""",,
gaDHOvisitElekHubSelC2c,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gaDHO_visitElekHubSelC3,"$askedWhatLookingFor = true 0
FireAll gaDHOvisitElekHub","""I theorize that it is one of these planets our sensor array was targeting.""

His tone grows less heated. ""Or, rather, an unknown energetic event involving or concerning one such planet. We are not certain exactly which, however, and it is exceedingly difficult - and expensive - to perform any kind of broad analysis of these wayward children from afar. And with our sadly reduced means compared to the grand days of the old Domain... alas, alack.""",,
gaDHOvisitElekAccept,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gaDHO_visitElekAccept,"AddTextSmall ""Acquired data extraction hardware package"" highlight
$global.gaDHO_gotScanPackage = true
Call $global.gaDHO_ref updateStage","""Excellent. I'll have the hardware package transferred to your $shipOrFleet immediately,"" he taps at a datapad, connecting comms and reels off some imperious orders at some poor support staff.

""Off you go! We made the package installation idiot-proof. So I'm sure you...r technicians will be capable of installing it.""","gaDHO_visitElekAccept2a:""I'm sure we'll manage.""
gaDHO_visitElekAccept2b:""Wait, which end goes in the sensor array again?""",
gaDHOvisitElekAccept2a,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gaDHO_visitElekAccept2a,,"""Good.""

He turns back to his holodisplay and begins arranging moons again.

""I await your return, captain,"" he says over his shoulder.",gaDHO_visitElekLeave:Leave,
gaDHOvisitElekAccept2b,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gaDHO_visitElekAccept2b,$player.ethosSarcastic++,"""The attached specifications will..."" Elek pauses, then squints at you.

""I see. You're engaging in a bit of jocularity. Well, I can't exactly disapprove of high spirits at the outset of the expedition provided you mind the technical details.""

He turns back to his holodisplay and begins re-arranging moons. ""I await your return, captain,"" he says over his shoulder.",gaDHO_visitElekLeave:Leave,
gaDHOvisitElekNotInterested,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gaDHO_visitElekNotInterested,$global.gaDHO_rejectedOffer = true,"""Excellent, we'll start by..."" He pauses, processing your words.

""What? Don't be ridiculous,"" Elek huffs irritably. ""Take the time to think it through, captain. I'm sure reason will win out eventually.""

""Or, at least, greed,"" he says more quietly as he turns back to his holodisplay in a huff and begins arranging moons, a clear indication that he believes the conversation is over.",gaDHO_visitElekLeave:Leave,
gaDHOvisitElekEnd,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gaDHO_visitElekLeave,"EndConversation
