Ignoring you.",gaDHO_visitElekLeave:Leave,
# gaDHO found array w/o mission,,,,,,# gaDHO but player finds array w/o Elek etc
gaDHOjustFoundArrayStart,OpenInteractionDialog,"!$global.foundOneslaught
$oneslaughtSensorArray score:100
!$global.gaDHO_inProgress","ShowDefaultVisual
PrintDescription 1
AddText ""A routine scan shows that this sensor array has been modified.""","



","gaDHO_justFoundArray0:Investigate the modifications
100:defaultLeave:Leave",
gaDHOjustFoundArray0,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gaDHO_justFoundArray0,,"Your sensors officer casts the visual output to the primary bridge display. It is all struts and masses and harsh geometric shadows - then with a flash, a LIDAR overlay reveals the structure in the light of a false day.

A section near the center flashes at Sensor's prompting. There- a small workframe has been attached to the central processing module, a clutch of equipment cases spewing wires and cables outward like a parasitic growth.","gaDHO_justFoundArray1:""Ops, deploy your teams.""",
gaDHOjustFoundArray1,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gaDHO_justFoundArray1,,"Your ops chief deploys salvors with caution bordering on paranoia despite all appearances of this arrangement being of standard civilian parts. If it's pirates seeking a detection advantage, it would be customary for the arrangement to be trapped, and your ops chief's custom to oversee their disarming with seeming ease.

Each check is made, each movement coordinated with your sensors officer to ensure there are no surprises. The salvor teams look for everything from crude chemical bombs set off by millimeter-thin thermal detector patches to invisible thresholds of exotic physics which surround certain advanced technologies that might have been plundered from some old Domain cache.

Everything goes quiet for a moment. Ops taps a console, then turns to you.","gaDHO_justFoundArray2:""Report.""",
gaDHOjustFoundArray2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gaDHO_justFoundArray2,,"""$PlayerSirOrMadam. It's clean.""

Ops orders a start to the real work now. A senior salvage technician boots up a small, cheap interfacer which they hold out on a simple telescoping pole to probe the mod-hardware control system. Telemetry pours into the isolated computing environment set up by your technology officer's team, and they begin to interpret the results.

""Well, we think it's from the Galatia Academy,"" Tech says, eyes on an expanding visual model of the computing environment.
","gaDHO_justFoundArray3:""How can you tell?""",
gaDHOjustFoundArray3,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gaDHO_justFoundArray3,,"""Um. It's written on the equipment cases. See, here."" They pull a zoom-panel up on their TriPad. ""It says 'property of the Galatia Academy Planetology Department by the authority of Academician Cornelius Elek..."" their words drift off as the tech team's finding begin to coalesce into comprehensible patterns.
 
The story comes together: this old sensor array scanned a broad swath of the Abyss for very particular signatures over 200 cycles ago. Someone installed this new hardware quite recently, and it extracted that data from the sensor array's buffers, processed it using a clever suite of algorithms concocted as, presumably, the thesis project of some bright student of the Galatia Academy.

Then no one ever came back to collect the data.","gaDHO_justFoundArray4:""What are they looking for and what did they find?""",
gaDHOjustFoundArray3e1,DialogOptionSelected,"$option == gaDHO_justFoundArray3
$player.metElek",,"""Um. It's written on the equipment cases. See, here. It says 'property of the Galatia Academy Planetology Department by the authority of Academician Cornelius Elek..."" their words drift off as results start to come in.

Academician Cornelius Elek. A somewhat self-important man, as you recall. You found his datacore on some inner Fringe planet and received the reward authorized by Provost Kallichore for your trouble.",gaDHO_justFoundArray3e2:Continue,
gaDHOjustFoundArray3e2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gaDHO_justFoundArray3e2,,"The story comes together as Tech assembles the pieces: this sensor array scanned a broad swath of the Abyss for very particular signatures over 200 cycles ago. This hardware found that data in the sensor array's buffers, processed it with a clever suite of algorithms concocted as, presumably, the thesis project of some bright student of the Galatia Academy.

No one ever came back to collect the data.","gaDHO_justFoundArray4:""What was Elek looking for and what this find?""",
gaDHOjustFoundArray4,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gaDHO_justFoundArray4,,"""There's no, ah, obvious indication of what exactly they were looking for,"" Tech reports. ""It's all... complex self-modifying algorithms. A series of energetic events at a certain location, perhaps?""

""But,"" they say, trying to find the good news in this mess, ""it did find what it was looking for. There's a raw data buffer output with coordinates attached for what the modified processor claims is... some kind of rogue planet in the Abyss. Just a lone rock, no star, no other primary.""","gaDHO_justFoundArray5:""Some nameless rock, huh. Let's have the coordinates.""",
gaDHOjustFoundArray5,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gaDHO_justFoundArray5,"
AddTextSmall ""Acquired coordinates for rogue planet in the Abyss"" highlight
$global.gaDHO_foundArrayFirst = true
BeginMission gaDHO","""$PlayerSirOrMadam."" They tap a few commands and release a data-packet from the isolated computing environment to your personal datapad.

You have the coordinates for... something. Something that someone thought was important 200 cycles in the past. And that Cornelius Elek thought was important much more recently.

You could either go in blind to find out what's out there, or go to the Galatia Academy to see if this Academician Cornelius Elek has some kind of explanation.","gaDHO_justFoundArrayEndElek:Talk to Academician Elek at the Galatia Academy first
gaDHO_justFoundArrayEndAbyss:Why wait? Go straight to the coordinates in the Abyss",
gaDHOjustFoundArrayEndElek,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gaDHO_justFoundArrayEndElek,"$global.gaDHO_arrayFirstThenElek = true
Call $global.gaDHO_ref updateStage",The Abyss is not a place to be trifled with. Better to get all the information you possibly can - to say nothing of stocking up on fuel and supplies - before finding out what lies in darkest hyperspace.,defaultLeave:Leave,
gaDHOjustFoundArrayEndAbyss,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gaDHO_justFoundArrayEndAbyss,"$global.gaDHO_arrayFirstThenAbyss = true
Call $global.gaDHO_ref updateStage","Who cares about some academician's speculation? Their perspective is limited to the walls of their ivory torus orbiting a gas giant in the Galatia System.

You can simply strike at the heart of this mystery.",defaultLeave:Leave,
