gaDHOabyssEndElekMyDiscovery,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gaDHO_abyssEndElekMyDiscovery,AdjustRepActivePerson HOSTILE -2,"""You're a heartless mercenary with no appreciation for science,"" Elek says, his tone growing heated.

""You'd never have found... whatever you found... without me!"" He seems to realize in the moment how weak this sounds, and recomposes himself.

""This is practically piracy, you know.""","gaDHO_abyssEndElekAltIntroPiracy2:""No, this is business. And I took on great risk to see it done.""
gaDHO_abyssEndElekAltIntroPiracy:""Yes, it is. And if you don't pay me, you'll never get your precious data.""",
gaDHOabyssEndElekMyDiscovery2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gaDHO_abyssEndElekAltIntroPiracy,AdjustRepActivePerson HOSTILE -3,"He takes a deep breath and looks at you for a long time. He begins, but does not speak as he thinks better of it once, twice. You can see the anger in his eyes.

But you hold the data.

How many cycles of his academic career has he invested already? How many more will he get out of these results? He is a man of science, of reason. And of pride. But can he set it aside for a few minutes?",gaDHO_abyssEndElekAltIntroPiracy2:Continue,
gaDHOabyssEndElekMyDiscovery3,DialogOptionSelected,$option == gaDHO_abyssEndElekAltIntroPiracy2,"Highlight ""50,000""","Academician Cornelius Elek forms a tight, unkind smile.

""I see you are an unyielding negotiator, $playerSirOrMadam. I bow to the inescapable logic of your proposal.""

With trembling hand, he taps at his datapad.

""I shall pay you 50,000 credits for the data. It is the amount I promised the freelancer who installed the modifications and... failed to return.""","gaDHO_abyssEndElekAltIntroPiracy4a:""I accept.""
gaDHO_abyssEndElekAltIntroPiracy4b:""That's a failure's rate. I DID return, and from the Abyss. 100k.""",
