#adonyaOptTellStraight,AdonyaOptions,,,,"adonya_tellStraight:""Scylla was being held by League intelligence on Laicaille Habitat."" (explain)",
adonyaMoreHolosOutA,AdonyaOptions,$didTell,,,"adonya_outA:""Wonderful. Well, I shouldn't take any more of your time...""",
adonyaMoreHolosOutB,AdonyaOptions,,,,"adonya_outB:""I need to get back to my $shipOrFleet. Goodbye.""",
adonyaNotFleet,DialogOptionSelected,$option == adonya_notFleet,"$toldNotFleet = true 0
FireAll AdonyaOptions","""Oh... isn't that nice."" She smiles. ""You must be very successful.""",,
adonyaTell,DialogOptionSelected,$option == adonya_tell,"$option = adonya_tell2 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected",You explain that you found Scylla on Laicalle Habitat and helped her initiate a very important project at the Galatia Academy.,,
adonyaTell2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == adonya_tell2,"Highlight ""traverse the Gates""","With Zal's assistance, Scylla helped Provost Baird develop a method to open the Gate System.

It was a high-pressure project, and dangerous. Not for her, of course. Her job was on the theory and numbers side. Adonya nods, an extra wrinkle of concern on her forehead.

It didn't quite work out as expected, you explain, however you did manage to make history by using the so-called Janus Device to traverse the Gates, the first such trip in over 200 cycles. And it was made possible through Elissa Zal's engineering based on theoretical developments by Academician Scylla Coureuse.",adonya_tell3:Continue,
adonyaTell3,DialogOptionSelected,$option == adonya_tell3,$global.talkedtoAdonyaAfterGAATG = true,"""Oh!"" Adonya lights up at your words. ""I'm so happy she found Elissa again, what a nice girl. A little strange, though. Always up to something. But that's my Scylla.""

""I think she gets her taste from me,"" Adonya says in a  conspiratorial half-whisper.

""You should have met her father! You'd have liked him, I think. Stars above, he could be a troublemaker. But he was fun,"" she nods to herself.","adonya_tell4a:""And, um, that's all there is to tell.""
adonya_tell4b:""And then Scylla and Zal disappeared. I don't know where to.""
adonya_tell4c:""Then they disappeared together. I'm trying to find them.""",
adonyaTell4a,DialogOptionSelected,$option == adonya_tell4a,"$option = adonya_tell5 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","""Oh, okay,"" she says.",,
adonyaTell4b,DialogOptionSelected,$option == adonya_tell4b,"$option = adonya_tell5 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","""Oh, okay,"" she says, unconcerned.",,
adonyaTell4c,DialogOptionSelected,$option == adonya_tell4c,"$option = adonya_tell5 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected","""Oh,"" she says, apparently unconcerned. ""Good luck.""",,
adonyaTell5,DialogOptionSelected,$option == adonya_tell5,"$didTell = true 0
FireAll AdonyaOptions","""Thank you for stopping by, captain. I know you must be very busy and an old woman's worries are probably the last thing on your mind, but it was good of you to take the time.""

She pauses for a moment. ""If you find her, tell her she could send comms more often. I do so love hearing from her.""",,
adonyaMoreHolos,DialogOptionSelected,$option == adonya_moreHolos,"$moreHolos = true 0
FireAll AdonyaOptions","""Of course,"" she says. ""Scylla is a good daughter.""

""Sometimes it's a long time between them, and I get worried."" She glances back toward her holotainment unit. ""It'd be nice if she came for a visit.""",,
adonyaOutA,DialogOptionSelected,$option == adonya_outA,"$option = adonya_out 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected",,,
adonyaOutB,DialogOptionSelected,$option == adonya_outB,"$option = adonya_out 0
FireBest DialogOptionSelected",,,
adonyaOut,DialogOptionSelected,$option == adonya_out,"SetPersonHidden adonya_coureuse true
EndConversation
ShowDefaultVisual","""Now you be careful out there,"" she says. ""I know you're young, but you're not immortal. And I heard on the holo all about these terrible pirates who...""

Her impression of what happens between the Fringe and Core is somehow both ridiculously exaggerated and entirely insufficient. The holo-networks of Fikenhild are famously more entertaining than informative.

Eventually you manage to extract yourself from the comms-link.",,
adonyaImportantToFind,DialogOptionSelected,$option == adonya_importantToFind,"$saidImportant = true 0
FireAll AdonyaOptions","""I know, dear, you already mentioned it,"" she says.",,
adonyaImportantToFind2,DialogOptionSelected,$option == adonya_importantToFind2,"$global.knowSiyavongIsLookingForSyZal = true
$saidImportant2 = true 0
FireAll AdonyaOptions","""Of course it is,"" she says, humoring you. ""It's always the fate of the worlds with Scylla, isn't it?""

""I know this is all very important to you, captain."" Her voice takes on a more incisive tone. ""But if she's hiding from someone, if she's hiding from you, I'm sure it's for a good reason. And like I told Mister Siyavong when he came by, I don't know where my daughter or Elissa are - and I wouldn't tell him if I did.""

She crosses her arms.",,variant id
